{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Model migration should be treated as a {{c1::production change}} and re-evaluated.","D2.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Use prompts to guide behavior; use {{c1::deterministic controls}} to enforce hard security and policy invariants.","D2.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Keep trusted instructions structurally separate from {{c1::untrusted user or retrieved content}}.","D2.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["If a clear zero-shot prompt already passes the eval, extra examples may add {{c1::unnecessary tokens and maintenance}}.","D2.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Prompt engineering should respond to {{c1::observed evaluation failures}}, not ritual complexity.","D2.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["The context window should be treated as a finite {{c1::working set}}, not a database.","D2.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Large corpora are often better handled with {{c1::just-in-time retrieval}} than by preloading everything.","D2.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Reuse is safest when the content is {{c1::stable enough}} that freshness is not compromised.","D2.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Agent Skills use {{c1::progressive disclosure}} so detailed resources can load only when relevant.","D2.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What lifecycle state follows Active in the documented set Active, Legacy, Deprecated, Retired?","Legacy"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What should compare candidate models on the real workload rather than generic reputation?","Evaluation suite"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What prompt layer should hold stable high-trust behavioral instructions?","System prompt"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What should enforce authorization rather than relying on the model?","Deterministic control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What prompting technique provides representative examples?","Few-shot prompting"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What structured markup style can separate instructions, context, and examples in complex Claude prompts?","XML tags"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What technique summarizes a long trace while preserving critical state?","Compaction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What Anthropic mechanism packages reusable instructions, scripts, and resources for agents?","Agent Skills"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A routine classifier passes all quality thresholds on a faster model while a stronger model costs much more. What is the best choice?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use the faster model for that workload unless other constraints justify the stronger model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always use the strongest model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always use the cheapest model even if it fails quality.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Route randomly between models.\"}]","a","Model choice is a workload-specific trade-off, not a prestige decision."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A model is being retired. What should the team do before switching to its replacement?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run task-specific regression, safety, latency, and cost evaluation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newer model is behaviorally identical.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only compare benchmark scores.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change the model without testing because the API shape is similar.\"}]","a","Model migration can change behavior and should be evaluated."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A workflow has easy classification cases and rare complex exceptions. What design may improve economics if validated?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Route routine cases to a fast model and difficult cases to a stronger model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use the strongest model for every request by default.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use the cheapest model for every request regardless of errors.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove evaluation and route by input length only.\"}]","a","Evaluated routing can match model capability to workload difficulty."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which evidence is strongest for choosing between two Claude models for a production task?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Results on a representative eval suite for that task plus latency/cost measurements.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A generic leaderboard alone.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Which model name sounds newer.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A single anecdotal prompt.\"}]","a","Architecture should use representative workload evidence."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A refund policy says amounts over $500 require manager approval. What is the strongest implementation?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explain the rule in the prompt and enforce the threshold in deterministic approval logic.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Put the rule only in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use a longer example showing a $499 refund.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ask the model to self-check twice.\"}]","a","Prompts guide behavior; protected thresholds need enforceable controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Retrieved documents may contain malicious instructions. What prompt design is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clearly separate untrusted retrieved content from trusted instructions and restrict capabilities independently.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Concatenate all text into one unstructured prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell retrieved text it is trusted.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely on the model to always ignore injections.\"}]","a","Trust boundaries should be explicit and backed by controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Downstream software requires valid structured output. What should the architecture add?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"An explicit output contract plus schema validation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only ask for JSON politely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove the system prompt.\"}]","a","Structure should be specified and validated when machines depend on it."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team wants reusable prompts with changing request data. Which design is best?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep stable instructions in a template and inject request-specific variables separately.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Copy-paste a new giant prompt for every request.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Put all user data into the system policy section.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Mix examples, policy, and untrusted data without structure.\"}]","a","Templates separate stable instructions from variable content."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A classifier confuses two boundary cases even with clear instructions. What is a strong next step?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add a few representative examples that demonstrate the boundary distinction and re-evaluate.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add dozens of irrelevant examples.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Switch to an agent immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide the labels from the prompt.\"}]","a","Few-shot examples are useful when they target observed ambiguity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A straightforward extraction task already meets its quality target zero-shot. What should the team do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep the simpler prompt unless evaluation identifies a failure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add chain-of-thought instructions automatically.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add ten examples for safety.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Create a multi-agent workflow.\"}]","a","Use the lightest technique that passes the evaluation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A long prompt mixes policy, examples, retrieved text, and user data. What improvement is most direct?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Structure the prompt so trusted instructions, examples, context, and inputs are clearly separated.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Repeat every instruction three times.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove all examples regardless of performance.\"}]","a","Clear structure reduces ambiguity about the role of each section."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A retrieval system is returning the wrong document. What is the least promising first response?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Endlessly rewrite the prompt without fixing retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Inspect retrieval results.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Evaluate chunking/ranking.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Correct the retrieval layer.\"}]","a","Prompting cannot compensate for missing or wrong evidence indefinitely."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent preloads thousands of pages although each task uses only a few. What is the strongest change?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Retrieve relevant content just in time instead of preloading the corpus.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase prompt verbosity.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the corpus in conversation history.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Always use multiple agents.\"}]","a","JIT retrieval preserves context for relevant information."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A long-running agent approaches practical context limits. What should compaction preserve?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Key decisions, constraints, unresolved work, and important evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Every raw tool response verbatim.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only the last user message.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Nothing; simply drop all prior state.\"}]","a","Compaction reduces size while preserving decision-critical information."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Two independent research tasks pollute each other's context. What pattern can help?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use context isolation with separate workers/subagents.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Merge all transcripts into one prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Cache every tool result forever.\"}]","a","Separate contexts reduce interference between independent workstreams."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team stores the only copy of an order's authoritative state in conversation history. What is wrong?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Application state should live in an authoritative external store, not depend on the model context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Conversation history is always more durable than databases.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The context should be made longer.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only the system prompt needs changing.\"}]","a","Model context is a working set, not durable system state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A legal workflow reuses the same large policy manual for thousands of requests. What is a strong optimization?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse/cache the stable reference content while fetching case-specific current state separately.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache each client's live case status indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the manual into every variable section.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove freshness checks from current data.\"}]","a","Stable repeated context is a good reuse target; volatile state is not."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A shared Skill changes how production agents perform a regulated workflow. How should it be managed?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Version, review, test, and control changes like other operational assets.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat it as harmless prose with no review.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Let every user edit it globally.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Never regression-test Skill changes.\"}]","a","Reusable agent instructions/resources can change behavior and should be governed."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which data is the worst prompt-caching candidate?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A user's current account balance that changes frequently.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A stable policy manual.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A fixed system instruction block.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A reusable set of examples.\"}]","a","Caching must not undermine freshness for live state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A huge Skill library exists, but only one Skill is relevant per task. What design principle helps?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Progressive disclosure/loading of the relevant Skill details.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Load every Skill in full on every request.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Disable Skills entirely.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Store live transactional state inside every Skill.\"}]","a","Progressive disclosure limits context to relevant reusable expertise."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support Claude model selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate models on the actual workload.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newest model is always best.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Re-run regressions after model changes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Swap models without regression testing.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Evaluate models on the actual workload.; Re-run regressions after model changes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing Claude model selection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Re-run regressions after model changes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose solely from generic benchmark rank.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Include latency and cost alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hard-code permanent assumptions about one model name.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Re-run regressions after model changes.; Include latency and cost alongside quality.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in Claude model selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Include latency and cost alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Swap models without regression testing.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Treat current model availability as time-sensitive.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Route only to reduce price even if quality falls below threshold.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Include latency and cost alongside quality.; Treat current model availability as time-sensitive.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on Claude model selection, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Treat current model availability as time-sensitive.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Hard-code permanent assumptions about one model name.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use routing only when it improves measured outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume the newest model is always best.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Treat current model availability as time-sensitive.; Use routing only when it improves measured outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support system prompts, templates, and guardrails?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use clear trusted instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat a system prompt as an access-control list.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate untrusted content from policy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume asking for JSON guarantees validity.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use clear trusted instructions.; Separate untrusted content from policy.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing system prompts, templates, and guardrails. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Separate untrusted content from policy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let retrieved text rewrite policy.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Validate machine-readable outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Mix policy and user data indiscriminately.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Separate untrusted content from policy.; Validate machine-readable outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in system prompts, templates, and guardrails?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Validate machine-readable outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume asking for JSON guarantees validity.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Enforce authorization outside the model.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely only on model refusal for irreversible actions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Validate machine-readable outputs.; Enforce authorization outside the model.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on system prompts, templates, and guardrails, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Enforce authorization outside the model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Mix policy and user data indiscriminately.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use templates for stable reusable structure.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat a system prompt as an access-control list.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Enforce authorization outside the model.; Use templates for stable reusable structure.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support prompt engineering techniques?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Start with clear direct instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Force visible step-by-step reasoning for every task.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only easy examples.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Start with clear direct instructions.; Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing prompt engineering techniques. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add examples before establishing a baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Structure complex prompts explicitly.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat retrieval failures as prompt failures.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.; Structure complex prompts explicitly.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in prompt engineering techniques?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Structure complex prompts explicitly.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only easy examples.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use current model-specific thinking guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Overfit a prompt to a tiny static eval.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Structure complex prompts explicitly.; Use current model-specific thinking guidance.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on prompt engineering techniques, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use current model-specific thinking guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat retrieval failures as prompt failures.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Change prompts in response to measured failures.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Force visible step-by-step reasoning for every task.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use current model-specific thinking guidance.; Change prompts in response to measured failures.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support context-window and token management?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Preload every available document.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume larger windows eliminate relevance problems.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.; Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing context-window and token management. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat chat history as the database.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep durable state outside model context.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Summarize away hard constraints.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.; Keep durable state outside model context.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in context-window and token management?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep durable state outside model context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume larger windows eliminate relevance problems.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use separate contexts for independent work.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep raw intermediate data forever.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep durable state outside model context.; Use separate contexts for independent work.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support prompt reuse, caching, and Skills?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse stable expensive context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache rapidly changing business state indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep volatile state fresh.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one giant reusable prompt for unrelated workloads.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reuse stable expensive context.; Keep volatile state fresh.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing prompt reuse, caching, and Skills. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep volatile state fresh.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let shared Skills change without review.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Version shared prompt assets and Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat cache freshness as irrelevant.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep volatile state fresh.; Version shared prompt assets and Skills.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in prompt reuse, caching, and Skills?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Version shared prompt assets and Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use one giant reusable prompt for unrelated workloads.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use templates to separate stable and variable content.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume reusable instructions cannot create operational risk.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Version shared prompt assets and Skills.; Use templates to separate stable and variable content.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a sound model-selection process.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define task quality and operational thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Evaluate candidate models on representative cases\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare quality, latency, cost, and risk\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the model/routing policy\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-test when the model or workload changes\"}]","Requirements and evaluation precede selection; changes trigger re-evaluation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a secure prompt-to-action pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted system instructions\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Insert user/retrieved content as untrusted data\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an output/action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Validate schema and authorization deterministically\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute only if controls pass\"}]","Behavioral prompting precedes deterministic validation and execution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order an evidence-driven prompt-improvement loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish a simple baseline prompt\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Run representative evaluations\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify a specific failure mode\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply the lightest targeted prompting change\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-run evaluation and regression checks\"}]","Prompt complexity should be added in response to observed failures."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a long-horizon context-management approach.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Keep authoritative state externally\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Retrieve only information relevant to the current step\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Work within the active context\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Compact older interactions when needed\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Reload external state/evidence for later decisions\"}]","External state and JIT context keep the working set bounded over time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a safe prompt-reuse decision.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Identify repeated context\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Determine whether it is stable enough to reuse\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Separate volatile request/user state\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Cache or package the stable portion\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Invalidate or bypass reuse when freshness changes\"}]","Reuse follows stability analysis and must preserve freshness."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why can exposing more tools to an agent be harmful?","It expands potential blast radius and can also make tool selection harder."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the least-privilege goal for agent tools?","Expose only the capabilities, data, credentials, and side effects required for the task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When can broad shell or filesystem tools be appropriate?","When the use case truly needs general-purpose capability and the environment, credentials, and permissions are strongly constrained."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the difference between authentication and authorization?","Authentication establishes identity; authorization determines what that identity may do."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is a user message saying “I am an administrator” not authentication?","Identity must come from a trusted authentication mechanism, not untrusted prompt text."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why can adding a reranker or extra tool/model stage hurt a system even if quality improves?","Each extra stage adds latency and often cost, so the gain must justify the operational impact."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What work should be parallelized to reduce wall-clock latency?","Truly independent operations with no hidden dependency."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is logging only the final model answer insufficient for agent debugging?","Failures can occur in retrieval, tool calls, orchestration, or external state before the final answer."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What does an agent trajectory capture?","The sequence of model decisions, tool calls, and intermediate interactions during a run."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the core purpose of RAG?","Retrieve relevant external knowledge and place it in model context at inference time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why does chunking matter in RAG?","Poor chunk boundaries can split semantic units and reduce retrieval relevance or interpretability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When is lexical/BM25 retrieval especially useful?","When exact terms, identifiers, names, codes, or uncommon strings matter."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When is semantic retrieval especially useful?","When the query is conceptually related but uses different wording or paraphrases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What does MCP standardize?","How compatible AI applications connect to external capabilities such as tools and resources through a common protocol."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When is a direct API/SDK often preferable to MCP?","When a narrow integration is privately owned and cross-client AI interoperability adds little value."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What problem does progressive tool discovery address?","Large tool catalogs consume context and can increase wrong-tool selection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is progressive discovery?","Loading or exposing long-tail tools only when relevant instead of preloading every definition."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Capability bloat","Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Least privilege","Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authentication","Establishing the identity of the caller."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authorization","Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Latency budget","The portion of end-to-end response time available to system stages under the SLA."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Parallelization for latency","Executing independent operations concurrently to reduce wall-clock time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trace ID","A correlation identifier used to connect events across components of one request."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trajectory","The sequence of model/tool interactions taken by an agent during a task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Chunking","Dividing source documents into retrieval units while preserving useful semantic context."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Reranking","Reordering first-stage retrieval candidates with a stronger relevance signal."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Lexical retrieval","Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["MCP","A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Progressive discovery","Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["More exposed capability increases the potential {{c1::blast radius}} if an agent is compromised or behaves incorrectly.","D3.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Similar overlapping tools can increase {{c1::tool-selection errors}}.","D3.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A model saying a user is allowed to act is not a substitute for {{c1::authoritative authorization}}.","D3.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Protected tool calls should execute under {{c1::scoped or delegated credentials}} rather than a universal superuser identity.","D3.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Keep an extra quality stage only when its measurable gain justifies the added {{c1::latency and cost}}.","D3.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Parallelize work only when the operations are {{c1::independent}}.","D3.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A production AI request should be {{c1::reconstructable across components}} when diagnosing failures.","D3.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Observability should capture enough evidence to debug without indiscriminately copying {{c1::sensitive data}} into logs.","D3.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["If the correct evidence is never retrieved, prompt changes cannot fix the underlying {{c1::retrieval failure}}.","D3.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["RAG should be evaluated at both the {{c1::retrieval}} and generation stages.","D3.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Exact identifiers and error strings are often strong candidates for {{c1::lexical retrieval}}.","D3.6"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Paraphrased conceptual questions are often strong candidates for {{c1::semantic retrieval}}.","D3.6"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Choose MCP for useful {{c1::standardized interoperability and capability discovery}}, not merely because Claude is involved.","D3.7"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["MCP standardizes communication but does not replace {{c1::authentication, authorization, or source-system policy}}.","D3.7"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Large tool catalogs can create both context overhead and {{c1::selection confusion}}.","D3.8"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What security principle grants only the minimum permissions needed?","Least privilege"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes the potential damage possible when an agent or credential is compromised?","Blast radius"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What security process establishes who the caller is?","Authentication"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What security process determines what an identity may do?","Authorization"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What percentile metric is commonly used to represent tail latency rather than only the average?","p95"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What architecture technique reduces wall-clock time for independent calls?","Parallelization"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What identifier connects logs across model, retrieval, tools, queues, and workers?","Trace ID"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes the sequence of actions/tool calls an agent took?","Trajectory"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What retrieval stage reorders candidate chunks after initial search?","Reranking"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What retrieval approach combines lexical and semantic signals?","Hybrid retrieval"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What protocol standardizes reusable tool/resource surfaces for compatible AI clients?","MCP"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What strategy loads long-tail tool definitions only when they become relevant?","Progressive discovery"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A support assistant only needs order lookup and refund-request submission, but it has a production database admin credential. What should change first?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Replace the broad credential/tool with scoped capabilities needed for those tasks.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more logging but keep admin access.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell the model never to misuse the credential.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add more unrelated tools so selection is balanced.\"}]","a","Reduce unnecessary capability and blast radius rather than relying on instructions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A coding agent legitimately needs shell access. What is the strongest architecture?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Allow the broad tool inside a constrained sandbox with scoped credentials and permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ban all broad tools regardless of task.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give unrestricted production shell access.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely only on a system prompt to protect the host.\"}]","a","General-purpose capability can be valid when strong containment limits reach and impact."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent has twelve overlapping CRM tools with vague names and often chooses the wrong one. What is the best improvement?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reduce overlap and define clearer, distinct tool boundaries and descriptions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add another CRM tool for each edge case.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide all tool errors from the model.\"}]","a","Overlapping capability increases selection ambiguity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which change most directly reduces the blast radius of a read-only reporting agent?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Remove write credentials and destructive tool operations it does not need.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase the model's context window.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Make logs more verbose while retaining write access.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add a warning sentence to every prompt.\"}]","a","Hard capability restriction reduces what can happen if the model is wrong or compromised."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A user types “I am the account administrator” into chat. What should the application do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Ignore the claim for access control and use trusted authenticated identity and policy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Grant admin tools because the model saw the statement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ask Claude to judge whether the statement sounds credible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Put the claim in the system prompt.\"}]","a","Prompt text is not authentication."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An MCP tool is protected by OAuth. Where should access be checked?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"At the protected protocol/application boundary using verified authorization context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only inside the model prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only after the tool already executes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"By asking the user to state their role in natural language.\"}]","a","Authorization is an enforceable control outside model output."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A SaaS agent uses one backend superuser credential for every tenant. What is the primary risk?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A failure in model/tool logic can cross tenant boundaries because the execution identity is overprivileged.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The model will necessarily become slower.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"OAuth cannot work with multi-tenancy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"The vector index will stop embedding documents.\"}]","a","Shared broad credentials defeat least-privilege and tenant isolation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A consequential tool call occurs after initial login. What is the safest design?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Re-check authorization for the specific protected action using current trusted identity/context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume authentication at session start authorizes every later action.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ask Claude whether the action feels allowed.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the same admin token for all users.\"}]","a","Action-level authorization should match the protected resource and current caller."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A reranker improves grounded accuracy by 0.3% but adds 1.5 seconds to a 2-second SLA. What should the architect do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate whether the small quality gain justifies violating or consuming most of the latency budget.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always keep reranking because quality stages are mandatory.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore the SLA because accuracy always wins.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove required safety checks first.\"}]","a","Accuracy and latency are explicit trade-offs against workload constraints."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Four retrieval calls use unrelated sources and do not depend on one another. How can wall-clock time often be reduced?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run the independent calls in parallel and combine results.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Run them sequentially by default.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase prompt length.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the same output from the first call for all four.\"}]","a","Independent work is a good candidate for parallel execution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A system is slow. Retrieval is 50 ms, model inference 2.8 s, and formatting 20 ms. Where should optimization start?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The dominant model-inference contribution, subject to quality constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Formatting because it is easiest.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Retrieval because RAG is always the bottleneck.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Randomly remove a safety control.\"}]","a","Optimize the dominant contributor rather than the easiest component."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Tool Search reduces context and wrong-tool calls but adds a lookup step. When is it most justified?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"When the accuracy/context benefit outweighs the added lookup latency for the workload.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"For every tool catalog regardless of size.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only when authorization is missing.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only when average latency is already zero.\"}]","a","Progressive discovery itself has a trade-off and should be evaluated."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A final answer is wrong, but logs contain only the final text. What is the strongest observability improvement?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Capture correlated trajectory/tool/retrieval events so the failing stage can be identified.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log the final answer twice.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase model temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove correlation IDs.\"}]","a","Agent failures require visibility into intermediate behavior and dependencies."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Worker logs exist but cannot be tied back to the originating user request. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A propagated trace/correlation identity.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More workers.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A larger context window.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"An additional prompt example.\"}]","a","Distributed observability needs cross-component correlation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team logs every prompt, credential, and tool payload indefinitely for debugging. What is the main issue?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Observability itself is creating privacy/security and retention risk.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Logs can never contain sensitive data.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More logs always reduce risk.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Tracing should only happen after incidents.\"}]","a","Debuggability must be balanced with data minimization and protection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent says it updated a CRM record, but the CRM state did not change. Which signal is most authoritative?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The actual external CRM outcome/state.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The agent's final sentence.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The user's expectation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"The prompt template version alone.\"}]","a","External state can reveal a failed action even when the model claims success."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A policy assistant keeps answering from an obsolete policy that ranks above the current version. What should be fixed first?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Freshness/metadata/ranking in the retrieval pipeline.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Tell Claude to be more accurate without changing retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add another unrelated tool.\"}]","a","The wrong evidence is reaching the model; fix retrieval before prompt wording."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A document is split at arbitrary character counts, separating headings from their explanations. What should the architect revisit?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Chunking strategy based on source structure and likely queries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"OAuth scopes.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model lifecycle state.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Human review sampling rate.\"}]","a","Chunk boundaries affect retrieval quality and meaning."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Initial hybrid retrieval returns many plausible chunks but ordering is weak. What optional stage can improve final relevance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reranking the candidate set.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Remove indexing.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use only conversation memory.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable metadata.\"}]","a","Reranking refines first-stage candidates with a stronger relevance signal."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["The model hallucinates because the relevant document never appears in retrieved context. What diagnostic conclusion is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"This is primarily a retrieval recall/ranking problem, not only a prompt problem.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The system needs a more persuasive system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The user must restate the question.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"The answer should be cached.\"}]","a","Generation cannot use evidence it never receives."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A user searches for exact error code ERR-9F21. Which retrieval signal should be strongly represented?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Lexical/exact-term retrieval such as BM25.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Semantic similarity only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Random chunk selection.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Conversation memory only.\"}]","a","Exact identifiers benefit from lexical matching."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Users ask policy questions with wording very different from the source text. Which retrieval method helps most?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Semantic embedding retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Exact keyword matching only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Sorting documents alphabetically.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Using only document timestamps.\"}]","a","Semantic retrieval captures conceptual similarity across paraphrases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A corpus contains product codes plus natural-language explanations. What strategy often provides robust coverage?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Hybrid lexical and semantic retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Semantic retrieval with no exact matching.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Lexical search with no semantic signal.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No retrieval; preload the entire corpus.\"}]","a","Both exact terminology and conceptual similarity matter."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["One internal service exposes a single private function to one application. No other AI client needs it. What is the simplest integration?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A direct API/SDK or internal function boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"MCP is mandatory for every Claude integration.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Agent-to-agent protocol is required.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A multi-agent runtime must wrap it.\"}]","a","A reusable protocol layer should earn its complexity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Several compatible AI clients need to discover and call the same enterprise tools through a standard interface. What is a strong fit?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A different bespoke private API per client only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Conversation memory.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A vector database with no tool protocol.\"}]","a","MCP is designed for standardized capability exposure and discovery."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team exposes a destructive MCP tool and assumes MCP makes it safe. What is wrong?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"MCP does not replace authorization, validation, least privilege, or source-system controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"MCP automatically denies all writes.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"MCP tools cannot be destructive.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"MCP removes the need for identity.\"}]","a","Protocol standardization is distinct from security policy."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An enterprise has hundreds of rarely used MCP tools and only a few are relevant per request. What architecture best reduces context overhead?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep common tools available and discover/load long-tail tools on demand.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Load every tool definition on every request.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove authorization because hidden tools are safe.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Duplicate every tool description in the system prompt.\"}]","a","Progressive discovery targets context bloat and tool-selection ambiguity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A system has five simple tools used on nearly every request. What is a reasonable choice?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Loading the small catalog directly may be simpler than adding a discovery layer.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Progressive discovery is mandatory regardless of catalog size.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Split each tool into ten more tools.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide all tools until after generation.\"}]","a","Discovery adds complexity and should be justified by catalog/context needs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A tool is not loaded into the current model context. Can the system assume the user is unauthorized to use it?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"No. Discovery/visibility and authorization are separate controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Yes, hidden tools are automatically forbidden.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Yes, context visibility is the authorization policy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only if the model says so.\"}]","a","Authorization must be enforced independently of what definitions are currently visible."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support tool and agent capability bloat?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Expose only tools required for the task.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give every agent a shared admin credential.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Expose every tool in case one becomes useful.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Expose only tools required for the task.; Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing tool and agent capability bloat. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume logging makes excessive permission safe.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use prompt instructions as the only containment control.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.; Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in tool and agent capability bloat?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Expose every tool in case one becomes useful.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give tools clear non-overlapping purposes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat broad tools as automatically safe because Claude is capable.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.; Give tools clear non-overlapping purposes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on tool and agent capability bloat, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Give tools clear non-overlapping purposes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use prompt instructions as the only containment control.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep inaccessible credentials outside the agent environment.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give every agent a shared admin credential.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Give tools clear non-overlapping purposes.; Keep inaccessible credentials outside the agent environment.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support authentication and authorization?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted identity before using it in model/tool decisions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust role claims typed into the conversation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one superuser credential across tenants.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Establish trusted identity before using it in model/tool decisions.; Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing authentication and authorization. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let the model invent access policy.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use scoped or delegated credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Authenticate once and never check action permissions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.; Use scoped or delegated credentials.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in authentication and authorization?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use scoped or delegated credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use one superuser credential across tenants.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve caller identity through the request path.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat MCP itself as automatic authorization.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use scoped or delegated credentials.; Preserve caller identity through the request path.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on authentication and authorization, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Preserve caller identity through the request path.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Authenticate once and never check action permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Enforce tenant boundaries independently of prompt text.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Trust role claims typed into the conversation.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Preserve caller identity through the request path.; Enforce tenant boundaries independently of prompt text.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support accuracy-latency trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure end-to-end latency by stage.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add reranking because every RAG system must have it.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compare quality gains against SLA impact.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Parallelize dependent steps.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure end-to-end latency by stage.; Compare quality gains against SLA impact.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing accuracy-latency trade-offs. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare quality gains against SLA impact.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Measure only average latency.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallelize independent work.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove required authorization to save time.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Compare quality gains against SLA impact.; Parallelize independent work.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in accuracy-latency trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallelize independent work.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Parallelize dependent steps.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Optimize the dominant latency contributor.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Optimize tiny stages while ignoring the dominant bottleneck.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Parallelize independent work.; Optimize the dominant latency contributor.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on accuracy-latency trade-offs, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Optimize the dominant latency contributor.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Remove required authorization to save time.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep required safety checks even under latency pressure.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add reranking because every RAG system must have it.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Optimize the dominant latency contributor.; Keep required safety checks even under latency pressure.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support observability at scale?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Propagate trace identity across components.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log only the final answer.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep component logs with no correlation.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Propagate trace identity across components.; Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing observability at scale. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Store secrets in logs for convenience.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Record tool names/results and dependency failures.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Trust model claims over external state.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.; Record tool names/results and dependency failures.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in observability at scale?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Record tool names/results and dependency failures.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep component logs with no correlation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Protect sensitive logging data.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Collect metrics with no operational owner.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Record tool names/results and dependency failures.; Protect sensitive logging data.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support RAG pipeline design?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Design chunking around document structure and queries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat RAG as synonymous with a vector database.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Measure retrieval separately from generation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change prompts when evidence is never retrieved.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Design chunking around document structure and queries.; Measure retrieval separately from generation.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing RAG pipeline design. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure retrieval separately from generation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore stale/current document status.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use metadata for freshness/access filtering where required.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Bypass document permissions during retrieval.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure retrieval separately from generation.; Use metadata for freshness/access filtering where required.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in RAG pipeline design?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use metadata for freshness/access filtering where required.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Change prompts when evidence is never retrieved.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add reranking only when it improves measured retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add every optional pipeline stage by default.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use metadata for freshness/access filtering where required.; Add reranking only when it improves measured retrieval.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support retrieval strategy selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Match retrieval strategy to query/data shape.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use embeddings for every exact-ID lookup.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume a stale index is authoritative for current balances.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Match retrieval strategy to query/data shape.; Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing retrieval strategy selection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only keyword search for heavily paraphrased questions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use semantic signals for paraphrases.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore access/freshness metadata.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.; Use semantic signals for paraphrases.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in retrieval strategy selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use semantic signals for paraphrases.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume a stale index is authoritative for current balances.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use hybrid retrieval when both signal types matter.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Choose retrieval methods because they are fashionable.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use semantic signals for paraphrases.; Use hybrid retrieval when both signal types matter.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support integration mechanism selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use direct APIs for narrow privately owned integrations when sufficient.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose MCP simply because Claude is present.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Wrap every private function in MCP.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use direct APIs for narrow privately owned integrations when sufficient.; Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing integration mechanism selection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume MCP tools are automatically secure.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep authorization separate from protocol choice.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use agent-to-agent when a normal function/tool boundary suffices.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.; Keep authorization separate from protocol choice.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in integration mechanism selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep authorization separate from protocol choice.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Wrap every private function in MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Evaluate ownership, reuse, and operational dependencies.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore who owns and operates the integration boundary.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep authorization separate from protocol choice.; Evaluate ownership, reuse, and operational dependencies.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support progressive discovery versus monolithic context?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Load long-tail tools only when relevant.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Load hundreds of definitions on every request.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Build discovery complexity for a tiny stable catalog without benefit.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Load long-tail tools only when relevant.; Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing progressive discovery versus monolithic context. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat hidden-from-context as unauthorized.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use discovery to reduce context and selection burden.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use discovery instead of access control.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.; Use discovery to reduce context and selection burden.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in progressive discovery versus monolithic context?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use discovery to reduce context and selection burden.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Build discovery complexity for a tiny stable catalog without benefit.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep authorization independent of visibility.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Turn product-specific tool-count thresholds into timeless exam rules.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use discovery to reduce context and selection burden.; Keep authorization independent of visibility.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a protected agent action flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the user\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted auth context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Authorize the specific protected action\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute with scoped credentials and record the result\"}]","Identity is established before proposal; authorization gates execution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a latency-optimization investigation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Measure end-to-end latency by stage\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Identify the dominant contributor\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Form a change hypothesis\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Measure quality/latency after the change\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Keep the change only if thresholds still pass\"}]","Optimization starts with measurement and must preserve required quality/safety."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a trace-based incident investigation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Start from the failing request/trace ID\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Inspect model/retrieval/tool trajectory\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare claimed action with external outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Identify the failing stage\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Fix and add a regression check\"}]","Correlated evidence narrows the failure before remediation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a basic RAG pipeline.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Ingest and parse source content\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Chunk and enrich/index the content\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Retrieve candidates for a query\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Filter/rerank and assemble relevant context\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Generate the answer from the selected context\"}]","RAG prepares indexed units first, then retrieves and assembles evidence at inference time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a retrieval-debugging check when a RAG answer is wrong.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Check whether the needed source exists in the corpus\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Check whether the right chunk was created/indexed\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Check whether retrieval returned it\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Check whether ranking/context assembly kept it\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Then inspect generation behavior\"}]","Debug retrieval upstream before blaming generation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order an integration-mechanism decision.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Identify the capability and its owner\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Determine clients/reuse/interoperability needs\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify security and operational boundaries\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Choose API/CLI, MCP, or agent-to-agent as appropriate\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Validate the choice against complexity and support burden\"}]","Integration choice follows requirements and boundaries rather than protocol fashion."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a progressive tool-discovery flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Start with a small set of common tools plus discovery capability\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Identify the task's missing capability\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Search/discover relevant long-tail tools\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Load the selected tool definitions\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Invoke authorized tools and continue the task\"}]","Definitions are added only after the task indicates they are needed."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is “good responses” an inadequate evaluation goal?","It is not operationally defined or measurable against a threshold."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What dimensions should an AI system evaluation consider?","Task quality plus relevant latency, cost, safety, security, and business outcomes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why can a single aggregate score be misleading?","A system can pass overall while failing important safety, subgroup, or tail-latency constraints."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an eval suite represent?","The real workload, important edge cases, historical failures, adversarial cases, and multi-turn behavior where relevant."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When is a deterministic grader preferable to an LLM judge?","When correctness can be checked exactly with code, schema, tests, or external state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why run repeated trials for some agent tasks?","Model/agent behavior can be stochastic, so one run may not characterize reliability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an A/B test begin with?","A specific hypothesis and pre-defined primary and guardrail metrics."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is shadow testing?","Running a candidate on real traffic without allowing its outputs to affect users or production state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the key diagnostic principle for AI systems?","Identify and fix the layer causing the failure rather than masking it downstream."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is “hallucination” an incomplete diagnosis?","Wrong output can originate from retrieval, tools, orchestration, stale data, model mismatch, or prompting."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should optimization minimize?","Resource use per successful outcome while preserving required quality, safety, and reliability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["How can context engineering reduce cost?","Remove low-value context, use just-in-time retrieval/compaction, and avoid repeatedly sending unnecessary data."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why must evaluation continue after launch?","Real traffic, dependencies, models, and data distributions change over time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is a regression eval?","A test that checks known-good behavior still works after changes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Outcome metric","A measure of whether the task produced the desired real-world result."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Guardrail metric","A secondary threshold that must not regress while optimizing a primary metric."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trial","One execution of an evaluation task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Grader","The mechanism that scores whether a task/run met defined criteria."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Control","The baseline experience/system in a controlled experiment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Treatment","The candidate change being tested against the control."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Retrieval failure","The relevant evidence is not retrieved or is outranked by wrong evidence."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Orchestration failure","Correct components are coordinated incorrectly, such as dropped worker results or wrong ordering."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Cost per successful outcome","Total resource cost divided by tasks that actually meet the success criteria."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Prompt caching","Reusing eligible stable prompt/context content rather than recomputing/sending it as uncached work each time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Capability eval","An evaluation asking whether the system can perform a new or harder capability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A useful metric needs a definition, a measurement method, and an {{c1::acceptance threshold}}.","D4.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Agent evaluation should include {{c1::external outcomes}} when model claims alone are insufficient.","D4.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Multi-dimensional systems should not be reduced to a single vague {{c1::accuracy score}}.","D4.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Use the {{c1::cheapest reliable grader}} that can accurately measure the property of interest.","D4.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For agents, inspect both final {{c1::outcomes and trajectories}} when intermediate behavior matters.","D4.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["An A/B experiment should define the hypothesis, primary metric, guardrails, assignment, and {{c1::decision/stopping rule}} before interpreting results.","D4.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["{{c1::Shadow testing}} uses real traffic while preventing candidate outputs from affecting production behavior.","D4.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Diagnose from {{c1::symptom → evidence → failing stage → targeted fix}}, rather than rewriting prompts blindly.","D4.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A fixed production failure should become a {{c1::regression case}}.","D4.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Optimize {{c1::cost per successful outcome}}, not just cost per request.","D4.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Removing tokens is useful only if required {{c1::quality and safety thresholds}} still pass.","D4.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Production monitoring reveals whether the {{c1::real workload or dependencies}} are drifting from assumptions.","D4.6"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Known failures should be converted into {{c1::regression tests/evals}} after remediation.","D4.6"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes a threshold metric that must not regress during optimization?","Guardrail metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What should define the minimum acceptable value for a metric?","Acceptance threshold"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What evaluation component scores a task result?","Grader"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes one execution of an eval task?","Trial"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What experiment mode runs a candidate on real traffic without exposing users to its outputs?","Shadow testing"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What is the baseline arm of an A/B experiment called?","Control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What failure class occurs when relevant evidence never reaches the model?","Retrieval failure"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What failure class occurs when correct components are sequenced or coordinated incorrectly?","Orchestration failure"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What efficiency metric accounts for failures/retries rather than only request price?","Cost per successful outcome"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What evaluation protects known-good behavior from breaking after changes?","Regression evaluation"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team says its support agent is “very accurate.” What should an architect request next?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A defined metric, representative measurement method, and acceptance threshold.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A longer system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A larger context window.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"More agents.\"}]","a","Evaluation claims must be operationalized."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A candidate model improves task success but doubles safety-policy violations. What should the team conclude?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The candidate fails a critical guardrail even if the primary quality metric improved.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ship it because primary accuracy is higher.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore safety because it is hard to score.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Average the two metrics into one number and accept any positive result.\"}]","a","Safety/security floors can constrain optimization."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A coding agent says it fixed a bug, but tests still fail. What is the stronger evaluation metric?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The external task outcome, such as passing the relevant tests.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The agent's confidence.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Length of the explanation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Number of tool calls.\"}]","a","External outcome can be more authoritative than model claims."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which metric best represents user-facing responsiveness when occasional slow requests matter?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A tail-latency percentile such as p95, paired with an SLA threshold.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only average latency.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Total tokens ever used.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Number of prompt lines.\"}]","a","Tail latency matters when a minority of very slow requests harm the experience."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A tool action should create exactly one database row. What is the best grader?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A deterministic check of the database state.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"An LLM judge reading the agent's explanation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A human reviewer for every run.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"The model's self-reported success.\"}]","a","Exact external state should be verified deterministically."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A style rubric is nuanced and cannot be checked with simple code. What grader may be appropriate after calibration?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A model-based grader evaluated against human-labeled examples.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A schema validator only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A random score.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No grader at all.\"}]","a","Model graders can score nuanced qualities but should be calibrated."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An eval suite contains only easy happy-path requests. What is the biggest weakness?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"It may miss boundary, adversarial, malformed, and historical failure modes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"It contains too many tasks.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"It should use only one trial.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"It should never include production failures.\"}]","a","Representative coverage includes important failures, not just routine cases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent's performance varies significantly between runs of the same task. What should the eval framework add?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Multiple trials per task to measure reliability under stochastic behavior.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One carefully chosen run only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A longer deck name.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fewer measurements.\"}]","a","Repeated trials characterize variance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team changes the model, prompt, retriever, and tool schema simultaneously, then sees improvement. What is the main problem?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The experiment cannot attribute the change because several major variables moved together.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A/B testing requires more than two models.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"All variables should always change together.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Guardrail metrics are unnecessary.\"}]","a","Controlled experiments isolate specific hypotheses."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A new agent can execute risky production writes. How can the team first test it on realistic traffic without exposing users to its actions?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use shadow testing with outputs/actions prevented from affecting production.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Turn it on for every user immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Disable logging.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only a synthetic prompt unrelated to production.\"}]","a","Shadow testing provides realistic input without direct production effect."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A treatment improves accuracy by 0.05% with strong statistical significance but adds major cost. What should the architect consider?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the improvement is practically valuable enough to justify the cost.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Statistical significance guarantees business value.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore cost once p<0.05.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Always ship any measurable improvement.\"}]","a","Practical significance and guardrails matter."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An experiment's primary quality metric rises while latency breaches the SLA. What should happen?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Treat the latency SLA as a guardrail and reject or revise the treatment.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ship because primary quality improved.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove the SLA from reporting.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Average quality and latency into one unbounded score.\"}]","a","Guardrails prevent one metric from improving by violating another requirement."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A model gives wrong answers because the retriever returns obsolete documents. What should change first?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Fix the retrieval freshness/ranking problem.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more system-prompt warnings.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Upgrade the model without inspecting retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry the same stale evidence.\"}]","a","The failing layer is retrieval, not necessarily prompting."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A tool returns malformed JSON and the agent fails. What is the most direct diagnosis?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Tool/interface contract failure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Hallucination by definition.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model lifecycle failure.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Business-value failure.\"}]","a","Inspect the interface actually producing the malformed data."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A worker computes the correct result, but the orchestrator drops it before synthesis. What failure class is this?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Orchestration failure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Retrieval failure.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Prompt injection.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Model deprecation.\"}]","a","The component result is correct; coordination is wrong."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["After repairing a recurrent production failure, what should the team add?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A regression test/eval reproducing the failure so it stays fixed.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Remove observability.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Delete historical evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only document that someone remembers the fix.\"}]","a","Known failures should become protected regression cases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A cheaper model causes twice as many retries and escalations. What metric should decide whether it is actually cheaper?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Cost per successful outcome including retries/escalations.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Price per single API call only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model name length.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Prompt token count alone.\"}]","a","A cheap failing request can raise total cost."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Tool results contain 100,000 rows but the model needs only an aggregate. What is a strong optimization?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Process/filter the data programmatically and pass only the high-signal result to the model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Send every row through multiple model turns.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the rows in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable the tool.\"}]","a","Programmatic processing reduces token/context overhead."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A prompt includes large historical logs that never affect decisions. What should the team test?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Remove or compact low-value context and confirm quality still passes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more logs to improve cost.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase output length.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the strongest model only.\"}]","a","Low-value context wastes tokens and may harm relevance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An optimization removes a safety validation step and lowers p95 latency. Is it acceptable?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Only if the validation was not required; required safety controls must remain even when they cost latency.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Yes, lower latency always dominates.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Yes, if average accuracy rises.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Yes, if the model promises to self-check.\"}]","a","Optimization is constrained by required safety/security thresholds."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Offline evals pass, but tool failures spike after launch because an external API changed. What caught this?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Production monitoring of real dependencies and outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A static benchmark alone.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A one-time prelaunch demo.\"}]","a","Production monitoring detects real-world changes offline suites may not predict."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A new model version is deployed. What should protect known behavior?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run the regression suite and monitor production after migration.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume newer means identical.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Delete old evals.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only compare price.\"}]","a","Model changes can alter behavior and require regression testing."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Users report a novel failure pattern. What should happen after root cause is fixed?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add representative cases to the regression suite and monitor the corrected behavior.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore it because launch evals already passed.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove the complaint from logs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only increase model temperature.\"}]","a","Production failures improve future evaluation coverage."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An alert fires but no team owns the metric or runbook. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Operational ownership and a defined response action.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Another model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More prompt examples.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A second vector database.\"}]","a","Monitoring without action/ownership does not close the loop."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support defining evaluation metrics?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define measurable thresholds before evaluation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use one vague “accuracy” number for everything.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Measure external outcomes where possible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore tail behavior.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define measurable thresholds before evaluation.; Measure external outcomes where possible.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing defining evaluation metrics. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure external outcomes where possible.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize only the easiest metric.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Declare success without a threshold.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure external outcomes where possible.; Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in defining evaluation metrics?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore tail behavior.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep safety/security guardrails alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Trust model self-reports over authoritative outcomes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.; Keep safety/security guardrails alongside quality.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on defining evaluation metrics, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep safety/security guardrails alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Declare success without a threshold.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Connect technical measures to user/business outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one vague “accuracy” number for everything.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep safety/security guardrails alongside quality.; Connect technical measures to user/business outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support evaluation datasets and frameworks?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Include representative and difficult cases.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Evaluate only final prose.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use deterministic graders for exact properties.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only happy-path data.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Include representative and difficult cases.; Use deterministic graders for exact properties.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing evaluation datasets and frameworks. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use deterministic graders for exact properties.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM judge when code can verify exactly.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Calibrate model graders.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume one stochastic trial is definitive.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use deterministic graders for exact properties.; Calibrate model graders.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in evaluation datasets and frameworks?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Calibrate model graders.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only happy-path data.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Inspect external outcomes for agent actions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Overfit the system to a tiny static eval set.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Calibrate model graders.; Inspect external outcomes for agent actions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on evaluation datasets and frameworks, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Inspect external outcomes for agent actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume one stochastic trial is definitive.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add production failures to regression suites.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Evaluate only final prose.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Inspect external outcomes for agent actions.; Add production failures to regression suites.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support A/B testing and iterative improvement?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"State the hypothesis before running the experiment.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Change many major variables at once.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define primary and guardrail metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore latency/cost after quality improves.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: State the hypothesis before running the experiment.; Define primary and guardrail metrics.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing A/B testing and iterative improvement. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define primary and guardrail metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Look at metrics until something becomes significant.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Live-test risky irreversible actions unnecessarily.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define primary and guardrail metrics.; Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in A/B testing and iterative improvement?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore latency/cost after quality improves.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use shadow testing for risky candidates.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Define success criteria after seeing results.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.; Use shadow testing for risky candidates.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on A/B testing and iterative improvement, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use shadow testing for risky candidates.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Live-test risky irreversible actions unnecessarily.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Evaluate practical as well as statistical impact.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change many major variables at once.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use shadow testing for risky candidates.; Evaluate practical as well as statistical impact.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support diagnosing AI system failures?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reproduce the symptom.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Call every wrong answer a hallucination.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Inspect traces and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Upgrade the model to fix a broken API contract.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reproduce the symptom.; Inspect traces and external outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing diagnosing AI system failures. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Inspect traces and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Rewrite prompts when retrieval is stale.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify the specific failing layer.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry authorization failures blindly.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Inspect traces and external outcomes.; Identify the specific failing layer.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in diagnosing AI system failures?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identify the specific failing layer.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Upgrade the model to fix a broken API contract.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use targeted tests to validate the hypothesis.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fix production bugs without regression coverage.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Identify the specific failing layer.; Use targeted tests to validate the hypothesis.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on diagnosing AI system failures, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use targeted tests to validate the hypothesis.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Retry authorization failures blindly.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add a regression case after the fix.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Call every wrong answer a hallucination.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use targeted tests to validate the hypothesis.; Add a regression case after the fix.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure cost per successful outcome.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize cost per request regardless of failures.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Reduce irrelevant context.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume the cheapest model is cheapest end to end.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure cost per successful outcome.; Reduce irrelevant context.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reduce irrelevant context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Remove required safety checks for speed.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use programmatic processing for large intermediate data.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add caches without freshness policy.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reduce irrelevant context.; Use programmatic processing for large intermediate data.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use programmatic processing for large intermediate data.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the cheapest model is cheapest end to end.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallelize independent work where appropriate.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Optimize tiny token savings while causing major quality regression.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use programmatic processing for large intermediate data.; Parallelize independent work where appropriate.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallelize independent work where appropriate.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add caches without freshness policy.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Re-evaluate quality after optimization.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Optimize cost per request regardless of failures.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Parallelize independent work where appropriate.; Re-evaluate quality after optimization.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support production monitoring and regression protection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Monitor real outcomes and dependencies.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Monitor infrastructure uptime only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Protect known behavior with regression evals.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Deploy model changes without regression tests.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Monitor real outcomes and dependencies.; Protect known behavior with regression evals.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing production monitoring and regression protection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Protect known behavior with regression evals.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep eval suites frozen forever.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Test model/version migrations.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Create alerts with no owner.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Protect known behavior with regression evals.; Test model/version migrations.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in production monitoring and regression protection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Test model/version migrations.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Deploy model changes without regression tests.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign owners and response actions to alerts.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume offline success guarantees production success.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Test model/version migrations.; Assign owners and response actions to alerts.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:evaluation\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a metric-definition workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the desired outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Choose observable measures\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Specify how each measure is computed\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Set acceptance and guardrail thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Run representative evaluation and compare to thresholds\"}]","Metrics become useful only after outcome, measurement, and thresholds are explicit."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a basic evaluation-framework design.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define representative tasks\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Choose appropriate graders\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run one or more trials\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Collect trajectories/outcomes\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Aggregate results against thresholds\"}]","Task definition and grading come before execution and aggregation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a controlled improvement experiment.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"State the hypothesis\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Choose primary and guardrail metrics\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Define assignment and decision rule\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Run control/treatment or shadow evaluation\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Analyze results and decide whether to ship\"}]","Pre-specification precedes execution and interpretation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a root-cause diagnostic loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Reproduce the symptom\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Inspect trace/outcome evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify the likely failing stage\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Run a targeted isolation test\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Apply the fix and add regression coverage\"}]","Evidence-driven isolation precedes remediation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a safe optimization cycle.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Measure baseline quality, latency, and cost\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Identify the dominant resource driver\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Apply one targeted optimization\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Re-run quality/safety/latency evals\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Keep the change only if all required thresholds pass\"}]","Optimization remains constrained by outcome quality and safety."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a production learning loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Monitor real system behavior\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Detect and investigate a failure/drift signal\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Fix the root cause\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Add a regression case\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Verify the fix in evaluation and production\"}]","Production evidence feeds back into regression protection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the core safety architecture principle for guardrails?","Use defense in depth rather than relying on a single control."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why are system prompts insufficient as hard security boundaries?","Model behavior is probabilistic and can be influenced by adversarial or unexpected inputs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Where should a safety or authorization control live?","At the boundary capable of actually enforcing the required property."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is indirect prompt injection?","Malicious instructions embedded in external content that an agent processes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is excessive agency?","Giving an agent more autonomy, tools, permissions, or side-effect power than the task requires."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What three control categories help structure risk treatment?","Prevention, detection, and recovery."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When should human involvement increase?","As consequence, irreversibility, uncertainty, or regulatory obligation increases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is pre-action approval?","A human reviews and authorizes a proposed consequential action before execution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why is human review ineffective when the reviewer lacks context?","The human cannot make a meaningful decision and may merely rubber-stamp the model."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the core architecture task for compliance requirements?","Translate applicable obligations into specific controls, owners, evidence, and review processes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why does a provider's compliance status not automatically make an application compliant?","Compliance depends on the full system boundary, data flows, configuration, controls, and organizational responsibilities."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why can aggregate accuracy hide fairness problems?","Different relevant populations or use cases may experience materially different error rates."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What does accountability require in AI architecture?","Named human/organizational ownership for decisions, residual risk, monitoring, incidents, and policy changes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Defense in depth","Using multiple independent layers so failure of one control does not remove all protection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Fail closed","Block the protected action when a required safety or authorization check cannot complete."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Indirect prompt injection","Adversarial instructions hidden in external content such as pages, documents, email, or tool results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Excessive agency","More autonomy or capability than is necessary for the intended task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Pre-action approval","Human authorization before a consequential action occurs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Sampled review","Reviewing a subset of lower-risk cases to monitor quality and drift."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Control evidence","Records/artifacts demonstrating that a required control is implemented and operating."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Compliance boundary","The systems, data, services, and responsibilities included in the regulated/authorized scope."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Fairness evaluation","Assessing relevant performance/outcomes across appropriate groups or slices instead of relying only on aggregate metrics."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Accountability","Clear ownership for architecture decisions, residual risk, monitoring, and incident response."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Hard safety properties should be enforced by {{c1::controls at the relevant system boundary}}, not only by prompt text.","D5.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["High-risk authorization checks often should {{c1::fail closed}} when verification is unavailable.","D5.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Agent safety benefits from {{c1::defense in depth}} across model, tool, environment, and human controls.","D5.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["External content consumed by an agent should be treated as {{c1::untrusted}} because it may contain indirect prompt injection.","D5.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Reducing unnecessary tools and credentials limits the {{c1::blast radius}} of excessive agency.","D5.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Human oversight should scale with {{c1::consequence and reversibility}}, not merely model confidence.","D5.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A reviewer needs enough {{c1::evidence and policy context}} to make a meaningful decision.","D5.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A useful compliance mapping is requirement → control → owner → {{c1::evidence}} → review cadence.","D5.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A vendor's compliance status does not automatically make the {{c1::entire application}} compliant.","D5.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Responsible AI requires clear {{c1::accountability}} rather than saying “the AI decided.”","D5.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Transparency does not require exposing private {{c1::chain-of-thought}}.","D5.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What security design uses several independent protective layers?","Defense in depth"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What failure behavior blocks an action when a required control cannot verify it?","Fail closed"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What attack embeds malicious instructions in content the agent reads?","Indirect prompt injection"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What risk describes granting an agent more autonomy or permissions than required?","Excessive agency"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What review pattern requires human authorization before execution?","Pre-action approval"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What review pattern checks only a fraction of lower-risk cases?","Sampled review"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes records proving a control is implemented and operating?","Control evidence"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What concept means a named person/team owns residual risk and response?","Accountability"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A refund tool can transfer money. The system prompt says “never refund more than $500,” but the API accepts any amount. What is the strongest improvement?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Enforce the limit in deterministic transaction/authorization logic before execution.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Repeat the warning five times in the prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use a more persuasive role description.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Log over-$500 refunds after they happen.\"}]","a","Hard financial limits belong at the execution boundary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A required authorization service is unavailable during a high-risk transaction. What is usually safest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Block or defer the action until authorization can be verified.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Allow the action and audit later.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ask the model to guess authorization.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable the authorization layer permanently.\"}]","a","High-risk controls commonly fail closed."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent reads untrusted web content and can also modify production systems. Which safety posture is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Layer prompt-injection defenses with scoped tools, sandboxing/permissions, authorization, and approval where needed.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only a stronger system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Trust the web page because the agent fetched it.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give broader tools so the agent can recover from mistakes.\"}]","a","No single prompt-level defense is sufficient."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An output moderation check runs only after an irreversible transfer has already executed. What is wrong?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The control is placed after the point where it could prevent the harmful action.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Moderation should always occur after side effects.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The model should have more tokens.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Transfers should never be logged.\"}]","a","Controls must sit at boundaries where they can enforce the property."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which statement best describes a system prompt as a guardrail?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"It is useful behavioral guidance but should not be the sole enforcement mechanism for hard security properties.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"It is equivalent to a permission system.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"It guarantees compliance with any stated rule.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"It makes sandboxing unnecessary.\"}]","a","Prompt controls are probabilistic; enforcement needs stronger boundaries."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A web page contains hidden text telling the browsing agent to upload secrets to an attacker. What failure mode is this?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Indirect prompt injection.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Model deprecation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ordinary lexical retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A/B contamination.\"}]","a","The malicious instruction is delivered through external content."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent has production write access even though its task is read-only analysis. Which risk is most direct?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Excessive agency / unnecessary capability.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Insufficient context length.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Prompt caching.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Underfitting a grader.\"}]","a","Permissions exceed what the task requires."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent loops through tools for hours and consumes a large budget. Which controls are most relevant?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Iteration/token/cost budgets, timeouts, rate limits, and stopping conditions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only a friendlier system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More write permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disabling monitoring.\"}]","a","Resource exhaustion needs enforceable execution limits."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A third-party MCP server is compromised. What architecture most limits damage?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provenance/review plus sandboxing, least privilege, scoped credentials, and monitored boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust all MCP servers because the protocol is standard.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give the server broader credentials to simplify failures.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove version pinning and review.\"}]","a","Tool/supply-chain risk requires constrained trust."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An AI proposes a large irreversible wire transfer. Which review pattern is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Human approval before the transfer executes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Review the transfer a week later.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Sample 1% after execution only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Let model confidence determine authorization.\"}]","a","High-consequence irreversible actions favor pre-action approval."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A mature low-risk classification workflow needs ongoing quality oversight without reviewing every case. What fits?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Sampled human review combined with monitoring.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Pre-approve every single low-risk label.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove all human oversight permanently.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Review only when the model says it is confident.\"}]","a","Sampling can monitor a mature lower-risk process without erasing automation value."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A reviewer sees only “Approve? yes/no” with no source evidence or policy. What is the main weakness?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The human cannot exercise meaningful judgment and may become a rubber stamp.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Human review must never show evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The model should hide uncertainty.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Approval should happen after execution.\"}]","a","HITL must provide enough context for a real decision."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A reversible low-impact content tag is wrong occasionally. Which oversight approach may be proportionate?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Post-action or sampled review with monitoring, if risk is acceptable.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Mandatory executive pre-approval for every tag.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"No monitoring because the action is reversible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use admin credentials for all cases.\"}]","a","Oversight should be proportionate to consequence and reversibility."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team says, “Our model provider is HIPAA compliant, so our whole app is compliant.” What is wrong?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Application compliance depends on the full system, data flows, controls, agreements, and responsibilities—not one provider alone.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Provider status never matters.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"HIPAA applies only to prompts.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Compliance can be implemented solely in the system prompt.\"}]","a","Compliance is a system-level responsibility."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A GDPR-related requirement affects deletion/retention of personal data. What should the architect do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Map the requirement to specific data lifecycle controls, ownership, and evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Write “comply with GDPR” in the prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep all logs forever just in case.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume the vector database handles deletion automatically.\"}]","a","Regulatory obligations must become operational controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A FedRAMP-scoped system adds a new cloud service. What architecture question is most important?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the service falls within the authorized boundary/control inheritance and change process.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Whether the model likes the service.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Whether prompts become shorter.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Whether the service has more UI features.\"}]","a","Boundary and authorization/control scope are central compliance concerns."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A flashcard claims a specific legal requirement not present in the primary source. What should the study deck do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Avoid or verify the claim against authoritative regulatory guidance before teaching it.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep it because it sounds reasonable.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Attribute it to the model.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Turn it into a mnemonic without verification.\"}]","a","Exact legal obligations require primary-source verification."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An AI system has 95% aggregate accuracy but performs much worse for an important subgroup. What should the team do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate relevant slices and address the disparity rather than relying only on aggregate accuracy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore subgroup results because aggregate accuracy is high.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Hide the subgroup metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Increase logging retention indefinitely.\"}]","a","Aggregate metrics can conceal uneven outcomes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["After a harmful automated decision, the team says “the AI decided.” What governance problem is most direct?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Lack of accountability and ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Too much semantic retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Insufficient prompt caching.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Too many A/B tests.\"}]","a","Organizations remain responsible for system decisions and controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A user asks why a consequential recommendation was made. What transparency approach is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provide relevant evidence, policy/reasoning summary, limitations, and appeal/ownership path without exposing private chain-of-thought.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Reveal raw hidden chain-of-thought.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Say only “the AI decided.”\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Provide no explanation because models are probabilistic.\"}]","a","Transparency should be useful and appropriate to the audience."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team stores every model/tool interaction forever to maximize traceability. What concern should be balanced?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Data minimization, privacy, retention, and access controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Traceability means retention can never be limited.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Privacy does not apply to logs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"More data is always safer.\"}]","a","Traceability must be balanced against unnecessary sensitive-data retention."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support guardrails and safety controls?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use layered independent controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use one giant safety prompt as the only protection.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give admin tools and rely on instructions not to misuse them.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use layered independent controls.; Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing guardrails and safety controls. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log dangerous actions instead of preventing them.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Scope tools and permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Moderate only after irreversible actions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.; Scope tools and permissions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in guardrails and safety controls?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Scope tools and permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give admin tools and rely on instructions not to misuse them.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use human approval for sufficiently consequential actions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat model refusal behavior as deterministic authorization.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Scope tools and permissions.; Use human approval for sufficiently consequential actions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on guardrails and safety controls, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use human approval for sufficiently consequential actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Moderate only after irreversible actions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Fail closed when a required high-risk check cannot be verified.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one giant safety prompt as the only protection.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use human approval for sufficiently consequential actions.; Fail closed when a required high-risk check cannot be verified.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Treat external content as untrusted.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume a better model eliminates prompt injection.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Minimize capability and secret exposure.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give agents secrets they never need.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Treat external content as untrusted.; Minimize capability and secret exposure.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Minimize capability and secret exposure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Call every wrong answer a hallucination.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Trust third-party tools solely because they use MCP.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Minimize capability and secret exposure.; Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give agents secrets they never need.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Review third-party tools/Skills and provenance.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Allow unbounded loops and spending.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.; Review third-party tools/Skills and provenance.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Review third-party tools/Skills and provenance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust third-party tools solely because they use MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Plan prevention, detection, and recovery.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume a better model eliminates prompt injection.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Review third-party tools/Skills and provenance.; Plan prevention, detection, and recovery.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support human-in-the-loop validation?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use pre-action review for high-consequence irreversible actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Place human approval after an irreversible action.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Review every trivial case regardless of cost.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use pre-action review for high-consequence irreversible actions.; Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing human-in-the-loop validation. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Make reviewers rubber-stamp opaque outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use model confidence as the only escalation criterion.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.; Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in human-in-the-loop validation?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Review every trivial case regardless of cost.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use sampling for mature low-risk workflows.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove humans where regulation explicitly requires review.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.; Use sampling for mature low-risk workflows.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on human-in-the-loop validation, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use sampling for mature low-risk workflows.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use model confidence as the only escalation criterion.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep clear escalation criteria and ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Place human approval after an irreversible action.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use sampling for mature low-risk workflows.; Keep clear escalation criteria and ownership.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support regulatory compliance architecture?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Map obligations to enforceable controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Put “comply with GDPR” in a prompt and stop there.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign control ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep sensitive logs indefinitely without policy.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Map obligations to enforceable controls.; Assign control ownership.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing regulatory compliance architecture. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Assign control ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume one compliant vendor makes the whole system compliant.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Collect appropriate evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore data residency/retention when applicable.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Assign control ownership.; Collect appropriate evidence.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in regulatory compliance architecture?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Collect appropriate evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep sensitive logs indefinitely without policy.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define regulated/system boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Invent legal requirements from memory.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Collect appropriate evidence.; Define regulated/system boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production system focused on regulatory compliance architecture, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define regulated/system boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore data residency/retention when applicable.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use primary regulatory sources for exact requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Put “comply with GDPR” in a prompt and stop there.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define regulated/system boundaries.; Use primary regulatory sources for exact requirements.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support responsible and ethical AI?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate relevant outcome slices.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use aggregate accuracy as the only fairness evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat transparency as raw chain-of-thought disclosure.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Evaluate relevant outcome slices.; Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing responsible and ethical AI. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Say “the AI decided” to avoid ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Provide audience-appropriate transparency.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep all sensitive logs forever.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.; Provide audience-appropriate transparency.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in responsible and ethical AI?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provide audience-appropriate transparency.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat transparency as raw chain-of-thought disclosure.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve enough evidence for traceability without unlimited retention.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide known system limitations from affected stakeholders.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Provide audience-appropriate transparency.; Preserve enough evidence for traceability without unlimited retention.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:security\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a defense-in-depth path for a consequential action.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Validate/classify the request\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Let the model reason within scoped context/tools\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Apply deterministic policy and authorization checks\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Require human approval when risk demands it\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute and record the authorized action\"}]","Probabilistic reasoning is surrounded by enforceable controls before execution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a risk-treatment cycle for an identified agent failure mode.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Identify the threat/failure mode\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Reduce likelihood with preventive controls\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Detect attempts or failures with monitoring\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Contain/stop harmful effects\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Recover and add regression/response improvements\"}]","Risk treatment combines prevention, detection, containment, and recovery."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order an indirect-prompt-injection defense path.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Treat external content as untrusted data\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Limit the agent's reachable tools/secrets\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Detect suspicious instructions/behavior where possible\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Re-authorize consequential actions outside the model\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Block or escalate unsafe execution\"}]","Untrusted content is paired with limited capability and independent action controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a meaningful pre-action HITL flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Model proposes the consequential action\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Collect the evidence/policy relevant to review\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Present proposal and context to the authorized reviewer\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Reviewer approves or rejects\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute only approved actions and record the decision\"}]","The human decision occurs before execution and is informed by evidence."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a compliance-control mapping workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Identify the applicable requirement\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Translate it into a technical/operational control\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Assign an owner\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Define evidence that proves operation\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Set review/monitoring cadence\"}]","Compliance becomes actionable through controls, ownership, evidence, and ongoing review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a responsible-AI review of a consequential feature.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Identify affected users and potential harms\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Measure relevant performance/fairness slices\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Define transparency and human ownership\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Implement monitoring/appeal or escalation controls\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Review outcomes and update controls\"}]","Responsible operation begins with affected outcomes and continues through ownership and monitoring."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the architect's first job during discovery?","Translate ambiguous stakeholder language into testable outcomes, constraints, and requirements."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why should adjectives such as “fast” or “accurate” be converted into numbers/tests?","So architecture and acceptance can be evaluated objectively."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What ownership questions belong in discovery?","Who approves requirements, owns residual risk, and supports the system in production."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What makes an architecture recommendation useful?","It explains why the chosen option fits the constraints and what trade-offs it accepts."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why adapt architecture communication by audience?","Different stakeholders need different implications and evidence while the underlying decision remains consistent."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should accompany a recommendation besides benefits?","Costs, risks, alternatives, reversibility, and supporting evidence."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why should stakeholders receive measurable expectations for AI systems?","Probabilistic systems cannot responsibly be described with promises of perfect behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What makes a feedback loop actionable?","A signal, trigger/threshold, owner, investigation process, action, and verification."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["When should a team re-architect instead of merely iterate?","When a fundamental constraint changed or the architecture pattern itself is the bottleneck."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should architecture documentation preserve besides diagrams?","Decision context, constraints, alternatives, rationale, assumptions, ownership, and review triggers."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the purpose of an ADR?","Record a significant architecture decision and the context/trade-offs behind it."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What lifecycle phases are explicitly in the CCAR-P objective?","Discovery, design, handoff, monitoring, and iteration."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why cannot monitoring compensate for missing discovery?","You cannot monitor success reliably if requirements and acceptance criteria were never defined."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Functional requirement","What the solution must do."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Non-functional requirement","How the solution must operate, such as latency, availability, scale, residency, or cost."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trade-off","A deliberate exchange where improving one property costs or constrains another."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Reversibility","How easily and cheaply an architecture decision can be changed later."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Feedback signal","Observed evidence such as user reports, tool errors, cost drift, or safety incidents."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["SLA","An agreed service-level expectation/commitment for measurable service behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["ADR","Architecture Decision Record documenting a significant decision, context, alternatives, and rationale."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Runbook","Operational guidance for diagnosing, responding to, and recovering from known conditions/incidents."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Handoff","Transition from architecture/design into implementation and operational ownership with acceptance criteria and guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Iteration","Evidence-driven changes after design/launch, accompanied by updated evaluation and documentation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Discovery should turn vague goals into {{c1::observable acceptance criteria}} before design.","D6.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A stakeholder's proposed implementation is not the same as the underlying {{c1::requirement}}.","D6.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Unresolved assumptions should have a named {{c1::owner}} rather than remaining implicit.","D6.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A strong recommendation explains {{c1::why the option fits the constraints}}, not just what components it uses.","D6.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Architecture communication should expose meaningful {{c1::trade-offs}} rather than hiding concessions.","D6.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A useful feedback loop has a signal, trigger, owner, action, and {{c1::verification}}.","D6.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A user thumbs-down is a {{c1::signal}}, not by itself a complete root-cause evaluation.","D6.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["An architecture diagram without {{c1::decision rationale}} is incomplete for long-term handoff.","D6.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Document decisions that are expensive, risky, or {{c1::hard to reverse}}.","D6.4"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["The CCAR-P lifecycle is discovery → design → handoff → monitoring → {{c1::iteration}}.","D6.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Handoff is incomplete without explicit {{c1::ownership and acceptance criteria}}.","D6.5"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What requirement category describes what the system must do?","Functional requirement"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What requirement category covers latency, availability, scale, and cost?","Non-functional requirement"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes the cost/ease of changing an architecture decision later?","Reversibility"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What term describes exchanging one architecture benefit for another cost or constraint?","Trade-off"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What agreement sets measurable service expectations such as latency or availability?","SLA"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What should happen after a feedback-driven change to confirm it worked?","Verification"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What document records an architecture decision, context, alternatives, and rationale?","ADR"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What lifecycle phase follows design before production operation?","Handoff"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A stakeholder says the assistant must be “very fast.” What should the architect ask next?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define a measurable latency target such as an agreed percentile/SLA.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the fastest model immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assume “fast” means under one minute.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore latency until after launch.\"}]","a","Discovery converts adjectives into measurable criteria."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A stakeholder asks for an agent but cannot explain the desired outcome. What is the best next step?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clarify the workflow problem, baseline, users, constraints, and success criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Start implementing an autonomous agent.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Pick tools before understanding users.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat “agent” as the business requirement.\"}]","a","Implementation language should not replace requirements discovery."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A proposed workflow handles sensitive data, but nobody has identified who owns residual privacy risk. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explicit risk/decision ownership as part of requirements and governance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More retrieval documents.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A second classifier.\"}]","a","Ownership is a requirement for operating consequential systems."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Two teams disagree on what “correct” means for an extraction task. What should happen before architecture selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Agree on testable quality criteria and representative examples/evals.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the strongest model and let it decide.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Build two unrelated systems.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Delay defining correctness until production.\"}]","a","Quality requirements need a shared measurable definition."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A latency SLA was copied from an unrelated service with no business reason. What should the architect do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Revalidate the target against the actual user workflow and business need.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat every inherited SLA as immutable.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore latency entirely.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change the SLA only after deployment.\"}]","a","Constraints should be justified by the current use case."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An executive asks why an agentic design costs more. Which explanation is most useful?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Connect added autonomy to expected business value, latency/cost impact, and residual risk.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"List every SDK method.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Show only a component diagram.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Say agents are the modern choice.\"}]","a","Executives need outcome, cost, timeline, and major risk implications."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A security reviewer evaluates the same architecture. What should communication emphasize?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identity, trust boundaries, permissions, data flows, and threat controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Marketing slogans.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only UI screenshots.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only token price.\"}]","a","Audience-specific emphasis should address the reviewer's responsibilities."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A proposal lists only the preferred architecture and omits alternatives. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evidence-based trade-off comparison and rationale for rejecting alternatives.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More jargon.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A bigger model.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"More diagrams with no rationale.\"}]","a","Decision quality is clearer when meaningful alternatives and concessions are visible."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Two architectures have different cost, quality, and reversibility. What should the recommendation include?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A comparison against the agreed constraints and the cost/risk of changing later.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only which is newest.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only which uses MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only which has more components.\"}]","a","Trade-off communication is contextual."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A stakeholder asks for 100% correctness from a probabilistic support assistant. What is the strongest response?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define measurable quality targets, unacceptable failure classes, escalation, and verification rather than promise perfection.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Promise 100% if the prompt is long enough.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Hide error rates.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the strongest model and call it deterministic.\"}]","a","Expectations must reflect probabilistic behavior and controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Users click thumbs-down more often after a release. What should the team do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Treat it as a signal, investigate affected cases/trajectories, identify cause, and verify a targeted fix.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the model alone is at fault.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Roll back every time without investigation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore it because thumbs-down is subjective.\"}]","a","Feedback becomes useful through investigation and action."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Prompts have been tuned repeatedly, but the architecture cannot meet a new real-time latency requirement. What is likely needed?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Re-architecture because a fundamental constraint changed.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only add more prompt text.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep the architecture forever.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove monitoring.\"}]","a","Pattern-level constraints can require architectural change."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A safety incident occurs but no threshold defines when to rollback or escalate. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explicit response triggers, ownership, and expected actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A longer model response.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More unrelated metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A second UI theme.\"}]","a","Feedback systems need actionable thresholds and owners."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An ADR says only “Use MCP.” What key information is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Context, alternatives, trade-offs, rationale, assumptions, and review triggers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More screenshots.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A model-generated slogan.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A longer title.\"}]","a","A decision record should preserve why the choice was made."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A system works, but only the original architect knows how to recover from tool failures. What documentation is most needed?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Operational runbooks plus ownership and escalation guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More marketing documentation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only a component logo sheet.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A longer system prompt.\"}]","a","Handoff requires operational knowledge, not just design diagrams."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A model/tool change invalidates assumptions in an old architecture document. What should happen?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Update or supersede the relevant decision/documentation so it matches the current system.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep docs unchanged forever.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Delete all history.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume code comments are enough.\"}]","a","Documentation should track the system/version it describes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which architecture decision most deserves an ADR?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A costly, risky, hard-to-reverse choice with meaningful alternatives.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A trivial typo fix.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A temporary local variable name.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A one-time console command with no architectural impact.\"}]","a","ADRs are most useful for consequential decisions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team launches before agreeing on acceptance criteria, then tries to infer success from dashboards. Which lifecycle problem occurred?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Discovery/design did not define success before handoff/monitoring.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Monitoring should always define requirements retroactively.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Handoff should happen before design.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Iteration eliminates the need for acceptance criteria.\"}]","a","Later phases cannot repair undefined earlier requirements."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Architecture is complete, but no implementation owner or rollback plan exists. Which phase is not ready?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Handoff / implementation readiness.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Discovery only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Retrieval indexing.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Model prompting.\"}]","a","Handoff requires ownership and operational readiness."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Production monitoring finds a new failure mode. What is the strongest lifecycle response?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Feed it into iteration: fix the system, update evals/docs/controls, and verify.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore it because design is complete.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Change prompts without testing.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Delete monitoring evidence.\"}]","a","Monitoring should inform evidence-driven iteration."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A system change alters its risk boundary. What should iteration include?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Update architecture/risk documentation and relevant controls/evals, not only code.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Leave all governance artifacts unchanged.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only change the UI.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove regression tests.\"}]","a","Lifecycle artifacts evolve with behavior and risk."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support structured discovery and requirement gathering?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Ask what changes if the project succeeds.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Accept implementation requests as final requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Establish a baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Copy unrelated SLAs without justification.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Ask what changes if the project succeeds.; Establish a baseline.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing structured discovery and requirement gathering. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Establish a baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Design before defining success.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Quantify quality and latency requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Leave risk ownership implicit.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Establish a baseline.; Quantify quality and latency requirements.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve structured discovery and requirement gathering?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Quantify quality and latency requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Copy unrelated SLAs without justification.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify prohibited/high-risk behavior early.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Wait until launch to decide what errors are catastrophic.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Quantify quality and latency requirements.; Identify prohibited/high-risk behavior early.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production program focused on structured discovery and requirement gathering, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identify prohibited/high-risk behavior early.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Leave risk ownership implicit.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign ownership for unresolved assumptions and production support.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Accept implementation requests as final requirements.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Identify prohibited/high-risk behavior early.; Assign ownership for unresolved assumptions and production support.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explain benefit, cost, and risk together.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Hide trade-offs to sell the proposal.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compare alternatives against the same constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Present diagrams without rationale.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Explain benefit, cost, and risk together.; Compare alternatives against the same constraints.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare alternatives against the same constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give every audience the same technical detail.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Compare options without shared constraints.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Compare alternatives against the same constraints.; Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Present diagrams without rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Discuss reversibility for costly decisions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Recommend technology because it is fashionable.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.; Discuss reversibility for costly decisions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production program focused on communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Discuss reversibility for costly decisions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Compare options without shared constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use evidence to support recommendations.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide trade-offs to sell the proposal.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Discuss reversibility for costly decisions.; Use evidence to support recommendations.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Set measurable expectations.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Promise deterministic perfection.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat every complaint as a model failure.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Set measurable expectations.; Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Say “we'll improve from feedback” with no mechanism.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Investigate before attributing cause.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep tuning prompts when architecture is the bottleneck.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.; Investigate before attributing cause.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Investigate before attributing cause.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat every complaint as a model failure.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Verify changes after action.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Create SLAs with no monitoring or response plan.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Investigate before attributing cause.; Verify changes after action.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production program focused on stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Verify changes after action.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep tuning prompts when architecture is the bottleneck.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Re-architect when the pattern no longer fits constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Promise deterministic perfection.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Verify changes after action.; Re-architect when the pattern no longer fits constraints.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support architecture documentation and implementation guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Record rationale and alternatives.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Produce diagrams with no rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Document assumptions and review triggers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Leave docs stale after major changes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Record rationale and alternatives.; Document assumptions and review triggers.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing architecture documentation and implementation guidance. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Document assumptions and review triggers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let critical knowledge live only in one person's head.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep implementation contracts close to the system.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Record only the chosen technology name.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Document assumptions and review triggers.; Keep implementation contracts close to the system.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve architecture documentation and implementation guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep implementation contracts close to the system.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Leave docs stale after major changes.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Provide runbooks for operations.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Omit rollback/operational guidance from handoff.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep implementation contracts close to the system.; Provide runbooks for operations.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production program focused on architecture documentation and implementation guidance, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provide runbooks for operations.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Record only the chosen technology name.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Make ownership explicit.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Produce diagrams with no rationale.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Provide runbooks for operations.; Make ownership explicit.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support solution lifecycle management?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Complete discovery before committing architecture.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Launch with no acceptance criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define acceptance criteria before handoff.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Monitor infrastructure only.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Complete discovery before committing architecture.; Define acceptance criteria before handoff.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing solution lifecycle management. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define acceptance criteria before handoff.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Handoff without ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign implementation and operations ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change behavior without updating evals.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define acceptance criteria before handoff.; Assign implementation and operations ownership.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve solution lifecycle management?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Assign implementation and operations ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Monitor infrastructure only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Monitor real outcomes after launch.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use monitoring to compensate for undefined requirements.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Assign implementation and operations ownership.; Monitor real outcomes after launch.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a structured discovery flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Clarify the business outcome and baseline\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Map users and current workflow\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Define measurable quality/latency/scale constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Identify risk/compliance boundaries\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Assign owners and acceptance criteria\"}]","Discovery progresses from outcome/workflow to measurable constraints and ownership."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a concise architecture-decision explanation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"State the decision context/constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Present the recommended option\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Explain benefits and evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Explain costs/risks and alternatives\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"State ownership/review triggers\"}]","The audience first needs context, then recommendation and its trade-offs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order an actionable stakeholder feedback loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Collect a signal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Compare it to a trigger/threshold\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Assign investigation to the owner\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Take the targeted action\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Verify the outcome and update expectations/evals\"}]","Signals drive owned investigation, action, and verification."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a useful ADR structure.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Describe context and constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"State the decision\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Record meaningful alternatives\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Explain trade-offs and rationale\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Record assumptions, owner, and review trigger\"}]","ADRs preserve why a decision was made and when it may need revisiting."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order the CCAR-P solution lifecycle.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Discovery\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Design\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Handoff\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Monitoring\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Iteration\"}]","The blueprint explicitly frames these phases in this lifecycle order."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a monitoring-to-iteration loop after launch.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Observe production signal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Investigate against requirements/evals\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Decide the targeted change\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Update system plus relevant docs/evals/controls\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Verify in monitoring\"}]","Production evidence drives controlled iteration and verification."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the key distinction between an instruction and a control?","An instruction influences model behavior; a control enforces what the runtime is permitted to do."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why should team-level Claude configuration be standardized?","Shared guidance, tools, permissions, and Skills reduce inconsistent behavior and operational drift."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should AI-assisted development optimize?","Developer throughput while preserving independent verification, security boundaries, and human accountability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["How should verification strength change with consequence?","More consequential changes require stronger independent tests, review, and approval."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What is the core operational debugging loop?","Move from symptom to evidence to likely layer to fix to verification."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Why should a runbook include rollback/fallback and an owner?","Operators need safe recovery actions and clear escalation responsibility during incidents."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Instruction","Guidance intended to influence model behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Runtime control","An enforceable runtime, permission, sandbox, policy, or CI boundary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Verification tool","An independent mechanism such as tests, linters, type checks, security scans, or CI used to check generated changes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Reviewability","The ability for developers to understand and own an AI-generated change."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Operational runbook","Documented operational steps for diagnosis, mitigation, rollback/fallback, escalation, and evidence preservation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["“Do not modify production” is an instruction; removing production credentials is an enforceable {{c1::control}}.","D7.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Shared Skills and configuration should be {{c1::versioned and reviewed}} like other operational assets.","D7.1"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["AI assistance should accelerate the engineering loop, not bypass {{c1::CI, code review, or security boundaries}}.","D7.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["The more consequential the change, the stronger the {{c1::independent verification}} required.","D7.2"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["Operational debugging should proceed from symptom → evidence → likely layer → fix → {{c1::verification}}.","D7.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["A production incident fix should become a {{c1::regression test}} when possible.","D7.3"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What mechanism enforces what the runtime is permitted to do?","Control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What reusable Anthropic package can contain instructions, scripts, and resources?","Agent Skill"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What quality means developers can understand and own an AI-generated change?","Reviewability"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What document gives repeatable incident diagnosis and recovery steps?","Runbook"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A team tells Claude Code “never touch production,” but every developer environment has production admin credentials. What is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Remove/restrict production credentials and permissions; keep the instruction as supplemental guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Repeat the instruction more often.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Disable code review.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give the model more context about production.\"}]","a","Hard permission boundaries should not depend on model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Each developer has a different MCP/tool configuration and shared workflows behave inconsistently. What should the team do?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Standardize high-value repository/team configuration and version it.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Encourage every developer to improvise permanently.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Hide configuration from version control.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give all developers broader credentials.\"}]","a","Shared configuration improves reproducibility and governance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A third-party Skill contains scripts and external resources. What should happen before team-wide adoption?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Review provenance/content, test it, and constrain permissions appropriately.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust it because it is called a Skill.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give it full production access first.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Skip review because Skills are only text.\"}]","a","Skills can affect behavior and execution and should be governed."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which is an enforceable control rather than an instruction?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A sandbox/network policy that prevents access to production.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A sentence saying “be careful.”\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A README asking the agent not to deploy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A prompt example showing a safe action.\"}]","a","Enforceable boundaries restrict capability independently of model choice."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent writes a large refactor and tests pass, but nobody reviews whether the tests cover the risk. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Independent human/system verification of both the change and test adequacy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Production credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fewer tests.\"}]","a","Passing tests are evidence, not a substitute for judging whether verification is sufficient."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A developer asks an agent to “make it work” using production admin credentials. What is the strongest correction?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use a scoped development/test environment and require approval for shared/destructive actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let the agent proceed because the developer asked.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Disable logs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove rollback mechanisms.\"}]","a","Developer productivity should not expand unnecessary production capability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["AI-generated code is merged, but no team member understands it well enough to maintain it. What principle was violated?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reviewability and human accountability for the change.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Prompt caching.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Semantic retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Model lifecycle.\"}]","a","Teams must be able to own and maintain generated changes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Quality drops after a deployment. Which evidence should be checked first?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Model/prompt versions, retrieval/index changes, traces, and input-distribution changes around the deployment.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only ask the model why it failed.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Delete old logs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Immediately add production admin access.\"}]","a","Debugging starts from correlated evidence around the affected layer/change."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["An agent suddenly receives “permission denied” from a tool. What areas are most relevant?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Credentials, scopes, authorization policy, tool contract, and dependency status.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"RAG chunk size only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model temperature only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Business ROI only.\"}]","a","Tool failures should be diagnosed at the integration/permission boundary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A cross-tenant data leak is observed. How should it be treated?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"As a security incident focused on authorization/filtering boundaries, with containment and evidence preservation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"As an ordinary style-quality issue.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"By only rewriting the prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"By deleting logs immediately.\"}]","a","Cross-tenant exposure is a security boundary failure."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support team-level Claude tools and environments?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Standardize shared high-value configuration.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Rely on one giant instruction file for enforcement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Let each developer use unreviewed global Skills.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Standardize shared high-value configuration.; Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing team-level Claude tools and environments. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give broad credentials because setup is easier.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Review third-party tools/Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat prompts as equivalent to permissions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.; Review third-party tools/Skills.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve team-level Claude tools and environments?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Review third-party tools/Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let each developer use unreviewed global Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Version shared instructions and Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep critical team configuration undocumented.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Review third-party tools/Skills.; Version shared instructions and Skills.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For a production team focused on team-level Claude tools and environments, which TWO statements are strongest?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Version shared instructions and Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat prompts as equivalent to permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep credentials scoped to the environment's needs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely on one giant instruction file for enforcement.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Version shared instructions and Skills.; Keep credentials scoped to the environment's needs.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support AI-assisted developer workflows?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provide goals, constraints, and acceptance criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Merge solely because the agent says tests passed.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable safeguards the agent finds inconvenient.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Provide goals, constraints, and acceptance criteria.; Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing AI-assisted developer workflows. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use production admin credentials for convenience.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Scope permissions to reversible local work by default.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Accept generated code nobody can maintain.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.; Scope permissions to reversible local work by default.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve AI-assisted developer workflows?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Scope permissions to reversible local work by default.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Disable safeguards the agent finds inconvenient.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Require stronger review for consequential changes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat AI assistance as a replacement for accountability.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Scope permissions to reversible local work by default.; Require stronger review for consequential changes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO practices best support debugging and operational issue resolution?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use correlated traces/evidence to isolate failures.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ask the model why it failed as the only incident process.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume every operator needs production admin access.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use correlated traces/evidence to isolate failures.; Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["An architect is reviewing debugging and operational issue resolution. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep logs that cannot correlate components.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define rollback/fallback and escalation owners.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fix incidents without regression tests.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.; Define rollback/fallback and escalation owners.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO decisions best improve debugging and operational issue resolution?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define rollback/fallback and escalation owners.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume every operator needs production admin access.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve evidence appropriately.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat security boundary failures as ordinary quality bugs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define rollback/fallback and escalation owners.; Preserve evidence appropriately.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a team enablement flow for a new Claude tool/Skill.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the intended team use case\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Review provenance and required permissions\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Configure the tool/Skill in a scoped environment\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Test behavior and controls\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Version and roll out the approved configuration\"}]","Use case and security review precede scoped rollout."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a safe AI-assisted coding loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the task and acceptance criteria\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Let the agent explore/implement within scoped permissions\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run independent automated checks\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Review the change and evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Merge/deploy through normal controlled processes\"}]","AI generation is followed by independent verification and normal release controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Order a repeatable incident-resolution loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Detect the symptom/alert\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Collect correlated evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify and isolate the likely failing layer\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Mitigate/fix with rollback or safe recovery as needed\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Verify and add regression coverage\"}]","Evidence-driven diagnosis precedes mitigation and regression protection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p0\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A stakeholder says, “Build us an autonomous agent.” What should the architect do first?","Clarify the business outcome, constraints, and measurable success criteria. Architecture starts from the outcome and constraints; “agent” is an implementation hypothesis."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: A finance workflow must classify expenses but refunds over $500 require exact enforcement. Where should the $500 rule live?","In deterministic policy/authorization logic outside the model. Hard thresholds should not depend on probabilistic model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this translating business problems into Claude-based solutions situation? A team has not defined what “better customer support” means. What is the best architecture next step?","Define measurable outcome and acceptance criteria before selecting components. A solution cannot be evaluated without a measurable target."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Which requirement should most strongly constrain architecture before model selection?","A rule that regulated decisions require human approval. Risk constraints can rule out otherwise capable architectures."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Outcome requirement — D1.1 application","The measurable value or change the solution should create."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Risk constraint — D1.1 application","A condition defining what the system must not do without stronger controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["business outcome — D1.1 application","Phrase that completes this translating business problems into Claude-based solutions rule: Architecture should begin with the _____, not the preferred AI component."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
