{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, the precise answer to “What requirement category includes latency, availability, residency, throughput, and cost constraints?” is {{c1::Non-functional requirements}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, the precise answer to “What implementation request should be treated as a hypothesis rather than a requirement when a stakeholder asks for one?” is {{c1::Agent}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, what term matches this definition: The measurable value or change the solution should create.","Outcome requirement"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, what term matches this definition: A condition defining what the system must not do without stronger controls.","Risk constraint"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved translating business problems into Claude-based solutions rule? Architecture should begin with the _____, not the preferred AI component.","business outcome"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A stakeholder says, “Build us an autonomous agent.” What should the architect do first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the most capable Claude model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Create a multi-agent architecture.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Implement MCP for every backend.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clarify the business outcome, constraints, and measurable success criteria.\"}]","a","Architecture starts from the outcome and constraints; “agent” is an implementation hypothesis. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved translating business problems into Claude-based solutions guidance to this case: A finance workflow must classify expenses but refunds over $500 require exact enforcement. Where should the $500 rule live?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"In a few-shot example.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only in the model's explanation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"In deterministic policy/authorization logic outside the model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only in the system prompt.\"}]","a","Hard thresholds should not depend on probabilistic model compliance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A team has not defined what “better customer support” means. What is the best architecture next step?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Start with an autonomous agent and refine later.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define measurable outcome and acceptance criteria before selecting components.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add retrieval immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Benchmark the largest model.\"}]","a","A solution cannot be evaluated without a measurable target. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Which requirement should most strongly constrain architecture before model selection? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A rule that regulated decisions require human approval.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A preference for a fashionable framework.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A desire to use as many tools as possible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A preference for longer prompts.\"}]","a","Risk constraints can rule out otherwise capable architectures. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a translating business problems into Claude-based solutions review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support translating business problems into Claude-based solutions?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use prompt wording as the only authorization control.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Select the strongest model before clarifying the workload.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.; Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on translating business problems into Claude-based solutions? Context: An architect is reviewing translating business problems into Claude-based solutions. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Skip measurable targets until after launch.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat the word “agent” as a mandatory architecture requirement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.; Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in translating business problems into Claude-based solutions?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use prompt wording as the only authorization control.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define success and failure criteria before implementation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume every step should use an LLM.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.; Define success and failure criteria before implementation.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A support agent can issue account credits. Which architecture is strongest?","Let Claude propose the credit, then deterministically verify identity, amount, and permission before execution. Consequential actions need explicit authorization and safe failure behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for end-to-end Claude architecture: A tool times out after a payment request, and the client cannot tell whether the payment executed. What must the architecture consider before retrying?","Whether the operation is idempotent or has an idempotency key. Blind retries of non-idempotent side effects can duplicate actions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this end-to-end Claude architecture situation? A vector index contains yesterday's account balance. The user asks for the current balance. What should supply the answer?","The authoritative account system/API. Current operational state should come from the system of record."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A multi-step agent fails intermittently, but no component shares a trace identifier. What architecture capability is missing?","End-to-end observability/correlation across the request path. The system must be reconstructable across components."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["System of record — D1.2 application","The authoritative source for current operational state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Idempotent retry — D1.2 application","A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["state ownership — D1.2 application","Phrase that completes this end-to-end Claude architecture rule: For stateful workflows, define _____ explicitly rather than treating model context as durable state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In end-to-end Claude architecture, {{c1::System of record}} is the concept described as: The authoritative source for current operational state.","Applied reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In end-to-end Claude architecture, {{c1::Idempotent retry}} is the concept described as: A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect.","Applied reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For end-to-end Claude architecture, the precise answer to “What term describes the authoritative source for current operational state?” is {{c1::System of record}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For end-to-end Claude architecture, the precise answer to “What property allows a side effect to be safely retried without unintended duplication?” is {{c1::Idempotency}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within end-to-end Claude architecture, what term matches this definition: The authoritative source for current operational state.","System of record"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within end-to-end Claude architecture, what term matches this definition: A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect.","Idempotent retry"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved end-to-end Claude architecture rule? For stateful workflows, define _____ explicitly rather than treating model context as durable state.","state ownership"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support agent can issue account credits. Which architecture is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let Claude issue the credit directly if the prompt says to be cautious.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Store account balance in conversation memory.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry the credit call automatically after any timeout without idempotency.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Let Claude propose the credit, then deterministically verify identity, amount, and permission before execution.\"}]","a","Consequential actions need explicit authorization and safe failure behavior. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved end-to-end Claude architecture guidance to this case: A tool times out after a payment request, and the client cannot tell whether the payment executed. What must the architecture consider before retrying?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Whether the model is the largest available.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Whether the response was friendly.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the operation is idempotent or has an idempotency key.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Whether the prompt is long enough.\"}]","a","Blind retries of non-idempotent side effects can duplicate actions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A vector index contains yesterday's account balance. The user asks for the current balance. What should supply the answer?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A cached summary from yesterday.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The authoritative account system/API.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The vector index because retrieval is faster.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Conversation memory.\"}]","a","Current operational state should come from the system of record. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A multi-step agent fails intermittently, but no component shares a trace identifier. What architecture capability is missing? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"End-to-end observability/correlation across the request path.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger context window.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More worker agents.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"More verbose system prompts.\"}]","a","The system must be reconstructable across components. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a end-to-end Claude architecture review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support end-to-end Claude architecture?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume chat history is durable application state.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat vector retrieval as the source of truth for current transactions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.; Keep durable application state outside model context.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on end-to-end Claude architecture? Context: An architect is reviewing end-to-end Claude architecture. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Design only the happy path.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Retry every failed side effect blindly.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep durable application state outside model context.; Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For end-to-end Claude architecture, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in end-to-end Claude architecture?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume chat history is durable application state.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Make failures visible to operators.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Let each worker keep conflicting copies of critical state.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.; Make failures visible to operators.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A request always follows classify → retrieve → draft → validate. Which pattern best fits?","A deterministic workflow. The steps are known in advance, so a workflow offers control without unnecessary autonomy."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: A research task requires discovering unknown subquestions and adapting to tool results. Which pattern is most appropriate?","A bounded agent with dynamic planning. Dynamic planning is valuable when the necessary steps cannot be predicted reliably."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns situation? One model call plus retrieval reliably solves a bounded classification task. What should the architect do?","Keep the simple augmented-LLM design unless evaluation shows a need for more orchestration. Complexity should earn measurable value."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A system needs flexible investigation but exact approval before money moves. Which architecture is strongest?","A hybrid: bounded agent for investigation plus deterministic approval/execution gates. Hybrid designs place flexibility where useful and deterministic controls at consequential boundaries."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Workflow — D1.3 application","LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Agent — D1.3 application","A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Workflow — rule application in choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns","Phrase that completes this choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns rule: A _____ follows predefined paths, while an agent dynamically chooses its process."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, {{c1::Workflow}} is the concept described as: LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths.","Applied reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, {{c1::Agent}} is the concept described as: A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use.","Applied reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, the precise answer to “What pattern uses predefined LLM/tool code paths?” is {{c1::Workflow}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, the precise answer to “What pattern lets the model dynamically choose steps and tool use?” is {{c1::Agent}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, what term matches this definition: LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths.","Workflow"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, what term matches this definition: A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use.","Agent"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns rule? A _____ follows predefined paths, while an agent dynamically chooses its process.","workflow"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A request always follows classify → retrieve → draft → validate. Which pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fully autonomous agent.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A multi-agent swarm.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"An open-ended planner with unrestricted tools.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A deterministic workflow.\"}]","a","The steps are known in advance, so a workflow offers control without unnecessary autonomy. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns guidance to this case: A research task requires discovering unknown subquestions and adapting to tool results. Which pattern is most appropriate?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A rigid workflow with every path enumerated.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A schema validator alone.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A bounded agent with dynamic planning.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fixed one-step prompt only.\"}]","a","Dynamic planning is valuable when the necessary steps cannot be predicted reliably. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? One model call plus retrieval reliably solves a bounded classification task. What should the architect do?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Split every label into a separate agent.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep the simple augmented-LLM design unless evaluation shows a need for more orchestration.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents for resilience.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add an evaluator loop by default.\"}]","a","Complexity should earn measurable value. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A system needs flexible investigation but exact approval before money moves. Which architecture is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A hybrid: bounded agent for investigation plus deterministic approval/execution gates.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fully autonomous agent with a warning prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A fixed workflow that cannot adapt to evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only a human with no automation.\"}]","a","Hybrid designs place flexibility where useful and deterministic controls at consequential boundaries. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents before testing a single-agent design.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use a workflow when steps are predictable.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an agent whenever a task has more than one step.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use a workflow when steps are predictable.; Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns? Context: An architect is reviewing choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat autonomy as inherently better.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume tool use automatically makes a system an agent.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.; Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents before testing a single-agent design.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use hybrids to combine flexible reasoning with deterministic gates.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore repeated-inference latency and cost.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep simple augmented calls when they already meet quality.; Use hybrids to combine flexible reasoning with deterministic gates.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? Financial, legal, and technical diligence can be researched independently. What architecture best exploits this?","Parallel specialist workers coordinated by an orchestrator. Independent specialist work benefits from parallelism and context isolation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for multi-agent orchestration: Three workers write into one mutable state object and overwrite each other's assumptions. What should be improved first?","Define state ownership and explicit handoff/output contracts. Coordination boundaries and state ownership are core multi-agent design concerns."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this multi-agent orchestration situation? A single agent with two tools already completes a task reliably. What is the strongest reason NOT to add three specialist agents?","The extra coordination complexity has no demonstrated benefit. Multi-agent complexity should be justified by isolation, parallelism, or specialization."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: An orchestrator assumes every worker completed its assigned section and publishes an incomplete report. What control is missing?","Coverage/completeness validation before synthesis. The coordinator must verify required work, not merely concatenate outputs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Orchestrator — D1.4 application","The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Context isolation — D1.4 application","Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["isolation, parallelism, or specialization — D1.4 application","Phrase that completes this multi-agent orchestration rule: Multi-agent systems are justified by meaningful _____, not by novelty."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In multi-agent orchestration, {{c1::Orchestrator}} is the concept described as: The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results.","Applied reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In multi-agent orchestration, {{c1::Context isolation}} is the concept described as: Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution.","Applied reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For multi-agent orchestration, the precise answer to “What multi-agent pattern uses a lead agent to delegate bounded subtasks?” is {{c1::Orchestrator-workers}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For multi-agent orchestration, the precise answer to “What term describes keeping worker contexts separate to reduce interference?” is {{c1::Context isolation}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within multi-agent orchestration, what term matches this definition: The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results.","Orchestrator"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within multi-agent orchestration, what term matches this definition: Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution.","Context isolation"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Financial, legal, and technical diligence can be researched independently. What architecture best exploits this? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One shared mutable prompt for all workers.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A worker agent for every sentence.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A fixed sequential chain even though tasks are independent.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallel specialist workers coordinated by an orchestrator.\"}]","a","Independent specialist work benefits from parallelism and context isolation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved multi-agent orchestration guidance to this case: Three workers write into one mutable state object and overwrite each other's assumptions. What should be improved first?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add more workers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove tracing to reduce overhead.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define state ownership and explicit handoff/output contracts.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase model temperature.\"}]","a","Coordination boundaries and state ownership are core multi-agent design concerns. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A single agent with two tools already completes a task reliably. What is the strongest reason NOT to add three specialist agents?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Subagents cannot have separate context.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The extra coordination complexity has no demonstrated benefit.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Agents cannot call tools.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallelism is never useful.\"}]","a","Multi-agent complexity should be justified by isolation, parallelism, or specialization. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An orchestrator assumes every worker completed its assigned section and publishes an incomplete report. What control is missing? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Coverage/completeness validation before synthesis.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger font in the final report.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More token budget for the orchestrator only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Removing worker boundaries.\"}]","a","The coordinator must verify required work, not merely concatenate outputs. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a multi-agent orchestration review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support multi-agent orchestration?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume worker completion without validation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Create one agent per trivial step.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.; Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on multi-agent orchestration? Context: An architect is reviewing multi-agent orchestration. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Lose trace continuity at handoffs.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Share mutable critical state without ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Propagate trace identity across workers.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.; Propagate trace identity across workers.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For multi-agent orchestration, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in multi-agent orchestration?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Propagate trace identity across workers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume worker completion without validation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign state ownership deliberately.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use multi-agent architecture when one agent already meets requirements.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Propagate trace identity across workers.; Assign state ownership deliberately.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A document must be translated, then summarized, then checked for required fields. Which decomposition pattern best fits?","Prompt chaining with validation between stages. Each stage depends on the preceding output, so chaining is appropriate."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for decomposing complex problems: Independent searches across four jurisdictions are required. Which pattern best reduces wall-clock time?","Parallelize the independent searches and combine results. Independent work can be parallelized safely."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this decomposing complex problems situation? Requests belong to billing, technical support, or sales, each with different tools. Which pattern best fits?","Routing to specialized paths. Classification followed by specialized handling is the routing pattern."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A generated report can be scored against a precise rubric and revised until it passes. Which pattern fits?","Evaluator-optimizer. The evaluator provides criterion-based feedback to an optimizer/generator."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Parallelization — D1.5 application","Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Routing — D1.5 application","Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In decomposing complex problems, {{c1::Parallelization}} is the concept described as: Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results.","Applied reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In decomposing complex problems, {{c1::Routing}} is the concept described as: Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path.","Applied reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For decomposing complex problems, the precise answer to “What decomposition pattern classifies a request and sends it to a specialized path?” is {{c1::Routing}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within decomposing complex problems, what term matches this definition: Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results.","Parallelization"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within decomposing complex problems, what term matches this definition: Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path.","Routing"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A document must be translated, then summarized, then checked for required fields. Which decomposition pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Unbounded multi-agent exploration.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallel execution of all stages.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No decomposition because multiple calls are always bad.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Prompt chaining with validation between stages.\"}]","a","Each stage depends on the preceding output, so chaining is appropriate. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved decomposing complex problems guidance to this case: Independent searches across four jurisdictions are required. Which pattern best reduces wall-clock time?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Route all four to one identical result.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use evaluator-optimizer without parallel work.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallelize the independent searches and combine results.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Run them sequentially by default.\"}]","a","Independent work can be parallelized safely. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Requests belong to billing, technical support, or sales, each with different tools. Which pattern best fits?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A random worker selection.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Routing to specialized paths.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One giant prompt with every tool.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Evaluator-optimizer only.\"}]","a","Classification followed by specialized handling is the routing pattern. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a decomposing complex problems review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support decomposing complex problems?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Validate useful intermediate outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM for every deterministic transformation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Decompose when stages need different context or tools.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Split work by organizational chart instead of information boundary.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Decompose when stages need different context or tools.; Validate useful intermediate outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on decomposing complex problems? Context: An architect is reviewing decomposing complex problems. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add critique loops with no measurable rubric.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Validate useful intermediate outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Pass entire worker transcripts when concise outputs suffice.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallelize only independent work.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Validate useful intermediate outputs.; Parallelize only independent work.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For decomposing complex problems, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main architecture risk in decomposing complex problems?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallelize only independent work.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM for every deterministic transformation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep deterministic transforms in code when appropriate.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Parallelize steps with hidden dependencies.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Parallelize only independent work.; Keep deterministic transforms in code when appropriate.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? Architecture A halves token cost but doubles human-review time. Architecture B costs more in tokens but sharply reduces review. What should decide?","Compare total operating cost and business outcome, not token cost alone. Business value depends on end-to-end cost and outcome."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for aligning architecture to business value: A team reports 95% model accuracy but cannot say whether customer resolution time improved. What is missing?","A link between technical performance and a business outcome/baseline. Technical metrics must connect to value."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this aligning architecture to business value situation? Which measurement best supports an ROI claim for an automation project?","Change from a pre-defined baseline in a business-relevant outcome, including ongoing costs. ROI requires baseline, outcome, and cost."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Technical metric — D1.6 application","A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Business metric — D1.6 application","An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In aligning architecture to business value, {{c1::Technical metric}} is the concept described as: A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task.","Applied reinforcement for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In aligning architecture to business value, {{c1::Business metric}} is the concept described as: An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction.","Applied reinforcement for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For aligning architecture to business value, the precise answer to “What term describes the starting measurement used to quantify improvement?” is {{c1::Baseline}}.","Applied reinforcement for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within aligning architecture to business value, what term matches this definition: A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task.","Technical metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within aligning architecture to business value, what term matches this definition: An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction.","Business metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Architecture A halves token cost but doubles human-review time. Architecture B costs more in tokens but sharply reduces review. What should decide? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always choose the cheaper model call.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always choose the higher-capability model.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore human-review cost because it is not AI spend.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare total operating cost and business outcome, not token cost alone.\"}]","a","Business value depends on end-to-end cost and outcome. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved aligning architecture to business value guidance to this case: A team reports 95% model accuracy but cannot say whether customer resolution time improved. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More agent autonomy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A second vector database.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A link between technical performance and a business outcome/baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger model.\"}]","a","Technical metrics must connect to value. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Which measurement best supports an ROI claim for an automation project?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Number of tools exposed.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Change from a pre-defined baseline in a business-relevant outcome, including ongoing costs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Number of prompts written.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Total tokens consumed.\"}]","a","ROI requires baseline, outcome, and cost. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a aligning architecture to business value review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support aligning architecture to business value?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat human review as free.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define a baseline before claiming improvement.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize token cost even when task success drops.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define a baseline before claiming improvement.; Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on aligning architecture to business value? Context: An architect is reviewing aligning architecture to business value. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore operations and compliance cost.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Report model accuracy without business context.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Include human review and operational complexity in cost.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.; Include human review and operational complexity in cost.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sound discovery-to-architecture flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the business outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Quantify success and constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Separate model vs deterministic responsibilities\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the simplest viable architecture\"}]","The architecture follows the outcome and constraints, not the reverse. Sequence reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a typical protected request path.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the caller\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate input and gather context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run model/tool work\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply deterministic verification\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute output/action and record telemetry\"}]","Identity and validation precede model/tool work; protected execution follows verification. Sequence reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sensible architecture-escalation strategy.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Test a simple augmented model call\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Add a workflow if predictable stages are needed\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Use a bounded agent if dynamic planning is required\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Add multi-agent complexity only when evaluation justifies it\"}]","Start simple and escalate only when measured requirements demand it. Sequence reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order the orchestrator-worker pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Interpret the overall goal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Decompose into bounded subtasks\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Delegate work to workers\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Collect and validate results\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Synthesize the final result\"}]","The orchestrator plans, delegates, validates, then synthesizes. Sequence reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a prompt-chaining workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Run the first bounded stage\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate its intermediate output\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Pass the validated result to the next stage\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Produce and verify the final output\"}]","Dependent stages execute in order with validation at useful boundaries. Sequence reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A routine classifier passes all quality thresholds on a faster model while a stronger model costs much more. What is the best choice?","Use the faster model for that workload unless other constraints justify the stronger model. Model choice is a workload-specific trade-off, not a prestige decision."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for Claude model selection: A model is being retired. What should the team do before switching to its replacement?","Run task-specific regression, safety, latency, and cost evaluation. Model migration can change behavior and should be evaluated."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this Claude model selection situation? A workflow has easy classification cases and rare complex exceptions. What design may improve economics if validated?","Route routine cases to a fast model and difficult cases to a stronger model. Evaluated routing can match model capability to workload difficulty."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Which evidence is strongest for choosing between two Claude models for a production task?","Results on a representative eval suite for that task plus latency/cost measurements. Architecture should use representative workload evidence."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active model — D2.1 application","A fully supported model recommended for current use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Deprecated model — D2.1 application","A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["quality threshold — D2.1 application","Phrase that completes this Claude model selection rule: Choose the model that meets the workload's _____ at acceptable latency and cost."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In Claude model selection, {{c1::Active model}} is the concept described as: A fully supported model recommended for current use.","Applied reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In Claude model selection, {{c1::Deprecated model}} is the concept described as: A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement.","Applied reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For Claude model selection, the precise answer to “What lifecycle state follows Active in the documented set Active, Legacy, Deprecated, Retired?” is {{c1::Legacy}}.","Applied reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For Claude model selection, the precise answer to “What should compare candidate models on the real workload rather than generic reputation?” is {{c1::Evaluation suite}}.","Applied reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within Claude model selection, what term matches this definition: A fully supported model recommended for current use.","Active model"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within Claude model selection, what term matches this definition: A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement.","Deprecated model"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved Claude model selection rule? Choose the model that meets the workload's _____ at acceptable latency and cost.","quality threshold"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A routine classifier passes all quality thresholds on a faster model while a stronger model costs much more. What is the best choice? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always use the strongest model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always use the cheapest model even if it fails quality.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Route randomly between models.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use the faster model for that workload unless other constraints justify the stronger model.\"}]","a","Model choice is a workload-specific trade-off, not a prestige decision. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved Claude model selection guidance to this case: A model is being retired. What should the team do before switching to its replacement?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only compare benchmark scores.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change the model without testing because the API shape is similar.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run task-specific regression, safety, latency, and cost evaluation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newer model is behaviorally identical.\"}]","a","Model migration can change behavior and should be evaluated. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A workflow has easy classification cases and rare complex exceptions. What design may improve economics if validated?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove evaluation and route by input length only.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Route routine cases to a fast model and difficult cases to a stronger model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use the strongest model for every request by default.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use the cheapest model for every request regardless of errors.\"}]","a","Evaluated routing can match model capability to workload difficulty. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Which evidence is strongest for choosing between two Claude models for a production task? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Results on a representative eval suite for that task plus latency/cost measurements.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A generic leaderboard alone.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Which model name sounds newer.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A single anecdotal prompt.\"}]","a","Architecture should use representative workload evidence. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a Claude model selection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support Claude model selection?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Re-run regressions after model changes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Swap models without regression testing.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate models on the actual workload.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newest model is always best.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Evaluate models on the actual workload.; Re-run regressions after model changes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on Claude model selection? Context: An architect is reviewing Claude model selection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hard-code permanent assumptions about one model name.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Re-run regressions after model changes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose solely from generic benchmark rank.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Include latency and cost alongside quality.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Re-run regressions after model changes.; Include latency and cost alongside quality.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For Claude model selection, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in Claude model selection?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Include latency and cost alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Swap models without regression testing.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Treat current model availability as time-sensitive.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Route only to reduce price even if quality falls below threshold.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Include latency and cost alongside quality.; Treat current model availability as time-sensitive.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A refund policy says amounts over $500 require manager approval. What is the strongest implementation?","Explain the rule in the prompt and enforce the threshold in deterministic approval logic. Prompts guide behavior; protected thresholds need enforceable controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: Retrieved documents may contain malicious instructions. What prompt design is strongest?","Clearly separate untrusted retrieved content from trusted instructions and restrict capabilities independently. Trust boundaries should be explicit and backed by controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this system prompts, templates, and guardrails situation? Downstream software requires valid structured output. What should the architecture add?","An explicit output contract plus schema validation. Structure should be specified and validated when machines depend on it."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A team wants reusable prompts with changing request data. Which design is best?","Keep stable instructions in a template and inject request-specific variables separately. Templates separate stable instructions from variable content."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Behavioral instruction — D2.2 application","Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Enforceable control — D2.2 application","Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["deterministic controls — D2.2 application","Phrase that completes this system prompts, templates, and guardrails rule: Use prompts to guide behavior; use _____ to enforce hard security and policy invariants."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In system prompts, templates, and guardrails, {{c1::Behavioral instruction}} is the concept described as: Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act.","Applied reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In system prompts, templates, and guardrails, {{c1::Enforceable control}} is the concept described as: Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance.","Applied reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For system prompts, templates, and guardrails, the precise answer to “What prompt layer should hold stable high-trust behavioral instructions?” is {{c1::System prompt}}.","Applied reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For system prompts, templates, and guardrails, the precise answer to “What should enforce authorization rather than relying on the model?” is {{c1::Deterministic control}}.","Applied reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within system prompts, templates, and guardrails, what term matches this definition: Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act.","Behavioral instruction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within system prompts, templates, and guardrails, what term matches this definition: Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance.","Enforceable control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails rule? Use prompts to guide behavior; use _____ to enforce hard security and policy invariants.","deterministic controls"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A refund policy says amounts over $500 require manager approval. What is the strongest implementation? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Put the rule only in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use a longer example showing a $499 refund.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ask the model to self-check twice.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explain the rule in the prompt and enforce the threshold in deterministic approval logic.\"}]","a","Prompts guide behavior; protected thresholds need enforceable controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails guidance to this case: Retrieved documents may contain malicious instructions. What prompt design is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell retrieved text it is trusted.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely on the model to always ignore injections.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clearly separate untrusted retrieved content from trusted instructions and restrict capabilities independently.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Concatenate all text into one unstructured prompt.\"}]","a","Trust boundaries should be explicit and backed by controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Downstream software requires valid structured output. What should the architecture add?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"An explicit output contract plus schema validation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only ask for JSON politely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"}]","a","Structure should be specified and validated when machines depend on it. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a system prompts, templates, and guardrails review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support system prompts, templates, and guardrails?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate untrusted content from policy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume asking for JSON guarantees validity.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use clear trusted instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat a system prompt as an access-control list.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use clear trusted instructions.; Separate untrusted content from policy.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on system prompts, templates, and guardrails? Context: An architect is reviewing system prompts, templates, and guardrails. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Mix policy and user data indiscriminately.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Separate untrusted content from policy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let retrieved text rewrite policy.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Validate machine-readable outputs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Separate untrusted content from policy.; Validate machine-readable outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For system prompts, templates, and guardrails, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in system prompts, templates, and guardrails?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Validate machine-readable outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume asking for JSON guarantees validity.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Enforce authorization outside the model.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely only on model refusal for irreversible actions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Validate machine-readable outputs.; Enforce authorization outside the model.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A classifier confuses two boundary cases even with clear instructions. What is a strong next step?","Add a few representative examples that demonstrate the boundary distinction and re-evaluate. Few-shot examples are useful when they target observed ambiguity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for prompt engineering techniques: A straightforward extraction task already meets its quality target zero-shot. What should the team do?","Keep the simpler prompt unless evaluation identifies a failure. Use the lightest technique that passes the evaluation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this prompt engineering techniques situation? A long prompt mixes policy, examples, retrieved text, and user data. What improvement is most direct?","Structure the prompt so trusted instructions, examples, context, and inputs are clearly separated. Clear structure reduces ambiguity about the role of each section."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A retrieval system is returning the wrong document. What is the least promising first response?","Endlessly rewrite the prompt without fixing retrieval. Prompting cannot compensate for missing or wrong evidence indefinitely."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Zero-shot — D2.3 application","Clear direct instructions without worked examples."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Few-shot / multishot — D2.3 application","Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In prompt engineering techniques, {{c1::Zero-shot}} is the concept described as: Clear direct instructions without worked examples.","Applied reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In prompt engineering techniques, {{c1::Few-shot / multishot}} is the concept described as: Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior.","Applied reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For prompt engineering techniques, the precise answer to “What prompting technique provides representative examples?” is {{c1::Few-shot prompting}}.","Applied reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within prompt engineering techniques, what term matches this definition: Clear direct instructions without worked examples.","Zero-shot"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within prompt engineering techniques, what term matches this definition: Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior.","Few-shot / multishot"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A classifier confuses two boundary cases even with clear instructions. What is a strong next step? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add dozens of irrelevant examples.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Switch to an agent immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide the labels from the prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add a few representative examples that demonstrate the boundary distinction and re-evaluate.\"}]","a","Few-shot examples are useful when they target observed ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved prompt engineering techniques guidance to this case: A straightforward extraction task already meets its quality target zero-shot. What should the team do?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add ten examples for safety.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Create a multi-agent workflow.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep the simpler prompt unless evaluation identifies a failure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add chain-of-thought instructions automatically.\"}]","a","Use the lightest technique that passes the evaluation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A long prompt mixes policy, examples, retrieved text, and user data. What improvement is most direct?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove all examples regardless of performance.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Structure the prompt so trusted instructions, examples, context, and inputs are clearly separated.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Repeat every instruction three times.\"}]","a","Clear structure reduces ambiguity about the role of each section. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a prompt engineering techniques review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support prompt engineering techniques?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only easy examples.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Start with clear direct instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Force visible step-by-step reasoning for every task.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Start with clear direct instructions.; Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on prompt engineering techniques? Context: An architect is reviewing prompt engineering techniques. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat retrieval failures as prompt failures.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add examples before establishing a baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Structure complex prompts explicitly.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.; Structure complex prompts explicitly.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For prompt engineering techniques, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in prompt engineering techniques?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Structure complex prompts explicitly.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only easy examples.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use current model-specific thinking guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Overfit a prompt to a tiny static eval.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Structure complex prompts explicitly.; Use current model-specific thinking guidance.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? An agent preloads thousands of pages although each task uses only a few. What is the strongest change?","Retrieve relevant content just in time instead of preloading the corpus. JIT retrieval preserves context for relevant information."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for context-window and token management: A long-running agent approaches practical context limits. What should compaction preserve?","Key decisions, constraints, unresolved work, and important evidence. Compaction reduces size while preserving decision-critical information."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this context-window and token management situation? Two independent research tasks pollute each other's context. What pattern can help?","Use context isolation with separate workers/subagents. Separate contexts reduce interference between independent workstreams."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A team stores the only copy of an order's authoritative state in conversation history. What is wrong?","Application state should live in an authoritative external store, not depend on the model context. Model context is a working set, not durable system state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active context — D2.4 application","Information currently visible to the model for the present inference."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Compaction — D2.4 application","Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In context-window and token management, {{c1::Active context}} is the concept described as: Information currently visible to the model for the present inference.","Applied reinforcement for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In context-window and token management, {{c1::Compaction}} is the concept described as: Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions.","Applied reinforcement for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For context-window and token management, the precise answer to “What technique summarizes a long trace while preserving critical state?” is {{c1::Compaction}}.","Applied reinforcement for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within context-window and token management, what term matches this definition: Information currently visible to the model for the present inference.","Active context"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within context-window and token management, what term matches this definition: Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions.","Compaction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An agent preloads thousands of pages although each task uses only a few. What is the strongest change? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase prompt verbosity.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the corpus in conversation history.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Always use multiple agents.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Retrieve relevant content just in time instead of preloading the corpus.\"}]","a","JIT retrieval preserves context for relevant information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved context-window and token management guidance to this case: A long-running agent approaches practical context limits. What should compaction preserve?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only the last user message.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Nothing; simply drop all prior state.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Key decisions, constraints, unresolved work, and important evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Every raw tool response verbatim.\"}]","a","Compaction reduces size while preserving decision-critical information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Two independent research tasks pollute each other's context. What pattern can help?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Cache every tool result forever.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use context isolation with separate workers/subagents.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Merge all transcripts into one prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"}]","a","Separate contexts reduce interference between independent workstreams. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a context-window and token management review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support context-window and token management?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume larger windows eliminate relevance problems.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Preload every available document.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.; Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on context-window and token management? Context: An architect is reviewing context-window and token management. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Summarize away hard constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat chat history as the database.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep durable state outside model context.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.; Keep durable state outside model context.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A legal workflow reuses the same large policy manual for thousands of requests. What is a strong optimization?","Reuse/cache the stable reference content while fetching case-specific current state separately. Stable repeated context is a good reuse target; volatile state is not."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: A shared Skill changes how production agents perform a regulated workflow. How should it be managed?","Version, review, test, and control changes like other operational assets. Reusable agent instructions/resources can change behavior and should be governed."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this prompt reuse, caching, and Skills situation? Which data is the worst prompt-caching candidate?","A user's current account balance that changes frequently. Caching must not undermine freshness for live state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Prompt template — D2.5 application","Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["stable enough — D2.5 application","Phrase that completes this prompt reuse, caching, and Skills rule: Reuse is safest when the content is _____ that freshness is not compromised."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, {{c1::Prompt template}} is the concept described as: Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables.","Applied reinforcement for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, the precise answer to “What Anthropic mechanism packages reusable instructions, scripts, and resources for agents?” is {{c1::Agent Skills}}.","Applied reinforcement for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["During an operational review, apply this prompt reuse, caching, and Skills rule: In prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, {{c1::Prompt template}} is the concept described as: Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables.","Applied reinforcement for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, what term matches this definition: Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables.","Prompt template"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved prompt reuse, caching, and Skills rule? Reuse is safest when the content is _____ that freshness is not compromised.","stable enough"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A legal workflow reuses the same large policy manual for thousands of requests. What is a strong optimization? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache each client's live case status indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the manual into every variable section.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove freshness checks from current data.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse/cache the stable reference content while fetching case-specific current state separately.\"}]","a","Stable repeated context is a good reuse target; volatile state is not. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved prompt reuse, caching, and Skills guidance to this case: A shared Skill changes how production agents perform a regulated workflow. How should it be managed?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Let every user edit it globally.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Never regression-test Skill changes.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Version, review, test, and control changes like other operational assets.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat it as harmless prose with no review.\"}]","a","Reusable agent instructions/resources can change behavior and should be governed. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Which data is the worst prompt-caching candidate?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A reusable set of examples.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A user's current account balance that changes frequently.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A stable policy manual.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A fixed system instruction block.\"}]","a","Caching must not undermine freshness for live state. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a prompt reuse, caching, and Skills review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support prompt reuse, caching, and Skills?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep volatile state fresh.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one giant reusable prompt for unrelated workloads.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse stable expensive context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache rapidly changing business state indefinitely.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reuse stable expensive context.; Keep volatile state fresh.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on prompt reuse, caching, and Skills? Context: An architect is reviewing prompt reuse, caching, and Skills. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat cache freshness as irrelevant.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep volatile state fresh.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let shared Skills change without review.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Version shared prompt assets and Skills.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep volatile state fresh.; Version shared prompt assets and Skills.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sound model-selection process.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define task quality and operational thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Evaluate candidate models on representative cases\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare quality, latency, cost, and risk\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the model/routing policy\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-test when the model or workload changes\"}]","Requirements and evaluation precede selection; changes trigger re-evaluation. Sequence reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a secure prompt-to-action pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted system instructions\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Insert user/retrieved content as untrusted data\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an output/action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Validate schema and authorization deterministically\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute only if controls pass\"}]","Behavioral prompting precedes deterministic validation and execution. Sequence reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order an evidence-driven prompt-improvement loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish a simple baseline prompt\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Run representative evaluations\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify a specific failure mode\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply the lightest targeted prompting change\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-run evaluation and regression checks\"}]","Prompt complexity should be added in response to observed failures. Sequence reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A support assistant only needs order lookup and refund-request submission, but it has a production database admin credential. What should change first?","Replace the broad credential/tool with scoped capabilities needed for those tasks. Reduce unnecessary capability and blast radius rather than relying on instructions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for tool and agent capability bloat: A coding agent legitimately needs shell access. What is the strongest architecture?","Allow the broad tool inside a constrained sandbox with scoped credentials and permissions. General-purpose capability can be valid when strong containment limits reach and impact."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this tool and agent capability bloat situation? An agent has twelve overlapping CRM tools with vague names and often chooses the wrong one. What is the best improvement?","Reduce overlap and define clearer, distinct tool boundaries and descriptions. Overlapping capability increases selection ambiguity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Which change most directly reduces the blast radius of a read-only reporting agent?","Remove write credentials and destructive tool operations it does not need. Hard capability restriction reduces what can happen if the model is wrong or compromised."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Capability bloat — D3.1 application","Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Least privilege — D3.1 application","Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["blast radius — D3.1 application","Phrase that completes this tool and agent capability bloat rule: More exposed capability increases the potential _____ if an agent is compromised or behaves incorrectly."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In tool and agent capability bloat, {{c1::Capability bloat}} is the concept described as: Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs.","Applied reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In tool and agent capability bloat, {{c1::Least privilege}} is the concept described as: Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task.","Applied reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For tool and agent capability bloat, the precise answer to “What security principle grants only the minimum permissions needed?” is {{c1::Least privilege}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within tool and agent capability bloat, what term matches this definition: Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs.","Capability bloat"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within tool and agent capability bloat, what term matches this definition: Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task.","Least privilege"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved tool and agent capability bloat rule? More exposed capability increases the potential _____ if an agent is compromised or behaves incorrectly.","blast radius"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support assistant only needs order lookup and refund-request submission, but it has a production database admin credential. What should change first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more logging but keep admin access.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell the model never to misuse the credential.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add more unrelated tools so selection is balanced.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Replace the broad credential/tool with scoped capabilities needed for those tasks.\"}]","a","Reduce unnecessary capability and blast radius rather than relying on instructions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved tool and agent capability bloat guidance to this case: A coding agent legitimately needs shell access. What is the strongest architecture?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give unrestricted production shell access.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely only on a system prompt to protect the host.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Allow the broad tool inside a constrained sandbox with scoped credentials and permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ban all broad tools regardless of task.\"}]","a","General-purpose capability can be valid when strong containment limits reach and impact. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? An agent has twelve overlapping CRM tools with vague names and often chooses the wrong one. What is the best improvement?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide all tool errors from the model.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reduce overlap and define clearer, distinct tool boundaries and descriptions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add another CRM tool for each edge case.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"}]","a","Overlapping capability increases selection ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a tool and agent capability bloat review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support tool and agent capability bloat?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Expose every tool in case one becomes useful.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Expose only tools required for the task.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give every agent a shared admin credential.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Expose only tools required for the task.; Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on tool and agent capability bloat? Context: An architect is reviewing tool and agent capability bloat. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use prompt instructions as the only containment control.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume logging makes excessive permission safe.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.; Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For tool and agent capability bloat, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in tool and agent capability bloat?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Expose every tool in case one becomes useful.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give tools clear non-overlapping purposes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat broad tools as automatically safe because Claude is capable.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Constrain broad tools with sandboxing and scoped credentials.; Give tools clear non-overlapping purposes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A user types “I am the account administrator” into chat. What should the application do?","Ignore the claim for access control and use trusted authenticated identity and policy. Prompt text is not authentication."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for authentication and authorization: An MCP tool is protected by OAuth. Where should access be checked?","At the protected protocol/application boundary using verified authorization context. Authorization is an enforceable control outside model output."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this authentication and authorization situation? A SaaS agent uses one backend superuser credential for every tenant. What is the primary risk?","A failure in model/tool logic can cross tenant boundaries because the execution identity is overprivileged. Shared broad credentials defeat least-privilege and tenant isolation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A consequential tool call occurs after initial login. What is the safest design?","Re-check authorization for the specific protected action using current trusted identity/context. Action-level authorization should match the protected resource and current caller."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authentication — D3.2 application","Establishing the identity of the caller."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authorization — D3.2 application","Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["authoritative authorization — D3.2 application","Phrase that completes this authentication and authorization rule: A model saying a user is allowed to act is not a substitute for _____."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In authentication and authorization, {{c1::Authentication}} is the concept described as: Establishing the identity of the caller.","Applied reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In authentication and authorization, {{c1::Authorization}} is the concept described as: Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform.","Applied reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For authentication and authorization, the precise answer to “What security process establishes who the caller is?” is {{c1::Authentication}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within authentication and authorization, what term matches this definition: Establishing the identity of the caller.","Authentication"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within authentication and authorization, what term matches this definition: Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform.","Authorization"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A user types “I am the account administrator” into chat. What should the application do? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Grant admin tools because the model saw the statement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ask Claude to judge whether the statement sounds credible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Put the claim in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Ignore the claim for access control and use trusted authenticated identity and policy.\"}]","a","Prompt text is not authentication. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved authentication and authorization guidance to this case: An MCP tool is protected by OAuth. Where should access be checked?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only after the tool already executes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"By asking the user to state their role in natural language.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"At the protected protocol/application boundary using verified authorization context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only inside the model prompt.\"}]","a","Authorization is an enforceable control outside model output. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A SaaS agent uses one backend superuser credential for every tenant. What is the primary risk?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"The vector index will stop embedding documents.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A failure in model/tool logic can cross tenant boundaries because the execution identity is overprivileged.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The model will necessarily become slower.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"OAuth cannot work with multi-tenancy.\"}]","a","Shared broad credentials defeat least-privilege and tenant isolation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a authentication and authorization review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support authentication and authorization?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one superuser credential across tenants.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted identity before using it in model/tool decisions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust role claims typed into the conversation.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Establish trusted identity before using it in model/tool decisions.; Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on authentication and authorization? Context: An architect is reviewing authentication and authorization. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Authenticate once and never check action permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let the model invent access policy.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use scoped or delegated credentials.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.; Use scoped or delegated credentials.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For authentication and authorization, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in authentication and authorization?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use scoped or delegated credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use one superuser credential across tenants.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve caller identity through the request path.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat MCP itself as automatic authorization.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use scoped or delegated credentials.; Preserve caller identity through the request path.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A reranker improves grounded accuracy by 0.3% but adds 1.5 seconds to a 2-second SLA. What should the architect do?","Evaluate whether the small quality gain justifies violating or consuming most of the latency budget. Accuracy and latency are explicit trade-offs against workload constraints."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for accuracy-latency trade-offs: Four retrieval calls use unrelated sources and do not depend on one another. How can wall-clock time often be reduced?","Run the independent calls in parallel and combine results. Independent work is a good candidate for parallel execution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this accuracy-latency trade-offs situation? A system is slow. Retrieval is 50 ms, model inference 2.8 s, and formatting 20 ms. Where should optimization start?","The dominant model-inference contribution, subject to quality constraints. Optimize the dominant contributor rather than the easiest component."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Tool Search reduces context and wrong-tool calls but adds a lookup step. When is it most justified?","When the accuracy/context benefit outweighs the added lookup latency for the workload. Progressive discovery itself has a trade-off and should be evaluated."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Latency budget — D3.3 application","The portion of end-to-end response time available to system stages under the SLA."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Parallelization for latency — D3.3 application","Executing independent operations concurrently to reduce wall-clock time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In accuracy-latency trade-offs, {{c1::Latency budget}} is the concept described as: The portion of end-to-end response time available to system stages under the SLA.","Applied reinforcement for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In accuracy-latency trade-offs, {{c1::Parallelization for latency}} is the concept described as: Executing independent operations concurrently to reduce wall-clock time.","Applied reinforcement for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For accuracy-latency trade-offs, the precise answer to “What percentile metric is commonly used to represent tail latency rather than only the average?” is {{c1::p95}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within accuracy-latency trade-offs, what term matches this definition: The portion of end-to-end response time available to system stages under the SLA.","Latency budget"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within accuracy-latency trade-offs, what term matches this definition: Executing independent operations concurrently to reduce wall-clock time.","Parallelization for latency"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A reranker improves grounded accuracy by 0.3% but adds 1.5 seconds to a 2-second SLA. What should the architect do? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always keep reranking because quality stages are mandatory.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore the SLA because accuracy always wins.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove required safety checks first.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate whether the small quality gain justifies violating or consuming most of the latency budget.\"}]","a","Accuracy and latency are explicit trade-offs against workload constraints. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved accuracy-latency trade-offs guidance to this case: Four retrieval calls use unrelated sources and do not depend on one another. How can wall-clock time often be reduced?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase prompt length.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the same output from the first call for all four.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run the independent calls in parallel and combine results.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Run them sequentially by default.\"}]","a","Independent work is a good candidate for parallel execution. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A system is slow. Retrieval is 50 ms, model inference 2.8 s, and formatting 20 ms. Where should optimization start?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Randomly remove a safety control.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The dominant model-inference contribution, subject to quality constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Formatting because it is easiest.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Retrieval because RAG is always the bottleneck.\"}]","a","Optimize the dominant contributor rather than the easiest component. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a accuracy-latency trade-offs review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support accuracy-latency trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compare quality gains against SLA impact.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Parallelize dependent steps.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure end-to-end latency by stage.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add reranking because every RAG system must have it.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure end-to-end latency by stage.; Compare quality gains against SLA impact.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on accuracy-latency trade-offs? Context: An architect is reviewing accuracy-latency trade-offs. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove required authorization to save time.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare quality gains against SLA impact.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Measure only average latency.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallelize independent work.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Compare quality gains against SLA impact.; Parallelize independent work.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For accuracy-latency trade-offs, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in accuracy-latency trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallelize independent work.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Parallelize dependent steps.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Optimize the dominant latency contributor.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Optimize tiny stages while ignoring the dominant bottleneck.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Parallelize independent work.; Optimize the dominant latency contributor.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A final answer is wrong, but logs contain only the final text. What is the strongest observability improvement?","Capture correlated trajectory/tool/retrieval events so the failing stage can be identified. Agent failures require visibility into intermediate behavior and dependencies."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for observability at scale: Worker logs exist but cannot be tied back to the originating user request. What is missing?","A propagated trace/correlation identity. Distributed observability needs cross-component correlation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this observability at scale situation? A team logs every prompt, credential, and tool payload indefinitely for debugging. What is the main issue?","Observability itself is creating privacy/security and retention risk. Debuggability must be balanced with data minimization and protection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trace ID — D3.4 application","A correlation identifier used to connect events across components of one request."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trajectory — D3.4 application","The sequence of model/tool interactions taken by an agent during a task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In observability at scale, {{c1::Trace ID}} is the concept described as: A correlation identifier used to connect events across components of one request.","Applied reinforcement for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In observability at scale, {{c1::Trajectory}} is the concept described as: The sequence of model/tool interactions taken by an agent during a task.","Applied reinforcement for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For observability at scale, the precise answer to “What identifier connects logs across model, retrieval, tools, queues, and workers?” is {{c1::Trace ID}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within observability at scale, what term matches this definition: A correlation identifier used to connect events across components of one request.","Trace ID"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within observability at scale, what term matches this definition: The sequence of model/tool interactions taken by an agent during a task.","Trajectory"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A final answer is wrong, but logs contain only the final text. What is the strongest observability improvement? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log the final answer twice.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase model temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove correlation IDs.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Capture correlated trajectory/tool/retrieval events so the failing stage can be identified.\"}]","a","Agent failures require visibility into intermediate behavior and dependencies. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved observability at scale guidance to this case: Worker logs exist but cannot be tied back to the originating user request. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A larger context window.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"An additional prompt example.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A propagated trace/correlation identity.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More workers.\"}]","a","Distributed observability needs cross-component correlation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A team logs every prompt, credential, and tool payload indefinitely for debugging. What is the main issue?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Tracing should only happen after incidents.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Observability itself is creating privacy/security and retention risk.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Logs can never contain sensitive data.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More logs always reduce risk.\"}]","a","Debuggability must be balanced with data minimization and protection. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a observability at scale review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support observability at scale?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep component logs with no correlation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Propagate trace identity across components.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log only the final answer.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Propagate trace identity across components.; Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on observability at scale? Context: An architect is reviewing observability at scale. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Trust model claims over external state.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Store secrets in logs for convenience.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Record tool names/results and dependency failures.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.; Record tool names/results and dependency failures.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A policy assistant keeps answering from an obsolete policy that ranks above the current version. What should be fixed first?","Freshness/metadata/ranking in the retrieval pipeline. The wrong evidence is reaching the model; fix retrieval before prompt wording."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for RAG pipeline design: A document is split at arbitrary character counts, separating headings from their explanations. What should the architect revisit?","Chunking strategy based on source structure and likely queries. Chunk boundaries affect retrieval quality and meaning."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this RAG pipeline design situation? Initial hybrid retrieval returns many plausible chunks but ordering is weak. What optional stage can improve final relevance?","Reranking the candidate set. Reranking refines first-stage candidates with a stronger relevance signal."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Chunking — D3.5 application","Dividing source documents into retrieval units while preserving useful semantic context."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Reranking — D3.5 application","Reordering first-stage retrieval candidates with a stronger relevance signal."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In RAG pipeline design, {{c1::Chunking}} is the concept described as: Dividing source documents into retrieval units while preserving useful semantic context.","Applied reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In RAG pipeline design, {{c1::Reranking}} is the concept described as: Reordering first-stage retrieval candidates with a stronger relevance signal.","Applied reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For RAG pipeline design, the precise answer to “What retrieval stage reorders candidate chunks after initial search?” is {{c1::Reranking}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within RAG pipeline design, what term matches this definition: Dividing source documents into retrieval units while preserving useful semantic context.","Chunking"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within RAG pipeline design, what term matches this definition: Reordering first-stage retrieval candidates with a stronger relevance signal.","Reranking"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A policy assistant keeps answering from an obsolete policy that ranks above the current version. What should be fixed first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Tell Claude to be more accurate without changing retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add another unrelated tool.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Freshness/metadata/ranking in the retrieval pipeline.\"}]","a","The wrong evidence is reaching the model; fix retrieval before prompt wording. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved RAG pipeline design guidance to this case: A document is split at arbitrary character counts, separating headings from their explanations. What should the architect revisit?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model lifecycle state.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Human review sampling rate.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Chunking strategy based on source structure and likely queries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"OAuth scopes.\"}]","a","Chunk boundaries affect retrieval quality and meaning. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Initial hybrid retrieval returns many plausible chunks but ordering is weak. What optional stage can improve final relevance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable metadata.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reranking the candidate set.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Remove indexing.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use only conversation memory.\"}]","a","Reranking refines first-stage candidates with a stronger relevance signal. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a RAG pipeline design review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support RAG pipeline design?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Measure retrieval separately from generation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change prompts when evidence is never retrieved.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Design chunking around document structure and queries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat RAG as synonymous with a vector database.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Design chunking around document structure and queries.; Measure retrieval separately from generation.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on RAG pipeline design? Context: An architect is reviewing RAG pipeline design. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Bypass document permissions during retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure retrieval separately from generation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore stale/current document status.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use metadata for freshness/access filtering where required.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure retrieval separately from generation.; Use metadata for freshness/access filtering where required.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A user searches for exact error code ERR-9F21. Which retrieval signal should be strongly represented?","Lexical/exact-term retrieval such as BM25. Exact identifiers benefit from lexical matching."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for retrieval strategy selection: Users ask policy questions with wording very different from the source text. Which retrieval method helps most?","Semantic embedding retrieval. Semantic retrieval captures conceptual similarity across paraphrases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this retrieval strategy selection situation? A corpus contains product codes plus natural-language explanations. What strategy often provides robust coverage?","Hybrid lexical and semantic retrieval. Both exact terminology and conceptual similarity matter."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Lexical retrieval — D3.6 application","Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Lexical retrieval — rule application in retrieval strategy selection","Phrase that completes this retrieval strategy selection rule: Exact identifiers and error strings are often strong candidates for _____."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In retrieval strategy selection, {{c1::Lexical retrieval}} is the concept described as: Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25.","Applied reinforcement for D3.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For retrieval strategy selection, the precise answer to “What retrieval approach combines lexical and semantic signals?” is {{c1::Hybrid retrieval}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["During an operational review, apply this retrieval strategy selection rule: In retrieval strategy selection, {{c1::Lexical retrieval}} is the concept described as: Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25.","Applied reinforcement for D3.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within retrieval strategy selection, what term matches this definition: Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25.","Lexical retrieval"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved retrieval strategy selection rule? Exact identifiers and error strings are often strong candidates for _____.","lexical retrieval"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A user searches for exact error code ERR-9F21. Which retrieval signal should be strongly represented? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Semantic similarity only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Random chunk selection.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Conversation memory only.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Lexical/exact-term retrieval such as BM25.\"}]","a","Exact identifiers benefit from lexical matching. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved retrieval strategy selection guidance to this case: Users ask policy questions with wording very different from the source text. Which retrieval method helps most?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Sorting documents alphabetically.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Using only document timestamps.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Semantic embedding retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Exact keyword matching only.\"}]","a","Semantic retrieval captures conceptual similarity across paraphrases. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A corpus contains product codes plus natural-language explanations. What strategy often provides robust coverage?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No retrieval; preload the entire corpus.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Hybrid lexical and semantic retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Semantic retrieval with no exact matching.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Lexical search with no semantic signal.\"}]","a","Both exact terminology and conceptual similarity matter. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a retrieval strategy selection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support retrieval strategy selection?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume a stale index is authoritative for current balances.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Match retrieval strategy to query/data shape.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use embeddings for every exact-ID lookup.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Match retrieval strategy to query/data shape.; Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on retrieval strategy selection? Context: An architect is reviewing retrieval strategy selection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore access/freshness metadata.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only keyword search for heavily paraphrased questions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use semantic signals for paraphrases.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.; Use semantic signals for paraphrases.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? One internal service exposes a single private function to one application. No other AI client needs it. What is the simplest integration?","A direct API/SDK or internal function boundary. A reusable protocol layer should earn its complexity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for integration mechanism selection: Several compatible AI clients need to discover and call the same enterprise tools through a standard interface. What is a strong fit?","MCP. MCP is designed for standardized capability exposure and discovery."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this integration mechanism selection situation? A team exposes a destructive MCP tool and assumes MCP makes it safe. What is wrong?","MCP does not replace authorization, validation, least privilege, or source-system controls. Protocol standardization is distinct from security policy."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["MCP — D3.7 application","A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["standardized interoperability and capability discovery — D3.7 application","Phrase that completes this integration mechanism selection rule: Choose MCP for useful _____, not merely because Claude is involved."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In integration mechanism selection, {{c1::MCP}} is the concept described as: A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers.","Applied reinforcement for D3.7."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For integration mechanism selection, the precise answer to “What protocol standardizes reusable tool/resource surfaces for compatible AI clients?” is {{c1::MCP}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.7."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["During an operational review, apply this integration mechanism selection rule: In integration mechanism selection, {{c1::MCP}} is the concept described as: A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers.","Applied reinforcement for D3.7."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within integration mechanism selection, what term matches this definition: A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers.","MCP"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved integration mechanism selection rule? Choose MCP for useful _____, not merely because Claude is involved.","standardized interoperability and capability discovery"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: One internal service exposes a single private function to one application. No other AI client needs it. What is the simplest integration? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"MCP is mandatory for every Claude integration.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Agent-to-agent protocol is required.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A multi-agent runtime must wrap it.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A direct API/SDK or internal function boundary.\"}]","a","A reusable protocol layer should earn its complexity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved integration mechanism selection guidance to this case: Several compatible AI clients need to discover and call the same enterprise tools through a standard interface. What is a strong fit?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Conversation memory.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A vector database with no tool protocol.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A different bespoke private API per client only.\"}]","a","MCP is designed for standardized capability exposure and discovery. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A team exposes a destructive MCP tool and assumes MCP makes it safe. What is wrong?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"MCP removes the need for identity.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"MCP does not replace authorization, validation, least privilege, or source-system controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"MCP automatically denies all writes.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"MCP tools cannot be destructive.\"}]","a","Protocol standardization is distinct from security policy. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a integration mechanism selection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support integration mechanism selection?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Wrap every private function in MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use direct APIs for narrow privately owned integrations when sufficient.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose MCP simply because Claude is present.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use direct APIs for narrow privately owned integrations when sufficient.; Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.7."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on integration mechanism selection? Context: An architect is reviewing integration mechanism selection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use agent-to-agent when a normal function/tool boundary suffices.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume MCP tools are automatically secure.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep authorization separate from protocol choice.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.; Keep authorization separate from protocol choice.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.7."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? An enterprise has hundreds of rarely used MCP tools and only a few are relevant per request. What architecture best reduces context overhead?","Keep common tools available and discover/load long-tail tools on demand. Progressive discovery targets context bloat and tool-selection ambiguity."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for progressive discovery versus monolithic context: A system has five simple tools used on nearly every request. What is a reasonable choice?","Loading the small catalog directly may be simpler than adding a discovery layer. Discovery adds complexity and should be justified by catalog/context needs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this progressive discovery versus monolithic context situation? A tool is not loaded into the current model context. Can the system assume the user is unauthorized to use it?","No. Discovery/visibility and authorization are separate controls. Authorization must be enforced independently of what definitions are currently visible."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Progressive discovery — D3.8 application","Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["selection confusion — D3.8 application","Phrase that completes this progressive discovery versus monolithic context rule: Large tool catalogs can create both context overhead and _____."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In progressive discovery versus monolithic context, {{c1::Progressive discovery}} is the concept described as: Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog.","Applied reinforcement for D3.8."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For progressive discovery versus monolithic context, the precise answer to “What strategy loads long-tail tool definitions only when they become relevant?” is {{c1::Progressive discovery}}.","Applied reinforcement for D3.8."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["During an operational review, apply this progressive discovery versus monolithic context rule: In progressive discovery versus monolithic context, {{c1::Progressive discovery}} is the concept described as: Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog.","Applied reinforcement for D3.8."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within progressive discovery versus monolithic context, what term matches this definition: Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog.","Progressive discovery"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved progressive discovery versus monolithic context rule? Large tool catalogs can create both context overhead and _____.","selection confusion"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An enterprise has hundreds of rarely used MCP tools and only a few are relevant per request. What architecture best reduces context overhead? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Load every tool definition on every request.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove authorization because hidden tools are safe.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Duplicate every tool description in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep common tools available and discover/load long-tail tools on demand.\"}]","a","Progressive discovery targets context bloat and tool-selection ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved progressive discovery versus monolithic context guidance to this case: A system has five simple tools used on nearly every request. What is a reasonable choice?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Split each tool into ten more tools.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide all tools until after generation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Loading the small catalog directly may be simpler than adding a discovery layer.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Progressive discovery is mandatory regardless of catalog size.\"}]","a","Discovery adds complexity and should be justified by catalog/context needs. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A tool is not loaded into the current model context. Can the system assume the user is unauthorized to use it?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only if the model says so.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"No. Discovery/visibility and authorization are separate controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Yes, hidden tools are automatically forbidden.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Yes, context visibility is the authorization policy.\"}]","a","Authorization must be enforced independently of what definitions are currently visible. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a progressive discovery versus monolithic context review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support progressive discovery versus monolithic context?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Build discovery complexity for a tiny stable catalog without benefit.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Load long-tail tools only when relevant.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Load hundreds of definitions on every request.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Load long-tail tools only when relevant.; Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.8."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on progressive discovery versus monolithic context? Context: An architect is reviewing progressive discovery versus monolithic context. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use discovery instead of access control.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat hidden-from-context as unauthorized.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use discovery to reduce context and selection burden.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.; Use discovery to reduce context and selection burden.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.8."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a protected agent action flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the user\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted auth context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Authorize the specific protected action\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute with scoped credentials and record the result\"}]","Identity is established before proposal; authorization gates execution. Sequence reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a latency-optimization investigation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Measure end-to-end latency by stage\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Identify the dominant contributor\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Form a change hypothesis\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Measure quality/latency after the change\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Keep the change only if thresholds still pass\"}]","Optimization starts with measurement and must preserve required quality/safety. Sequence reinforcement for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a trace-based incident investigation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Start from the failing request/trace ID\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Inspect model/retrieval/tool trajectory\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare claimed action with external outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Identify the failing stage\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Fix and add a regression check\"}]","Correlated evidence narrows the failure before remediation. Sequence reinforcement for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a basic RAG pipeline.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Ingest and parse source content\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Chunk and enrich/index the content\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Retrieve candidates for a query\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Filter/rerank and assemble relevant context\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Generate the answer from the selected context\"}]","RAG prepares indexed units first, then retrieves and assembles evidence at inference time. Sequence reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a retrieval-debugging check when a RAG answer is wrong.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Check whether the needed source exists in the corpus\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Check whether the right chunk was created/indexed\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Check whether retrieval returned it\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Check whether ranking/context assembly kept it\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Then inspect generation behavior\"}]","Debug retrieval upstream before blaming generation. Sequence reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A team says its support agent is “very accurate.” What should an architect request next?","A defined metric, representative measurement method, and acceptance threshold. Evaluation claims must be operationalized."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for defining evaluation metrics: A candidate model improves task success but doubles safety-policy violations. What should the team conclude?","The candidate fails a critical guardrail even if the primary quality metric improved. Safety/security floors can constrain optimization."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this defining evaluation metrics situation? A coding agent says it fixed a bug, but tests still fail. What is the stronger evaluation metric?","The external task outcome, such as passing the relevant tests. External outcome can be more authoritative than model claims."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Which metric best represents user-facing responsiveness when occasional slow requests matter?","A tail-latency percentile such as p95, paired with an SLA threshold. Tail latency matters when a minority of very slow requests harm the experience."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Outcome metric — D4.1 application","A measure of whether the task produced the desired real-world result."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Guardrail metric — D4.1 application","A secondary threshold that must not regress while optimizing a primary metric."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["acceptance threshold — D4.1 application","Phrase that completes this defining evaluation metrics rule: A useful metric needs a definition, a measurement method, and an _____."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In defining evaluation metrics, {{c1::Outcome metric}} is the concept described as: A measure of whether the task produced the desired real-world result.","Applied reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In defining evaluation metrics, {{c1::Guardrail metric}} is the concept described as: A secondary threshold that must not regress while optimizing a primary metric.","Applied reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For defining evaluation metrics, the precise answer to “What term describes a threshold metric that must not regress during optimization?” is {{c1::Guardrail metric}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For defining evaluation metrics, the precise answer to “What should define the minimum acceptable value for a metric?” is {{c1::Acceptance threshold}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within defining evaluation metrics, what term matches this definition: A measure of whether the task produced the desired real-world result.","Outcome metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within defining evaluation metrics, what term matches this definition: A secondary threshold that must not regress while optimizing a primary metric.","Guardrail metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved defining evaluation metrics rule? A useful metric needs a definition, a measurement method, and an _____.","acceptance threshold"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team says its support agent is “very accurate.” What should an architect request next? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A longer system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A larger context window.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"More agents.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A defined metric, representative measurement method, and acceptance threshold.\"}]","a","Evaluation claims must be operationalized. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved defining evaluation metrics guidance to this case: A candidate model improves task success but doubles safety-policy violations. What should the team conclude?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore safety because it is hard to score.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Average the two metrics into one number and accept any positive result.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The candidate fails a critical guardrail even if the primary quality metric improved.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ship it because primary accuracy is higher.\"}]","a","Safety/security floors can constrain optimization. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A coding agent says it fixed a bug, but tests still fail. What is the stronger evaluation metric?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Number of tool calls.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The external task outcome, such as passing the relevant tests.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"The agent's confidence.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Length of the explanation.\"}]","a","External outcome can be more authoritative than model claims. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Which metric best represents user-facing responsiveness when occasional slow requests matter? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A tail-latency percentile such as p95, paired with an SLA threshold.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only average latency.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Total tokens ever used.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Number of prompt lines.\"}]","a","Tail latency matters when a minority of very slow requests harm the experience. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a defining evaluation metrics review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support defining evaluation metrics?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Measure external outcomes where possible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore tail behavior.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define measurable thresholds before evaluation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use one vague “accuracy” number for everything.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define measurable thresholds before evaluation.; Measure external outcomes where possible.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on defining evaluation metrics? Context: An architect is reviewing defining evaluation metrics. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Declare success without a threshold.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure external outcomes where possible.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize only the easiest metric.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure external outcomes where possible.; Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For defining evaluation metrics, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in defining evaluation metrics?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore tail behavior.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep safety/security guardrails alongside quality.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Trust model self-reports over authoritative outcomes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use multiple metrics for multi-dimensional success.; Keep safety/security guardrails alongside quality.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A tool action should create exactly one database row. What is the best grader?","A deterministic check of the database state. Exact external state should be verified deterministically."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for evaluation datasets and frameworks: A style rubric is nuanced and cannot be checked with simple code. What grader may be appropriate after calibration?","A model-based grader evaluated against human-labeled examples. Model graders can score nuanced qualities but should be calibrated."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this evaluation datasets and frameworks situation? An eval suite contains only easy happy-path requests. What is the biggest weakness?","It may miss boundary, adversarial, malformed, and historical failure modes. Representative coverage includes important failures, not just routine cases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: An agent's performance varies significantly between runs of the same task. What should the eval framework add?","Multiple trials per task to measure reliability under stochastic behavior. Repeated trials characterize variance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trial — D4.2 application","One execution of an evaluation task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Grader — D4.2 application","The mechanism that scores whether a task/run met defined criteria."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["cheapest reliable grader — D4.2 application","Phrase that completes this evaluation datasets and frameworks rule: Use the _____ that can accurately measure the property of interest."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In evaluation datasets and frameworks, {{c1::Trial}} is the concept described as: One execution of an evaluation task.","Applied reinforcement for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In evaluation datasets and frameworks, {{c1::Grader}} is the concept described as: The mechanism that scores whether a task/run met defined criteria.","Applied reinforcement for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For evaluation datasets and frameworks, the precise answer to “What evaluation component scores a task result?” is {{c1::Grader}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For evaluation datasets and frameworks, the precise answer to “What term describes one execution of an eval task?” is {{c1::Trial}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within evaluation datasets and frameworks, what term matches this definition: One execution of an evaluation task.","Trial"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within evaluation datasets and frameworks, what term matches this definition: The mechanism that scores whether a task/run met defined criteria.","Grader"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved evaluation datasets and frameworks rule? Use the _____ that can accurately measure the property of interest.","cheapest reliable grader"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A tool action should create exactly one database row. What is the best grader? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"An LLM judge reading the agent's explanation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A human reviewer for every run.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"The model's self-reported success.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A deterministic check of the database state.\"}]","a","Exact external state should be verified deterministically. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved evaluation datasets and frameworks guidance to this case: A style rubric is nuanced and cannot be checked with simple code. What grader may be appropriate after calibration?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A random score.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No grader at all.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A model-based grader evaluated against human-labeled examples.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A schema validator only.\"}]","a","Model graders can score nuanced qualities but should be calibrated. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? An eval suite contains only easy happy-path requests. What is the biggest weakness?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"It should never include production failures.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"It may miss boundary, adversarial, malformed, and historical failure modes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"It contains too many tasks.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"It should use only one trial.\"}]","a","Representative coverage includes important failures, not just routine cases. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An agent's performance varies significantly between runs of the same task. What should the eval framework add? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Multiple trials per task to measure reliability under stochastic behavior.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One carefully chosen run only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A longer deck name.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fewer measurements.\"}]","a","Repeated trials characterize variance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a evaluation datasets and frameworks review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support evaluation datasets and frameworks?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use deterministic graders for exact properties.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only happy-path data.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Include representative and difficult cases.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Evaluate only final prose.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Include representative and difficult cases.; Use deterministic graders for exact properties.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on evaluation datasets and frameworks? Context: An architect is reviewing evaluation datasets and frameworks. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume one stochastic trial is definitive.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use deterministic graders for exact properties.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM judge when code can verify exactly.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Calibrate model graders.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use deterministic graders for exact properties.; Calibrate model graders.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For evaluation datasets and frameworks, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in evaluation datasets and frameworks?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Calibrate model graders.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only happy-path data.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Inspect external outcomes for agent actions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Overfit the system to a tiny static eval set.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Calibrate model graders.; Inspect external outcomes for agent actions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A team changes the model, prompt, retriever, and tool schema simultaneously, then sees improvement. What is the main problem?","The experiment cannot attribute the change because several major variables moved together. Controlled experiments isolate specific hypotheses."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for A/B testing and iterative improvement: A new agent can execute risky production writes. How can the team first test it on realistic traffic without exposing users to its actions?","Use shadow testing with outputs/actions prevented from affecting production. Shadow testing provides realistic input without direct production effect."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this A/B testing and iterative improvement situation? A treatment improves accuracy by 0.05% with strong statistical significance but adds major cost. What should the architect consider?","Whether the improvement is practically valuable enough to justify the cost. Practical significance and guardrails matter."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: An experiment's primary quality metric rises while latency breaches the SLA. What should happen?","Treat the latency SLA as a guardrail and reject or revise the treatment. Guardrails prevent one metric from improving by violating another requirement."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Control — D4.3 application","The baseline experience/system in a controlled experiment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Treatment — D4.3 application","The candidate change being tested against the control."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In A/B testing and iterative improvement, {{c1::Control}} is the concept described as: The baseline experience/system in a controlled experiment.","Applied reinforcement for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In A/B testing and iterative improvement, {{c1::Treatment}} is the concept described as: The candidate change being tested against the control.","Applied reinforcement for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For A/B testing and iterative improvement, the precise answer to “What experiment mode runs a candidate on real traffic without exposing users to its outputs?” is {{c1::Shadow testing}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For A/B testing and iterative improvement, the precise answer to “What is the baseline arm of an A/B experiment called?” is {{c1::Control}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within A/B testing and iterative improvement, what term matches this definition: The baseline experience/system in a controlled experiment.","Control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within A/B testing and iterative improvement, what term matches this definition: The candidate change being tested against the control.","Treatment"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved A/B testing and iterative improvement rule? An A/B experiment should define the hypothesis, primary metric, guardrails, assignment, and _____ before interpreting results.","decision/stopping rule"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team changes the model, prompt, retriever, and tool schema simultaneously, then sees improvement. What is the main problem? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A/B testing requires more than two models.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"All variables should always change together.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Guardrail metrics are unnecessary.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The experiment cannot attribute the change because several major variables moved together.\"}]","a","Controlled experiments isolate specific hypotheses. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved A/B testing and iterative improvement guidance to this case: A new agent can execute risky production writes. How can the team first test it on realistic traffic without exposing users to its actions?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Disable logging.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only a synthetic prompt unrelated to production.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use shadow testing with outputs/actions prevented from affecting production.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Turn it on for every user immediately.\"}]","a","Shadow testing provides realistic input without direct production effect. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A treatment improves accuracy by 0.05% with strong statistical significance but adds major cost. What should the architect consider?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Always ship any measurable improvement.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the improvement is practically valuable enough to justify the cost.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Statistical significance guarantees business value.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore cost once p<0.05.\"}]","a","Practical significance and guardrails matter. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An experiment's primary quality metric rises while latency breaches the SLA. What should happen? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Treat the latency SLA as a guardrail and reject or revise the treatment.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ship because primary quality improved.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove the SLA from reporting.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Average quality and latency into one unbounded score.\"}]","a","Guardrails prevent one metric from improving by violating another requirement. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a A/B testing and iterative improvement review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support A/B testing and iterative improvement?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define primary and guardrail metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore latency/cost after quality improves.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"State the hypothesis before running the experiment.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Change many major variables at once.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: State the hypothesis before running the experiment.; Define primary and guardrail metrics.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on A/B testing and iterative improvement? Context: An architect is reviewing A/B testing and iterative improvement. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Live-test risky irreversible actions unnecessarily.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define primary and guardrail metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Look at metrics until something becomes significant.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define primary and guardrail metrics.; Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For A/B testing and iterative improvement, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in A/B testing and iterative improvement?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore latency/cost after quality improves.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use shadow testing for risky candidates.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Define success criteria after seeing results.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use consistent assignment where cross-exposure would confound results.; Use shadow testing for risky candidates.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A model gives wrong answers because the retriever returns obsolete documents. What should change first?","Fix the retrieval freshness/ranking problem. The failing layer is retrieval, not necessarily prompting."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for diagnosing AI system failures: A tool returns malformed JSON and the agent fails. What is the most direct diagnosis?","Tool/interface contract failure. Inspect the interface actually producing the malformed data."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this diagnosing AI system failures situation? A worker computes the correct result, but the orchestrator drops it before synthesis. What failure class is this?","Orchestration failure. The component result is correct; coordination is wrong."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: After repairing a recurrent production failure, what should the team add?","A regression test/eval reproducing the failure so it stays fixed. Known failures should become protected regression cases."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Retrieval failure — D4.4 application","The relevant evidence is not retrieved or is outranked by wrong evidence."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Orchestration failure — D4.4 application","Correct components are coordinated incorrectly, such as dropped worker results or wrong ordering."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In diagnosing AI system failures, {{c1::Retrieval failure}} is the concept described as: The relevant evidence is not retrieved or is outranked by wrong evidence.","Applied reinforcement for D4.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In diagnosing AI system failures, {{c1::Orchestration failure}} is the concept described as: Correct components are coordinated incorrectly, such as dropped worker results or wrong ordering.","Applied reinforcement for D4.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For diagnosing AI system failures, the precise answer to “What failure class occurs when relevant evidence never reaches the model?” is {{c1::Retrieval failure}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within diagnosing AI system failures, what term matches this definition: The relevant evidence is not retrieved or is outranked by wrong evidence.","Retrieval failure"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within diagnosing AI system failures, what term matches this definition: Correct components are coordinated incorrectly, such as dropped worker results or wrong ordering.","Orchestration failure"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A model gives wrong answers because the retriever returns obsolete documents. What should change first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more system-prompt warnings.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Upgrade the model without inspecting retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry the same stale evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Fix the retrieval freshness/ranking problem.\"}]","a","The failing layer is retrieval, not necessarily prompting. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved diagnosing AI system failures guidance to this case: A tool returns malformed JSON and the agent fails. What is the most direct diagnosis?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model lifecycle failure.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Business-value failure.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Tool/interface contract failure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Hallucination by definition.\"}]","a","Inspect the interface actually producing the malformed data. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A worker computes the correct result, but the orchestrator drops it before synthesis. What failure class is this?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Model deprecation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Orchestration failure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Retrieval failure.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Prompt injection.\"}]","a","The component result is correct; coordination is wrong. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a diagnosing AI system failures review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support diagnosing AI system failures?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Inspect traces and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Upgrade the model to fix a broken API contract.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reproduce the symptom.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Call every wrong answer a hallucination.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reproduce the symptom.; Inspect traces and external outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on diagnosing AI system failures? Context: An architect is reviewing diagnosing AI system failures. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry authorization failures blindly.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Inspect traces and external outcomes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Rewrite prompts when retrieval is stale.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify the specific failing layer.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Inspect traces and external outcomes.; Identify the specific failing layer.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For diagnosing AI system failures, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in diagnosing AI system failures?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identify the specific failing layer.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Upgrade the model to fix a broken API contract.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use targeted tests to validate the hypothesis.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fix production bugs without regression coverage.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Identify the specific failing layer.; Use targeted tests to validate the hypothesis.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A cheaper model causes twice as many retries and escalations. What metric should decide whether it is actually cheaper?","Cost per successful outcome including retries/escalations. A cheap failing request can raise total cost."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance: Tool results contain 100,000 rows but the model needs only an aggregate. What is a strong optimization?","Process/filter the data programmatically and pass only the high-signal result to the model. Programmatic processing reduces token/context overhead."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance situation? A prompt includes large historical logs that never affect decisions. What should the team test?","Remove or compact low-value context and confirm quality still passes. Low-value context wastes tokens and may harm relevance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: An optimization removes a safety validation step and lowers p95 latency. Is it acceptable?","Only if the validation was not required; required safety controls must remain even when they cost latency. Optimization is constrained by required safety/security thresholds."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Cost per successful outcome — D4.5 application","Total resource cost divided by tasks that actually meet the success criteria."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Prompt caching — D4.5 application","Reusing eligible stable prompt/context content rather than recomputing/sending it as uncached work each time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance, {{c1::Cost per successful outcome}} is the concept described as: Total resource cost divided by tasks that actually meet the success criteria.","Applied reinforcement for D4.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance, {{c1::Prompt caching}} is the concept described as: Reusing eligible stable prompt/context content rather than recomputing/sending it as uncached work each time.","Applied reinforcement for D4.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance, the precise answer to “What efficiency metric accounts for failures/retries rather than only request price?” is {{c1::Cost per successful outcome}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance, what term matches this definition: Total resource cost divided by tasks that actually meet the success criteria.","Cost per successful outcome"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance, what term matches this definition: Reusing eligible stable prompt/context content rather than recomputing/sending it as uncached work each time.","Prompt caching"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A cheaper model causes twice as many retries and escalations. What metric should decide whether it is actually cheaper? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Price per single API call only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model name length.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Prompt token count alone.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Cost per successful outcome including retries/escalations.\"}]","a","A cheap failing request can raise total cost. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance guidance to this case: Tool results contain 100,000 rows but the model needs only an aggregate. What is a strong optimization?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the rows in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable the tool.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Process/filter the data programmatically and pass only the high-signal result to the model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Send every row through multiple model turns.\"}]","a","Programmatic processing reduces token/context overhead. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A prompt includes large historical logs that never affect decisions. What should the team test?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the strongest model only.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Remove or compact low-value context and confirm quality still passes.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more logs to improve cost.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase output length.\"}]","a","Low-value context wastes tokens and may harm relevance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Reduce irrelevant context.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume the cheapest model is cheapest end to end.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure cost per successful outcome.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize cost per request regardless of failures.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure cost per successful outcome.; Reduce irrelevant context.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance? Context: An architect is reviewing optimizing token, latency, and cost-performance. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add caches without freshness policy.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reduce irrelevant context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Remove required safety checks for speed.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use programmatic processing for large intermediate data.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reduce irrelevant context.; Use programmatic processing for large intermediate data.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? Offline evals pass, but tool failures spike after launch because an external API changed. What caught this?","Production monitoring of real dependencies and outcomes. Production monitoring detects real-world changes offline suites may not predict."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for production monitoring and regression protection: A new model version is deployed. What should protect known behavior?","Run the regression suite and monitor production after migration. Model changes can alter behavior and require regression testing."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this production monitoring and regression protection situation? Users report a novel failure pattern. What should happen after root cause is fixed?","Add representative cases to the regression suite and monitor the corrected behavior. Production failures improve future evaluation coverage."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Capability eval — D4.6 application","An evaluation asking whether the system can perform a new or harder capability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["real workload or dependencies — D4.6 application","Phrase that completes this production monitoring and regression protection rule: Production monitoring reveals whether the _____ are drifting from assumptions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In production monitoring and regression protection, {{c1::Capability eval}} is the concept described as: An evaluation asking whether the system can perform a new or harder capability.","Applied reinforcement for D4.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For production monitoring and regression protection, the precise answer to “What evaluation protects known-good behavior from breaking after changes?” is {{c1::Regression evaluation}}.","Applied reinforcement for D4.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["During an operational review, apply this production monitoring and regression protection rule: In production monitoring and regression protection, {{c1::Capability eval}} is the concept described as: An evaluation asking whether the system can perform a new or harder capability.","Applied reinforcement for D4.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within production monitoring and regression protection, what term matches this definition: An evaluation asking whether the system can perform a new or harder capability.","Capability eval"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved production monitoring and regression protection rule? Production monitoring reveals whether the _____ are drifting from assumptions.","real workload or dependencies"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Offline evals pass, but tool failures spike after launch because an external API changed. What caught this? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A static benchmark alone.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A one-time prelaunch demo.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Production monitoring of real dependencies and outcomes.\"}]","a","Production monitoring detects real-world changes offline suites may not predict. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved production monitoring and regression protection guidance to this case: A new model version is deployed. What should protect known behavior?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Delete old evals.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only compare price.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run the regression suite and monitor production after migration.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume newer means identical.\"}]","a","Model changes can alter behavior and require regression testing. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Users report a novel failure pattern. What should happen after root cause is fixed?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only increase model temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add representative cases to the regression suite and monitor the corrected behavior.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore it because launch evals already passed.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove the complaint from logs.\"}]","a","Production failures improve future evaluation coverage. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a production monitoring and regression protection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support production monitoring and regression protection?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Protect known behavior with regression evals.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Deploy model changes without regression tests.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Monitor real outcomes and dependencies.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Monitor infrastructure uptime only.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Monitor real outcomes and dependencies.; Protect known behavior with regression evals.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on production monitoring and regression protection? Context: An architect is reviewing production monitoring and regression protection. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Create alerts with no owner.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Protect known behavior with regression evals.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep eval suites frozen forever.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Test model/version migrations.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Protect known behavior with regression evals.; Test model/version migrations.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D4.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.6\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a metric-definition workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the desired outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Choose observable measures\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Specify how each measure is computed\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Set acceptance and guardrail thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Run representative evaluation and compare to thresholds\"}]","Metrics become useful only after outcome, measurement, and thresholds are explicit. Sequence reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a basic evaluation-framework design.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define representative tasks\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Choose appropriate graders\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run one or more trials\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Collect trajectories/outcomes\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Aggregate results against thresholds\"}]","Task definition and grading come before execution and aggregation. Sequence reinforcement for D4.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a controlled improvement experiment.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"State the hypothesis\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Choose primary and guardrail metrics\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Define assignment and decision rule\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Run control/treatment or shadow evaluation\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Analyze results and decide whether to ship\"}]","Pre-specification precedes execution and interpretation. Sequence reinforcement for D4.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a root-cause diagnostic loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Reproduce the symptom\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Inspect trace/outcome evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify the likely failing stage\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Run a targeted isolation test\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Apply the fix and add regression coverage\"}]","Evidence-driven isolation precedes remediation. Sequence reinforcement for D4.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A refund tool can transfer money. The system prompt says “never refund more than $500,” but the API accepts any amount. What is the strongest improvement?","Enforce the limit in deterministic transaction/authorization logic before execution. Hard financial limits belong at the execution boundary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for guardrails and safety controls: A required authorization service is unavailable during a high-risk transaction. What is usually safest?","Block or defer the action until authorization can be verified. High-risk controls commonly fail closed."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this guardrails and safety controls situation? An agent reads untrusted web content and can also modify production systems. Which safety posture is strongest?","Layer prompt-injection defenses with scoped tools, sandboxing/permissions, authorization, and approval where needed. No single prompt-level defense is sufficient."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: An output moderation check runs only after an irreversible transfer has already executed. What is wrong?","The control is placed after the point where it could prevent the harmful action. Controls must sit at boundaries where they can enforce the property."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Defense in depth — D5.1 application","Using multiple independent layers so failure of one control does not remove all protection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Fail closed — D5.1 application","Block the protected action when a required safety or authorization check cannot complete."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["controls at the relevant system boundary — D5.1 application","Phrase that completes this guardrails and safety controls rule: Hard safety properties should be enforced by _____, not only by prompt text."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In guardrails and safety controls, {{c1::Defense in depth}} is the concept described as: Using multiple independent layers so failure of one control does not remove all protection.","Applied reinforcement for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In guardrails and safety controls, {{c1::Fail closed}} is the concept described as: Block the protected action when a required safety or authorization check cannot complete.","Applied reinforcement for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For guardrails and safety controls, the precise answer to “What security design uses several independent protective layers?” is {{c1::Defense in depth}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For guardrails and safety controls, the precise answer to “What failure behavior blocks an action when a required control cannot verify it?” is {{c1::Fail closed}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within guardrails and safety controls, what term matches this definition: Using multiple independent layers so failure of one control does not remove all protection.","Defense in depth"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within guardrails and safety controls, what term matches this definition: Block the protected action when a required safety or authorization check cannot complete.","Fail closed"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved guardrails and safety controls rule? Hard safety properties should be enforced by _____, not only by prompt text.","controls at the relevant system boundary"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A refund tool can transfer money. The system prompt says “never refund more than $500,” but the API accepts any amount. What is the strongest improvement? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Repeat the warning five times in the prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use a more persuasive role description.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Log over-$500 refunds after they happen.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Enforce the limit in deterministic transaction/authorization logic before execution.\"}]","a","Hard financial limits belong at the execution boundary. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved guardrails and safety controls guidance to this case: A required authorization service is unavailable during a high-risk transaction. What is usually safest?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ask the model to guess authorization.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable the authorization layer permanently.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Block or defer the action until authorization can be verified.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Allow the action and audit later.\"}]","a","High-risk controls commonly fail closed. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? An agent reads untrusted web content and can also modify production systems. Which safety posture is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give broader tools so the agent can recover from mistakes.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Layer prompt-injection defenses with scoped tools, sandboxing/permissions, authorization, and approval where needed.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use only a stronger system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Trust the web page because the agent fetched it.\"}]","a","No single prompt-level defense is sufficient. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An output moderation check runs only after an irreversible transfer has already executed. What is wrong? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The control is placed after the point where it could prevent the harmful action.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Moderation should always occur after side effects.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The model should have more tokens.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Transfers should never be logged.\"}]","a","Controls must sit at boundaries where they can enforce the property. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a guardrails and safety controls review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support guardrails and safety controls?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give admin tools and rely on instructions not to misuse them.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use layered independent controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use one giant safety prompt as the only protection.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use layered independent controls.; Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on guardrails and safety controls? Context: An architect is reviewing guardrails and safety controls. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Moderate only after irreversible actions.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log dangerous actions instead of preventing them.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Scope tools and permissions.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Put hard authorization at the protected action boundary.; Scope tools and permissions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For guardrails and safety controls, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in guardrails and safety controls?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Scope tools and permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give admin tools and rely on instructions not to misuse them.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use human approval for sufficiently consequential actions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat model refusal behavior as deterministic authorization.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Scope tools and permissions.; Use human approval for sufficiently consequential actions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A web page contains hidden text telling the browsing agent to upload secrets to an attacker. What failure mode is this?","Indirect prompt injection. The malicious instruction is delivered through external content."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes: An agent has production write access even though its task is read-only analysis. Which risk is most direct?","Excessive agency / unnecessary capability. Permissions exceed what the task requires."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes situation? An agent loops through tools for hours and consumes a large budget. Which controls are most relevant?","Iteration/token/cost budgets, timeouts, rate limits, and stopping conditions. Resource exhaustion needs enforceable execution limits."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A third-party MCP server is compromised. What architecture most limits damage?","Provenance/review plus sandboxing, least privilege, scoped credentials, and monitored boundaries. Tool/supply-chain risk requires constrained trust."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Indirect prompt injection — D5.2 application","Adversarial instructions hidden in external content such as pages, documents, email, or tool results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Excessive agency — D5.2 application","More autonomy or capability than is necessary for the intended task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["untrusted — D5.2 application","Phrase that completes this LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes rule: External content consumed by an agent should be treated as _____ because it may contain indirect prompt injection."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, {{c1::Indirect prompt injection}} is the concept described as: Adversarial instructions hidden in external content such as pages, documents, email, or tool results.","Applied reinforcement for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, {{c1::Excessive agency}} is the concept described as: More autonomy or capability than is necessary for the intended task.","Applied reinforcement for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, the precise answer to “What attack embeds malicious instructions in content the agent reads?” is {{c1::Indirect prompt injection}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, the precise answer to “What risk describes granting an agent more autonomy or permissions than required?” is {{c1::Excessive agency}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, what term matches this definition: Adversarial instructions hidden in external content such as pages, documents, email, or tool results.","Indirect prompt injection"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, what term matches this definition: More autonomy or capability than is necessary for the intended task.","Excessive agency"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes rule? External content consumed by an agent should be treated as _____ because it may contain indirect prompt injection.","untrusted"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A web page contains hidden text telling the browsing agent to upload secrets to an attacker. What failure mode is this? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Model deprecation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ordinary lexical retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A/B contamination.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Indirect prompt injection.\"}]","a","The malicious instruction is delivered through external content. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes guidance to this case: An agent has production write access even though its task is read-only analysis. Which risk is most direct?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Prompt caching.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Underfitting a grader.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Excessive agency / unnecessary capability.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Insufficient context length.\"}]","a","Permissions exceed what the task requires. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? An agent loops through tools for hours and consumes a large budget. Which controls are most relevant?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disabling monitoring.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Iteration/token/cost budgets, timeouts, rate limits, and stopping conditions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only a friendlier system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More write permissions.\"}]","a","Resource exhaustion needs enforceable execution limits. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A third-party MCP server is compromised. What architecture most limits damage? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provenance/review plus sandboxing, least privilege, scoped credentials, and monitored boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust all MCP servers because the protocol is standard.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give the server broader credentials to simplify failures.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove version pinning and review.\"}]","a","Tool/supply-chain risk requires constrained trust. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Minimize capability and secret exposure.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give agents secrets they never need.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Treat external content as untrusted.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume a better model eliminates prompt injection.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Treat external content as untrusted.; Minimize capability and secret exposure.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes? Context: An architect is reviewing LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Trust third-party tools solely because they use MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Minimize capability and secret exposure.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Call every wrong answer a hallucination.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Minimize capability and secret exposure.; Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in LLM and agent risks, limitations, and failure modes?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give agents secrets they never need.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Review third-party tools/Skills and provenance.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Allow unbounded loops and spending.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use budgets/timeouts for runaway execution.; Review third-party tools/Skills and provenance.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? An AI proposes a large irreversible wire transfer. Which review pattern is strongest?","Human approval before the transfer executes. High-consequence irreversible actions favor pre-action approval."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for human-in-the-loop validation: A mature low-risk classification workflow needs ongoing quality oversight without reviewing every case. What fits?","Sampled human review combined with monitoring. Sampling can monitor a mature lower-risk process without erasing automation value."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this human-in-the-loop validation situation? A reviewer sees only “Approve? yes/no” with no source evidence or policy. What is the main weakness?","The human cannot exercise meaningful judgment and may become a rubber stamp. HITL must provide enough context for a real decision."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A reversible low-impact content tag is wrong occasionally. Which oversight approach may be proportionate?","Post-action or sampled review with monitoring, if risk is acceptable. Oversight should be proportionate to consequence and reversibility."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Pre-action approval — D5.3 application","Human authorization before a consequential action occurs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Sampled review — D5.3 application","Reviewing a subset of lower-risk cases to monitor quality and drift."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In human-in-the-loop validation, {{c1::Pre-action approval}} is the concept described as: Human authorization before a consequential action occurs.","Applied reinforcement for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In human-in-the-loop validation, {{c1::Sampled review}} is the concept described as: Reviewing a subset of lower-risk cases to monitor quality and drift.","Applied reinforcement for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For human-in-the-loop validation, the precise answer to “What review pattern requires human authorization before execution?” is {{c1::Pre-action approval}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For human-in-the-loop validation, the precise answer to “What review pattern checks only a fraction of lower-risk cases?” is {{c1::Sampled review}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within human-in-the-loop validation, what term matches this definition: Human authorization before a consequential action occurs.","Pre-action approval"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within human-in-the-loop validation, what term matches this definition: Reviewing a subset of lower-risk cases to monitor quality and drift.","Sampled review"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An AI proposes a large irreversible wire transfer. Which review pattern is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Review the transfer a week later.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Sample 1% after execution only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Let model confidence determine authorization.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Human approval before the transfer executes.\"}]","a","High-consequence irreversible actions favor pre-action approval. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved human-in-the-loop validation guidance to this case: A mature low-risk classification workflow needs ongoing quality oversight without reviewing every case. What fits?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove all human oversight permanently.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Review only when the model says it is confident.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Sampled human review combined with monitoring.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Pre-approve every single low-risk label.\"}]","a","Sampling can monitor a mature lower-risk process without erasing automation value. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A reviewer sees only “Approve? yes/no” with no source evidence or policy. What is the main weakness?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Approval should happen after execution.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"The human cannot exercise meaningful judgment and may become a rubber stamp.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Human review must never show evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"The model should hide uncertainty.\"}]","a","HITL must provide enough context for a real decision. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A reversible low-impact content tag is wrong occasionally. Which oversight approach may be proportionate? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Post-action or sampled review with monitoring, if risk is acceptable.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Mandatory executive pre-approval for every tag.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"No monitoring because the action is reversible.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use admin credentials for all cases.\"}]","a","Oversight should be proportionate to consequence and reversibility. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a human-in-the-loop validation review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support human-in-the-loop validation?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Review every trivial case regardless of cost.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use pre-action review for high-consequence irreversible actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Place human approval after an irreversible action.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use pre-action review for high-consequence irreversible actions.; Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on human-in-the-loop validation? Context: An architect is reviewing human-in-the-loop validation. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use model confidence as the only escalation criterion.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Make reviewers rubber-stamp opaque outputs.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Give reviewers relevant evidence and policy.; Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For human-in-the-loop validation, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in human-in-the-loop validation?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Review every trivial case regardless of cost.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use sampling for mature low-risk workflows.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove humans where regulation explicitly requires review.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Scale oversight with consequence and regulation.; Use sampling for mature low-risk workflows.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A team says, “Our model provider is HIPAA compliant, so our whole app is compliant.” What is wrong?","Application compliance depends on the full system, data flows, controls, agreements, and responsibilities—not one provider alone. Compliance is a system-level responsibility."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for regulatory compliance architecture: A GDPR-related requirement affects deletion/retention of personal data. What should the architect do?","Map the requirement to specific data lifecycle controls, ownership, and evidence. Regulatory obligations must become operational controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this regulatory compliance architecture situation? A FedRAMP-scoped system adds a new cloud service. What architecture question is most important?","Whether the service falls within the authorized boundary/control inheritance and change process. Boundary and authorization/control scope are central compliance concerns."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A flashcard claims a specific legal requirement not present in the primary source. What should the study deck do?","Avoid or verify the claim against authoritative regulatory guidance before teaching it. Exact legal obligations require primary-source verification."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Control evidence — D5.4 application","Records/artifacts demonstrating that a required control is implemented and operating."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Compliance boundary — D5.4 application","The systems, data, services, and responsibilities included in the regulated/authorized scope."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In regulatory compliance architecture, {{c1::Control evidence}} is the concept described as: Records/artifacts demonstrating that a required control is implemented and operating.","Applied reinforcement for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In regulatory compliance architecture, {{c1::Compliance boundary}} is the concept described as: The systems, data, services, and responsibilities included in the regulated/authorized scope.","Applied reinforcement for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For regulatory compliance architecture, the precise answer to “What term describes records proving a control is implemented and operating?” is {{c1::Control evidence}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["During an operational review, apply this regulatory compliance architecture rule: In regulatory compliance architecture, {{c1::Control evidence}} is the concept described as: Records/artifacts demonstrating that a required control is implemented and operating.","Applied reinforcement for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within regulatory compliance architecture, what term matches this definition: Records/artifacts demonstrating that a required control is implemented and operating.","Control evidence"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within regulatory compliance architecture, what term matches this definition: The systems, data, services, and responsibilities included in the regulated/authorized scope.","Compliance boundary"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team says, “Our model provider is HIPAA compliant, so our whole app is compliant.” What is wrong? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Provider status never matters.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"HIPAA applies only to prompts.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Compliance can be implemented solely in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Application compliance depends on the full system, data flows, controls, agreements, and responsibilities—not one provider alone.\"}]","a","Compliance is a system-level responsibility. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved regulatory compliance architecture guidance to this case: A GDPR-related requirement affects deletion/retention of personal data. What should the architect do?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep all logs forever just in case.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume the vector database handles deletion automatically.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Map the requirement to specific data lifecycle controls, ownership, and evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Write “comply with GDPR” in the prompt.\"}]","a","Regulatory obligations must become operational controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A FedRAMP-scoped system adds a new cloud service. What architecture question is most important?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Whether the service has more UI features.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the service falls within the authorized boundary/control inheritance and change process.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Whether the model likes the service.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Whether prompts become shorter.\"}]","a","Boundary and authorization/control scope are central compliance concerns. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a regulatory compliance architecture review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support regulatory compliance architecture?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign control ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep sensitive logs indefinitely without policy.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Map obligations to enforceable controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Put “comply with GDPR” in a prompt and stop there.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Map obligations to enforceable controls.; Assign control ownership.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on regulatory compliance architecture? Context: An architect is reviewing regulatory compliance architecture. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore data residency/retention when applicable.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Assign control ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume one compliant vendor makes the whole system compliant.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Collect appropriate evidence.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Assign control ownership.; Collect appropriate evidence.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For regulatory compliance architecture, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions reduce the main risk in regulatory compliance architecture?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Collect appropriate evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep sensitive logs indefinitely without policy.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define regulated/system boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Invent legal requirements from memory.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Collect appropriate evidence.; Define regulated/system boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? An AI system has 95% aggregate accuracy but performs much worse for an important subgroup. What should the team do?","Evaluate relevant slices and address the disparity rather than relying only on aggregate accuracy. Aggregate metrics can conceal uneven outcomes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for responsible and ethical AI: After a harmful automated decision, the team says “the AI decided.” What governance problem is most direct?","Lack of accountability and ownership. Organizations remain responsible for system decisions and controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this responsible and ethical AI situation? A user asks why a consequential recommendation was made. What transparency approach is strongest?","Provide relevant evidence, policy/reasoning summary, limitations, and appeal/ownership path without exposing private chain-of-thought. Transparency should be useful and appropriate to the audience."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A team stores every model/tool interaction forever to maximize traceability. What concern should be balanced?","Data minimization, privacy, retention, and access controls. Traceability must be balanced against unnecessary sensitive-data retention."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Fairness evaluation — D5.5 application","Assessing relevant performance/outcomes across appropriate groups or slices instead of relying only on aggregate metrics."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Accountability — D5.5 application","Clear ownership for architecture decisions, residual risk, monitoring, and incident response."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In responsible and ethical AI, {{c1::Fairness evaluation}} is the concept described as: Assessing relevant performance/outcomes across appropriate groups or slices instead of relying only on aggregate metrics.","Applied reinforcement for D5.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In responsible and ethical AI, {{c1::Accountability}} is the concept described as: Clear ownership for architecture decisions, residual risk, monitoring, and incident response.","Applied reinforcement for D5.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For responsible and ethical AI, the precise answer to “What concept means a named person/team owns residual risk and response?” is {{c1::Accountability}}.","Applied reinforcement for D5.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within responsible and ethical AI, what term matches this definition: Assessing relevant performance/outcomes across appropriate groups or slices instead of relying only on aggregate metrics.","Fairness evaluation"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within responsible and ethical AI, what term matches this definition: Clear ownership for architecture decisions, residual risk, monitoring, and incident response.","Accountability"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An AI system has 95% aggregate accuracy but performs much worse for an important subgroup. What should the team do? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore subgroup results because aggregate accuracy is high.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Hide the subgroup metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Increase logging retention indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate relevant slices and address the disparity rather than relying only on aggregate accuracy.\"}]","a","Aggregate metrics can conceal uneven outcomes. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved responsible and ethical AI guidance to this case: After a harmful automated decision, the team says “the AI decided.” What governance problem is most direct?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Insufficient prompt caching.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Too many A/B tests.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Lack of accountability and ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Too much semantic retrieval.\"}]","a","Organizations remain responsible for system decisions and controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A user asks why a consequential recommendation was made. What transparency approach is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Provide no explanation because models are probabilistic.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provide relevant evidence, policy/reasoning summary, limitations, and appeal/ownership path without exposing private chain-of-thought.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Reveal raw hidden chain-of-thought.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Say only “the AI decided.”\"}]","a","Transparency should be useful and appropriate to the audience. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a responsible and ethical AI review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support responsible and ethical AI?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat transparency as raw chain-of-thought disclosure.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate relevant outcome slices.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use aggregate accuracy as the only fairness evidence.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Evaluate relevant outcome slices.; Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on responsible and ethical AI? Context: An architect is reviewing responsible and ethical AI. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep all sensitive logs forever.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Say “the AI decided” to avoid ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Provide audience-appropriate transparency.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep human/organizational accountability explicit.; Provide audience-appropriate transparency.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D5.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a defense-in-depth path for a consequential action.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Validate/classify the request\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Let the model reason within scoped context/tools\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Apply deterministic policy and authorization checks\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Require human approval when risk demands it\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute and record the authorized action\"}]","Probabilistic reasoning is surrounded by enforceable controls before execution. Sequence reinforcement for D5.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a risk-treatment cycle for an identified agent failure mode.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Identify the threat/failure mode\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Reduce likelihood with preventive controls\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Detect attempts or failures with monitoring\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Contain/stop harmful effects\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Recover and add regression/response improvements\"}]","Risk treatment combines prevention, detection, containment, and recovery. Sequence reinforcement for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order an indirect-prompt-injection defense path.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Treat external content as untrusted data\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Limit the agent's reachable tools/secrets\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Detect suspicious instructions/behavior where possible\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Re-authorize consequential actions outside the model\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Block or escalate unsafe execution\"}]","Untrusted content is paired with limited capability and independent action controls. Sequence reinforcement for D5.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a meaningful pre-action HITL flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Model proposes the consequential action\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Collect the evidence/policy relevant to review\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Present proposal and context to the authorized reviewer\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Reviewer approves or rejects\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute only approved actions and record the decision\"}]","The human decision occurs before execution and is informed by evidence. Sequence reinforcement for D5.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a compliance-control mapping workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Identify the applicable requirement\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Translate it into a technical/operational control\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Assign an owner\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Define evidence that proves operation\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Set review/monitoring cadence\"}]","Compliance becomes actionable through controls, ownership, evidence, and ongoing review. Sequence reinforcement for D5.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d5\",\"obj:d5.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A stakeholder says the assistant must be “very fast.” What should the architect ask next?","Define a measurable latency target such as an agreed percentile/SLA. Discovery converts adjectives into measurable criteria."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for structured discovery and requirement gathering: A stakeholder asks for an agent but cannot explain the desired outcome. What is the best next step?","Clarify the workflow problem, baseline, users, constraints, and success criteria. Implementation language should not replace requirements discovery."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this structured discovery and requirement gathering situation? A proposed workflow handles sensitive data, but nobody has identified who owns residual privacy risk. What is missing?","Explicit risk/decision ownership as part of requirements and governance. Ownership is a requirement for operating consequential systems."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Two teams disagree on what “correct” means for an extraction task. What should happen before architecture selection?","Agree on testable quality criteria and representative examples/evals. Quality requirements need a shared measurable definition."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
