{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within structured discovery and requirement gathering, what term matches this definition: What the solution must do.","Functional requirement"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within structured discovery and requirement gathering, what term matches this definition: How the solution must operate, such as latency, availability, scale, residency, or cost.","Non-functional requirement"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved structured discovery and requirement gathering rule? Discovery should turn vague goals into _____ before design.","observable acceptance criteria"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A stakeholder says the assistant must be “very fast.” What should the architect ask next? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the fastest model immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assume “fast” means under one minute.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore latency until after launch.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define a measurable latency target such as an agreed percentile/SLA.\"}]","a","Discovery converts adjectives into measurable criteria. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved structured discovery and requirement gathering guidance to this case: A stakeholder asks for an agent but cannot explain the desired outcome. What is the best next step?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Pick tools before understanding users.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat “agent” as the business requirement.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clarify the workflow problem, baseline, users, constraints, and success criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Start implementing an autonomous agent.\"}]","a","Implementation language should not replace requirements discovery. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A proposed workflow handles sensitive data, but nobody has identified who owns residual privacy risk. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A second classifier.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explicit risk/decision ownership as part of requirements and governance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More retrieval documents.\"}]","a","Ownership is a requirement for operating consequential systems. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Two teams disagree on what “correct” means for an extraction task. What should happen before architecture selection? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Agree on testable quality criteria and representative examples/evals.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the strongest model and let it decide.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Build two unrelated systems.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Delay defining correctness until production.\"}]","a","Quality requirements need a shared measurable definition. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a structured discovery and requirement gathering review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support structured discovery and requirement gathering?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Establish a baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Copy unrelated SLAs without justification.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Ask what changes if the project succeeds.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Accept implementation requests as final requirements.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Ask what changes if the project succeeds.; Establish a baseline.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on structured discovery and requirement gathering? Context: An architect is reviewing structured discovery and requirement gathering. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Leave risk ownership implicit.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Establish a baseline.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Design before defining success.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Quantify quality and latency requirements.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Establish a baseline.; Quantify quality and latency requirements.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For structured discovery and requirement gathering, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions best improve structured discovery and requirement gathering?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Quantify quality and latency requirements.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Copy unrelated SLAs without justification.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify prohibited/high-risk behavior early.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Wait until launch to decide what errors are catastrophic.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Quantify quality and latency requirements.; Identify prohibited/high-risk behavior early.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? An executive asks why an agentic design costs more. Which explanation is most useful?","Connect added autonomy to expected business value, latency/cost impact, and residual risk. Executives need outcome, cost, timeline, and major risk implications."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs: A security reviewer evaluates the same architecture. What should communication emphasize?","Identity, trust boundaries, permissions, data flows, and threat controls. Audience-specific emphasis should address the reviewer's responsibilities."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs situation? A proposal lists only the preferred architecture and omits alternatives. What is missing?","Evidence-based trade-off comparison and rationale for rejecting alternatives. Decision quality is clearer when meaningful alternatives and concessions are visible."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Two architectures have different cost, quality, and reversibility. What should the recommendation include?","A comparison against the agreed constraints and the cost/risk of changing later. Trade-off communication is contextual."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trade-off — D6.2 application","A deliberate exchange where improving one property costs or constrains another."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Reversibility — D6.2 application","How easily and cheaply an architecture decision can be changed later."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["why the option fits the constraints — D6.2 application","Phrase that completes this communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs rule: A strong recommendation explains _____, not just what components it uses."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, {{c1::Trade-off}} is the concept described as: A deliberate exchange where improving one property costs or constrains another.","Applied reinforcement for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, {{c1::Reversibility}} is the concept described as: How easily and cheaply an architecture decision can be changed later.","Applied reinforcement for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, the precise answer to “What term describes the cost/ease of changing an architecture decision later?” is {{c1::Reversibility}}.","Applied reinforcement for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, the precise answer to “What term describes exchanging one architecture benefit for another cost or constraint?” is {{c1::Trade-off}}.","Applied reinforcement for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, what term matches this definition: A deliberate exchange where improving one property costs or constrains another.","Trade-off"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, what term matches this definition: How easily and cheaply an architecture decision can be changed later.","Reversibility"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs rule? A strong recommendation explains _____, not just what components it uses.","why the option fits the constraints"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An executive asks why an agentic design costs more. Which explanation is most useful? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"List every SDK method.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Show only a component diagram.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Say agents are the modern choice.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Connect added autonomy to expected business value, latency/cost impact, and residual risk.\"}]","a","Executives need outcome, cost, timeline, and major risk implications. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs guidance to this case: A security reviewer evaluates the same architecture. What should communication emphasize?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only UI screenshots.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only token price.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identity, trust boundaries, permissions, data flows, and threat controls.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Marketing slogans.\"}]","a","Audience-specific emphasis should address the reviewer's responsibilities. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A proposal lists only the preferred architecture and omits alternatives. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"More diagrams with no rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evidence-based trade-off comparison and rationale for rejecting alternatives.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More jargon.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A bigger model.\"}]","a","Decision quality is clearer when meaningful alternatives and concessions are visible. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Two architectures have different cost, quality, and reversibility. What should the recommendation include? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A comparison against the agreed constraints and the cost/risk of changing later.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only which is newest.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only which uses MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only which has more components.\"}]","a","Trade-off communication is contextual. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compare alternatives against the same constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Present diagrams without rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explain benefit, cost, and risk together.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Hide trade-offs to sell the proposal.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Explain benefit, cost, and risk together.; Compare alternatives against the same constraints.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs? Context: An architect is reviewing communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Compare options without shared constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare alternatives against the same constraints.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give every audience the same technical detail.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Compare alternatives against the same constraints.; Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions best improve communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Present diagrams without rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Discuss reversibility for costly decisions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Recommend technology because it is fashionable.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Adapt emphasis to stakeholder needs.; Discuss reversibility for costly decisions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A stakeholder asks for 100% correctness from a probabilistic support assistant. What is the strongest response?","Define measurable quality targets, unacceptable failure classes, escalation, and verification rather than promise perfection. Expectations must reflect probabilistic behavior and controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment: Users click thumbs-down more often after a release. What should the team do?","Treat it as a signal, investigate affected cases/trajectories, identify cause, and verify a targeted fix. Feedback becomes useful through investigation and action."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment situation? Prompts have been tuned repeatedly, but the architecture cannot meet a new real-time latency requirement. What is likely needed?","Re-architecture because a fundamental constraint changed. Pattern-level constraints can require architectural change."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: A safety incident occurs but no threshold defines when to rollback or escalate. What is missing?","Explicit response triggers, ownership, and expected actions. Feedback systems need actionable thresholds and owners."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Feedback signal — D6.3 application","Observed evidence such as user reports, tool errors, cost drift, or safety incidents."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["SLA — D6.3 application","An agreed service-level expectation/commitment for measurable service behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, {{c1::Feedback signal}} is the concept described as: Observed evidence such as user reports, tool errors, cost drift, or safety incidents.","Applied reinforcement for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, {{c1::SLA}} is the concept described as: An agreed service-level expectation/commitment for measurable service behavior.","Applied reinforcement for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, the precise answer to “What agreement sets measurable service expectations such as latency or availability?” is {{c1::SLA}}.","Applied reinforcement for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, the precise answer to “What should happen after a feedback-driven change to confirm it worked?” is {{c1::Verification}}.","Applied reinforcement for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, what term matches this definition: Observed evidence such as user reports, tool errors, cost drift, or safety incidents.","Feedback signal"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, what term matches this definition: An agreed service-level expectation/commitment for measurable service behavior.","SLA"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment rule? A useful feedback loop has a signal, trigger, owner, action, and _____.","verification"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A stakeholder asks for 100% correctness from a probabilistic support assistant. What is the strongest response? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Promise 100% if the prompt is long enough.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Hide error rates.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the strongest model and call it deterministic.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define measurable quality targets, unacceptable failure classes, escalation, and verification rather than promise perfection.\"}]","a","Expectations must reflect probabilistic behavior and controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment guidance to this case: Users click thumbs-down more often after a release. What should the team do?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Roll back every time without investigation.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore it because thumbs-down is subjective.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Treat it as a signal, investigate affected cases/trajectories, identify cause, and verify a targeted fix.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the model alone is at fault.\"}]","a","Feedback becomes useful through investigation and action. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Prompts have been tuned repeatedly, but the architecture cannot meet a new real-time latency requirement. What is likely needed?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove monitoring.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Re-architecture because a fundamental constraint changed.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only add more prompt text.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep the architecture forever.\"}]","a","Pattern-level constraints can require architectural change. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A safety incident occurs but no threshold defines when to rollback or escalate. What is missing? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explicit response triggers, ownership, and expected actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A longer model response.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"More unrelated metrics.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A second UI theme.\"}]","a","Feedback systems need actionable thresholds and owners. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat every complaint as a model failure.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Set measurable expectations.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Promise deterministic perfection.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Set measurable expectations.; Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment? Context: An architect is reviewing stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep tuning prompts when architecture is the bottleneck.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Say “we'll improve from feedback” with no mechanism.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Investigate before attributing cause.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define triggers and owners for feedback signals.; Investigate before attributing cause.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions best improve stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Investigate before attributing cause.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat every complaint as a model failure.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Verify changes after action.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Create SLAs with no monitoring or response plan.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Investigate before attributing cause.; Verify changes after action.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? An ADR says only “Use MCP.” What key information is missing?","Context, alternatives, trade-offs, rationale, assumptions, and review triggers. A decision record should preserve why the choice was made."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for architecture documentation and implementation guidance: A system works, but only the original architect knows how to recover from tool failures. What documentation is most needed?","Operational runbooks plus ownership and escalation guidance. Handoff requires operational knowledge, not just design diagrams."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this architecture documentation and implementation guidance situation? A model/tool change invalidates assumptions in an old architecture document. What should happen?","Update or supersede the relevant decision/documentation so it matches the current system. Documentation should track the system/version it describes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["State the preferred architecture action for this design-review scenario: Which architecture decision most deserves an ADR?","A costly, risky, hard-to-reverse choice with meaningful alternatives. ADRs are most useful for consequential decisions."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["ADR — D6.4 application","Architecture Decision Record documenting a significant decision, context, alternatives, and rationale."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Runbook — D6.4 application","Operational guidance for diagnosing, responding to, and recovering from known conditions/incidents."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In architecture documentation and implementation guidance, {{c1::ADR}} is the concept described as: Architecture Decision Record documenting a significant decision, context, alternatives, and rationale.","Applied reinforcement for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In architecture documentation and implementation guidance, {{c1::Runbook}} is the concept described as: Operational guidance for diagnosing, responding to, and recovering from known conditions/incidents.","Applied reinforcement for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For architecture documentation and implementation guidance, the precise answer to “What document records an architecture decision, context, alternatives, and rationale?” is {{c1::ADR}}.","Applied reinforcement for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within architecture documentation and implementation guidance, what term matches this definition: Architecture Decision Record documenting a significant decision, context, alternatives, and rationale.","ADR"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within architecture documentation and implementation guidance, what term matches this definition: Operational guidance for diagnosing, responding to, and recovering from known conditions/incidents.","Runbook"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An ADR says only “Use MCP.” What key information is missing? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More screenshots.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A model-generated slogan.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A longer title.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Context, alternatives, trade-offs, rationale, assumptions, and review triggers.\"}]","a","A decision record should preserve why the choice was made. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved architecture documentation and implementation guidance guidance to this case: A system works, but only the original architect knows how to recover from tool failures. What documentation is most needed?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only a component logo sheet.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A longer system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Operational runbooks plus ownership and escalation guidance.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More marketing documentation.\"}]","a","Handoff requires operational knowledge, not just design diagrams. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A model/tool change invalidates assumptions in an old architecture document. What should happen?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume code comments are enough.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Update or supersede the relevant decision/documentation so it matches the current system.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep docs unchanged forever.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Delete all history.\"}]","a","Documentation should track the system/version it describes. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Which architecture decision most deserves an ADR? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A costly, risky, hard-to-reverse choice with meaningful alternatives.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A trivial typo fix.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A temporary local variable name.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A one-time console command with no architectural impact.\"}]","a","ADRs are most useful for consequential decisions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a architecture documentation and implementation guidance review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support architecture documentation and implementation guidance?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Document assumptions and review triggers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Leave docs stale after major changes.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Record rationale and alternatives.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Produce diagrams with no rationale.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Record rationale and alternatives.; Document assumptions and review triggers.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on architecture documentation and implementation guidance? Context: An architect is reviewing architecture documentation and implementation guidance. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Record only the chosen technology name.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Document assumptions and review triggers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let critical knowledge live only in one person's head.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep implementation contracts close to the system.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Document assumptions and review triggers.; Keep implementation contracts close to the system.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For architecture documentation and implementation guidance, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions best improve architecture documentation and implementation guidance?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep implementation contracts close to the system.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Leave docs stale after major changes.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Provide runbooks for operations.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Omit rollback/operational guidance from handoff.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep implementation contracts close to the system.; Provide runbooks for operations.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A team launches before agreeing on acceptance criteria, then tries to infer success from dashboards. Which lifecycle problem occurred?","Discovery/design did not define success before handoff/monitoring. Later phases cannot repair undefined earlier requirements."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for solution lifecycle management: Architecture is complete, but no implementation owner or rollback plan exists. Which phase is not ready?","Handoff / implementation readiness. Handoff requires ownership and operational readiness."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this solution lifecycle management situation? Production monitoring finds a new failure mode. What is the strongest lifecycle response?","Feed it into iteration: fix the system, update evals/docs/controls, and verify. Monitoring should inform evidence-driven iteration."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Handoff — D6.5 application","Transition from architecture/design into implementation and operational ownership with acceptance criteria and guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Iteration — D6.5 application","Evidence-driven changes after design/launch, accompanied by updated evaluation and documentation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In solution lifecycle management, {{c1::Handoff}} is the concept described as: Transition from architecture/design into implementation and operational ownership with acceptance criteria and guidance.","Applied reinforcement for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In solution lifecycle management, {{c1::Iteration}} is the concept described as: Evidence-driven changes after design/launch, accompanied by updated evaluation and documentation.","Applied reinforcement for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For solution lifecycle management, the precise answer to “What lifecycle phase follows design before production operation?” is {{c1::Handoff}}.","Applied reinforcement for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within solution lifecycle management, what term matches this definition: Transition from architecture/design into implementation and operational ownership with acceptance criteria and guidance.","Handoff"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within solution lifecycle management, what term matches this definition: Evidence-driven changes after design/launch, accompanied by updated evaluation and documentation.","Iteration"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team launches before agreeing on acceptance criteria, then tries to infer success from dashboards. Which lifecycle problem occurred? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Monitoring should always define requirements retroactively.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Handoff should happen before design.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Iteration eliminates the need for acceptance criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Discovery/design did not define success before handoff/monitoring.\"}]","a","Later phases cannot repair undefined earlier requirements. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved solution lifecycle management guidance to this case: Architecture is complete, but no implementation owner or rollback plan exists. Which phase is not ready?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Retrieval indexing.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Model prompting.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Handoff / implementation readiness.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Discovery only.\"}]","a","Handoff requires ownership and operational readiness. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Production monitoring finds a new failure mode. What is the strongest lifecycle response?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Delete monitoring evidence.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Feed it into iteration: fix the system, update evals/docs/controls, and verify.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ignore it because design is complete.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Change prompts without testing.\"}]","a","Monitoring should inform evidence-driven iteration. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a solution lifecycle management review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support solution lifecycle management?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define acceptance criteria before handoff.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Monitor infrastructure only.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Complete discovery before committing architecture.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Launch with no acceptance criteria.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Complete discovery before committing architecture.; Define acceptance criteria before handoff.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on solution lifecycle management? Context: An architect is reviewing solution lifecycle management. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change behavior without updating evals.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define acceptance criteria before handoff.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Handoff without ownership.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Assign implementation and operations ownership.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define acceptance criteria before handoff.; Assign implementation and operations ownership.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a structured discovery flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Clarify the business outcome and baseline\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Map users and current workflow\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Define measurable quality/latency/scale constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Identify risk/compliance boundaries\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Assign owners and acceptance criteria\"}]","Discovery progresses from outcome/workflow to measurable constraints and ownership. Sequence reinforcement for D6.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a concise architecture-decision explanation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"State the decision context/constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Present the recommended option\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Explain benefits and evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Explain costs/risks and alternatives\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"State ownership/review triggers\"}]","The audience first needs context, then recommendation and its trade-offs. Sequence reinforcement for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order an actionable stakeholder feedback loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Collect a signal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Compare it to a trigger/threshold\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Assign investigation to the owner\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Take the targeted action\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Verify the outcome and update expectations/evals\"}]","Signals drive owned investigation, action, and verification. Sequence reinforcement for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a useful ADR structure.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Describe context and constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"State the decision\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Record meaningful alternatives\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Explain trade-offs and rationale\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Record assumptions, owner, and review trigger\"}]","ADRs preserve why a decision was made and when it may need revisiting. Sequence reinforcement for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order the CCAR-P solution lifecycle.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Discovery\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Design\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Handoff\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Monitoring\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Iteration\"}]","The blueprint explicitly frames these phases in this lifecycle order. Sequence reinforcement for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? A team tells Claude Code “never touch production,” but every developer environment has production admin credentials. What is strongest?","Remove/restrict production credentials and permissions; keep the instruction as supplemental guidance. Hard permission boundaries should not depend on model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for team-level Claude tools and environments: Each developer has a different MCP/tool configuration and shared workflows behave inconsistently. What should the team do?","Standardize high-value repository/team configuration and version it. Shared configuration improves reproducibility and governance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this team-level Claude tools and environments situation? A third-party Skill contains scripts and external resources. What should happen before team-wide adoption?","Review provenance/content, test it, and constrain permissions appropriately. Skills can affect behavior and execution and should be governed."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Instruction — D7.1 application","Guidance intended to influence model behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Runtime control — D7.1 application","An enforceable runtime, permission, sandbox, policy, or CI boundary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In team-level Claude tools and environments, {{c1::Instruction}} is the concept described as: Guidance intended to influence model behavior.","Applied reinforcement for D7.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In team-level Claude tools and environments, {{c1::Runtime control}} is the concept described as: An enforceable runtime, permission, sandbox, policy, or CI boundary.","Applied reinforcement for D7.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For team-level Claude tools and environments, the precise answer to “What mechanism enforces what the runtime is permitted to do?” is {{c1::Control}}.","Applied reinforcement for D7.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within team-level Claude tools and environments, what term matches this definition: Guidance intended to influence model behavior.","Instruction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within team-level Claude tools and environments, what term matches this definition: An enforceable runtime, permission, sandbox, policy, or CI boundary.","Runtime control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team tells Claude Code “never touch production,” but every developer environment has production admin credentials. What is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Repeat the instruction more often.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Disable code review.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give the model more context about production.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Remove/restrict production credentials and permissions; keep the instruction as supplemental guidance.\"}]","a","Hard permission boundaries should not depend on model compliance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved team-level Claude tools and environments guidance to this case: Each developer has a different MCP/tool configuration and shared workflows behave inconsistently. What should the team do?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Hide configuration from version control.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Give all developers broader credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Standardize high-value repository/team configuration and version it.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Encourage every developer to improvise permanently.\"}]","a","Shared configuration improves reproducibility and governance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A third-party Skill contains scripts and external resources. What should happen before team-wide adoption?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Skip review because Skills are only text.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Review provenance/content, test it, and constrain permissions appropriately.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust it because it is called a Skill.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give it full production access first.\"}]","a","Skills can affect behavior and execution and should be governed. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Which is an enforceable control rather than an instruction? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A sandbox/network policy that prevents access to production.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A sentence saying “be careful.”\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A README asking the agent not to deploy.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A prompt example showing a safe action.\"}]","a","Enforceable boundaries restrict capability independently of model choice. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a team-level Claude tools and environments review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support team-level Claude tools and environments?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Let each developer use unreviewed global Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Standardize shared high-value configuration.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Rely on one giant instruction file for enforcement.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Standardize shared high-value configuration.; Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D7.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on team-level Claude tools and environments? Context: An architect is reviewing team-level Claude tools and environments. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat prompts as equivalent to permissions.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give broad credentials because setup is easier.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Review third-party tools/Skills.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use permission and sandbox boundaries for hard restrictions.; Review third-party tools/Skills.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D7.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["For team-level Claude tools and environments, select the TWO options that preserve the approved design principles. Which TWO decisions best improve team-level Claude tools and environments?","[{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Review third-party tools/Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let each developer use unreviewed global Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Version shared instructions and Skills.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep critical team configuration undocumented.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Review third-party tools/Skills.; Version shared instructions and Skills.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D7.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? An agent writes a large refactor and tests pass, but nobody reviews whether the tests cover the risk. What is missing?","Independent human/system verification of both the change and test adequacy. Passing tests are evidence, not a substitute for judging whether verification is sufficient."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for AI-assisted developer workflows: A developer asks an agent to “make it work” using production admin credentials. What is the strongest correction?","Use a scoped development/test environment and require approval for shared/destructive actions. Developer productivity should not expand unnecessary production capability."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this AI-assisted developer workflows situation? AI-generated code is merged, but no team member understands it well enough to maintain it. What principle was violated?","Reviewability and human accountability for the change. Teams must be able to own and maintain generated changes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Verification tool — D7.2 application","An independent mechanism such as tests, linters, type checks, security scans, or CI used to check generated changes."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Reviewability — D7.2 application","The ability for developers to understand and own an AI-generated change."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In AI-assisted developer workflows, {{c1::Verification tool}} is the concept described as: An independent mechanism such as tests, linters, type checks, security scans, or CI used to check generated changes.","Applied reinforcement for D7.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In AI-assisted developer workflows, {{c1::Reviewability}} is the concept described as: The ability for developers to understand and own an AI-generated change.","Applied reinforcement for D7.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For AI-assisted developer workflows, the precise answer to “What quality means developers can understand and own an AI-generated change?” is {{c1::Reviewability}}.","Applied reinforcement for D7.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within AI-assisted developer workflows, what term matches this definition: An independent mechanism such as tests, linters, type checks, security scans, or CI used to check generated changes.","Verification tool"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within AI-assisted developer workflows, what term matches this definition: The ability for developers to understand and own an AI-generated change.","Reviewability"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An agent writes a large refactor and tests pass, but nobody reviews whether the tests cover the risk. What is missing? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A larger model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Production credentials.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fewer tests.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Independent human/system verification of both the change and test adequacy.\"}]","a","Passing tests are evidence, not a substitute for judging whether verification is sufficient. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved AI-assisted developer workflows guidance to this case: A developer asks an agent to “make it work” using production admin credentials. What is the strongest correction?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Disable logs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove rollback mechanisms.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use a scoped development/test environment and require approval for shared/destructive actions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let the agent proceed because the developer asked.\"}]","a","Developer productivity should not expand unnecessary production capability. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? AI-generated code is merged, but no team member understands it well enough to maintain it. What principle was violated?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Model lifecycle.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reviewability and human accountability for the change.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Prompt caching.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Semantic retrieval.\"}]","a","Teams must be able to own and maintain generated changes. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a AI-assisted developer workflows review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support AI-assisted developer workflows?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Disable safeguards the agent finds inconvenient.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Provide goals, constraints, and acceptance criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Merge solely because the agent says tests passed.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Provide goals, constraints, and acceptance criteria.; Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D7.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on AI-assisted developer workflows? Context: An architect is reviewing AI-assisted developer workflows. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Accept generated code nobody can maintain.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use production admin credentials for convenience.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Scope permissions to reversible local work by default.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use tests/linters/type checks/security scans.; Scope permissions to reversible local work by default.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D7.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Without answer choices, what is the best architecture response to this scenario? Quality drops after a deployment. Which evidence should be checked first?","Model/prompt versions, retrieval/index changes, traces, and input-distribution changes around the deployment. Debugging starts from correlated evidence around the affected layer/change."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["Resolve this production scenario for debugging and operational issue resolution: An agent suddenly receives “permission denied” from a tool. What areas are most relevant?","Credentials, scopes, authorization policy, tool contract, and dependency status. Tool failures should be diagnosed at the integration/permission boundary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["What should an architect recommend in this debugging and operational issue resolution situation? A cross-tenant data leak is observed. How should it be treated?","As a security incident focused on authorization/filtering boundaries, with containment and evidence preservation. Cross-tenant exposure is a security boundary failure."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Operational runbook — D7.3 application","Documented operational steps for diagnosis, mitigation, rollback/fallback, escalation, and evidence preservation."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["verification — D7.3 application","Phrase that completes this debugging and operational issue resolution rule: Operational debugging should proceed from symptom → evidence → likely layer → fix → _____."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["In debugging and operational issue resolution, {{c1::Operational runbook}} is the concept described as: Documented operational steps for diagnosis, mitigation, rollback/fallback, escalation, and evidence preservation.","Applied reinforcement for D7.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["For debugging and operational issue resolution, the precise answer to “What document gives repeatable incident diagnosis and recovery steps?” is {{c1::Runbook}}.","Applied reinforcement for D7.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["During an operational review, apply this debugging and operational issue resolution rule: In debugging and operational issue resolution, {{c1::Operational runbook}} is the concept described as: Documented operational steps for diagnosis, mitigation, rollback/fallback, escalation, and evidence preservation.","Applied reinforcement for D7.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["Within debugging and operational issue resolution, what term matches this definition: Documented operational steps for diagnosis, mitigation, rollback/fallback, escalation, and evidence preservation.","Operational runbook"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["What phrase completes this approved debugging and operational issue resolution rule? Operational debugging should proceed from symptom → evidence → likely layer → fix → _____.","verification"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Quality drops after a deployment. Which evidence should be checked first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only ask the model why it failed.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Delete old logs.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Immediately add production admin access.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Model/prompt versions, retrieval/index changes, traces, and input-distribution changes around the deployment.\"}]","a","Debugging starts from correlated evidence around the affected layer/change. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Apply the approved debugging and operational issue resolution guidance to this case: An agent suddenly receives “permission denied” from a tool. What areas are most relevant?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Model temperature only.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Business ROI only.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Credentials, scopes, authorization policy, tool contract, and dependency status.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"RAG chunk size only.\"}]","a","Tool failures should be diagnosed at the integration/permission boundary. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A cross-tenant data leak is observed. How should it be treated?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"By deleting logs immediately.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"As a security incident focused on authorization/filtering boundaries, with containment and evidence preservation.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"As an ordinary style-quality issue.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"By only rewriting the prompt.\"}]","a","Cross-tenant exposure is a security boundary failure. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["During a debugging and operational issue resolution review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support debugging and operational issue resolution?","[{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume every operator needs production admin access.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use correlated traces/evidence to isolate failures.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ask the model why it failed as the only incident process.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use correlated traces/evidence to isolate failures.; Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D7.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on debugging and operational issue resolution? Context: An architect is reviewing debugging and operational issue resolution. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Fix incidents without regression tests.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Keep logs that cannot correlate components.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define rollback/fallback and escalation owners.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Maintain runbooks with safe diagnostic steps.; Define rollback/fallback and escalation owners.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D7.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a team enablement flow for a new Claude tool/Skill.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the intended team use case\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Review provenance and required permissions\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Configure the tool/Skill in a scoped environment\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Test behavior and controls\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Version and roll out the approved configuration\"}]","Use case and security review precede scoped rollout. Sequence reinforcement for D7.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a safe AI-assisted coding loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the task and acceptance criteria\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Let the agent explore/implement within scoped permissions\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run independent automated checks\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Review the change and evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Merge/deploy through normal controlled processes\"}]","AI generation is followed by independent verification and normal release controls. Sequence reinforcement for D7.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.2\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a repeatable incident-resolution loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Detect the symptom/alert\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Collect correlated evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify and isolate the likely failing layer\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Mitigate/fix with rollback or safe recovery as needed\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Verify and add regression coverage\"}]","Evidence-driven diagnosis precedes mitigation and regression protection. Sequence reinforcement for D7.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.3\",\"priority:p1\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A stakeholder says, “Build us an autonomous agent.” What should the architect do first? Which recommendation should they defend?","Clarify the business outcome, constraints, and measurable success criteria. Architecture starts from the outcome and constraints; “agent” is an implementation hypothesis. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved translating business problems into Claude-based solutions guidance to this case: A finance workflow must classify expenses but refunds over $500 require exact enforcement. Where should the $500 rule live?","In deterministic policy/authorization logic outside the model. Hard thresholds should not depend on probabilistic model compliance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A team has not defined what “better customer support” means. What is the best architecture next step?","Define measurable outcome and acceptance criteria before selecting components. A solution cannot be evaluated without a measurable target. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Outcome requirement — D1.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions","The measurable value or change the solution should create."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Risk constraint — D1.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions","A condition defining what the system must not do without stronger controls."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: the exact term for “Within translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, what term matches this definition: The measurable value or change the solution should create.” is {{c1::Outcome requirement}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: the exact term for “Within translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, what term matches this definition: A condition defining what the system must not do without stronger controls.” is {{c1::Risk constraint}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved translating business problems into Claude-based solutions rule? Architecture should begin with the _____, not the preferred AI component.” is {{c1::business outcome}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: what phrase completes this rule? In translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, _____ is the concept described as: The measurable value or change the solution should create.","Outcome requirement"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: what phrase completes this rule? In translating business problems into Claude-based solutions, _____ is the concept described as: A condition defining what the system must not do without stronger controls.","Risk constraint"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A stakeholder says, “Build us an autonomous agent.” What should the architect do first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Implement MCP for every backend.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clarify the business outcome, constraints, and measurable success criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose the most capable Claude model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Create a multi-agent architecture.\"}]","a","Architecture starts from the outcome and constraints; “agent” is an implementation hypothesis. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved translating business problems into Claude-based solutions guidance to this case: A finance workflow must classify expenses but refunds over $500 require exact enforcement. Where should the $500 rule live?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"In a few-shot example.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Only in the model's explanation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"In deterministic policy/authorization logic outside the model.\"}]","a","Hard thresholds should not depend on probabilistic model compliance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a translating business problems into Claude-based solutions review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support translating business problems into Claude-based solutions?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use prompt wording as the only authorization control.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Select the strongest model before clarifying the workload.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define the measurable business outcome before the component diagram.; Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 edge-case review for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: select the TWO recommendations that remain valid. Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on translating business problems into Claude-based solutions? Context: An architect is reviewing translating business problems into Claude-based solutions. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat the word “agent” as a mandatory architecture requirement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Skip measurable targets until after launch.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Identify hard risk constraints before choosing an autonomy level.; Separate probabilistic language work from deterministic enforcement.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support agent can issue account credits. Which architecture is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","Let Claude propose the credit, then deterministically verify identity, amount, and permission before execution. Consequential actions need explicit authorization and safe failure behavior. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved end-to-end Claude architecture guidance to this case: A tool times out after a payment request, and the client cannot tell whether the payment executed. What must the architecture consider before retrying?","Whether the operation is idempotent or has an idempotency key. Blind retries of non-idempotent side effects can duplicate actions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for end-to-end Claude architecture: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A vector index contains yesterday's account balance. The user asks for the current balance. What should supply the answer?","The authoritative account system/API. Current operational state should come from the system of record. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["System of record — D1.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for end-to-end Claude architecture","The authoritative source for current operational state."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Idempotent retry — D1.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for end-to-end Claude architecture","A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for end-to-end Claude architecture: the exact term for “Within end-to-end Claude architecture, what term matches this definition: The authoritative source for current operational state.” is {{c1::System of record}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for end-to-end Claude architecture: the exact term for “Within end-to-end Claude architecture, what term matches this definition: A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect.” is {{c1::Idempotent retry}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for end-to-end Claude architecture: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved end-to-end Claude architecture rule? For stateful workflows, define _____ explicitly rather than treating model context as durable state.” is {{c1::state ownership}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for end-to-end Claude architecture: what phrase completes this rule? In end-to-end Claude architecture, _____ is the concept described as: The authoritative source for current operational state.","System of record"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for end-to-end Claude architecture: what phrase completes this rule? In end-to-end Claude architecture, _____ is the concept described as: A retry that can safely repeat without duplicating an unintended side effect.","Idempotent retry"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for end-to-end Claude architecture: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support agent can issue account credits. Which architecture is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Retry the credit call automatically after any timeout without idempotency.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Let Claude propose the credit, then deterministically verify identity, amount, and permission before execution.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Let Claude issue the credit directly if the prompt says to be cautious.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Store account balance in conversation memory.\"}]","a","Consequential actions need explicit authorization and safe failure behavior. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved end-to-end Claude architecture guidance to this case: A tool times out after a payment request, and the client cannot tell whether the payment executed. What must the architecture consider before retrying?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Whether the prompt is long enough.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Whether the model is the largest available.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Whether the response was friendly.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Whether the operation is idempotent or has an idempotency key.\"}]","a","Blind retries of non-idempotent side effects can duplicate actions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for end-to-end Claude architecture: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a end-to-end Claude architecture review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support end-to-end Claude architecture?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume chat history is durable application state.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat vector retrieval as the source of truth for current transactions.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define retry/fallback/escalation behavior for external dependencies.; Keep durable application state outside model context.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.2. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 edge-case review for end-to-end Claude architecture: select the TWO recommendations that remain valid. Which TWO recommendations should survive an architecture review focused on end-to-end Claude architecture? Context: An architect is reviewing end-to-end Claude architecture. Which TWO choices align with the approved guidance?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Retry every failed side effect blindly.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Design only the happy path.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep durable application state outside model context.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Keep durable application state outside model context.; Preserve trusted identity across boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.2. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A request always follows classify → retrieve → draft → validate. Which pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","A deterministic workflow. The steps are known in advance, so a workflow offers control without unnecessary autonomy. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns guidance to this case: A research task requires discovering unknown subquestions and adapting to tool results. Which pattern is most appropriate?","A bounded agent with dynamic planning. Dynamic planning is valuable when the necessary steps cannot be predicted reliably. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? One model call plus retrieval reliably solves a bounded classification task. What should the architect do?","Keep the simple augmented-LLM design unless evaluation shows a need for more orchestration. Complexity should earn measurable value. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Workflow — D1.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns","LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Agent — D1.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns","A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: the exact term for “Within choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, what term matches this definition: LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths.” is {{c1::Workflow}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: the exact term for “Within choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, what term matches this definition: A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use.” is {{c1::Agent}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns rule? A _____ follows predefined paths, while an agent dynamically chooses its process.” is {{c1::workflow}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: what phrase completes this rule? In choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, _____ is the concept described as: LLM/tool orchestration through predefined code paths.","Workflow"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: what phrase completes this rule? In choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns, _____ is the concept described as: A system where the model dynamically directs its own process and tool use.","Agent"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A request always follows classify → retrieve → draft → validate. Which pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"An open-ended planner with unrestricted tools.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A deterministic workflow.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fully autonomous agent.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A multi-agent swarm.\"}]","a","The steps are known in advance, so a workflow offers control without unnecessary autonomy. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns guidance to this case: A research task requires discovering unknown subquestions and adapting to tool results. Which pattern is most appropriate?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"A fixed one-step prompt only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A rigid workflow with every path enumerated.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A schema validator alone.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A bounded agent with dynamic planning.\"}]","a","Dynamic planning is valuable when the necessary steps cannot be predicted reliably. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add multiple agents before testing a single-agent design.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use a workflow when steps are predictable.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use an agent whenever a task has more than one step.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use a workflow when steps are predictable.; Use an agent when dynamic planning is necessary and measured.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.3. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Financial, legal, and technical diligence can be researched independently. What architecture best exploits this? Which recommendation should they defend?","Parallel specialist workers coordinated by an orchestrator. Independent specialist work benefits from parallelism and context isolation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved multi-agent orchestration guidance to this case: Three workers write into one mutable state object and overwrite each other's assumptions. What should be improved first?","Define state ownership and explicit handoff/output contracts. Coordination boundaries and state ownership are core multi-agent design concerns. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Orchestrator — D1.4 application — P2 synthesis lens for multi-agent orchestration","The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Context isolation — D1.4 application — P2 synthesis lens for multi-agent orchestration","Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: the exact term for “Within multi-agent orchestration, what term matches this definition: The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results.” is {{c1::Orchestrator}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: the exact term for “Within multi-agent orchestration, what term matches this definition: Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution.” is {{c1::Context isolation}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for multi-agent orchestration: what phrase completes this rule? In multi-agent orchestration, _____ is the concept described as: The component that interprets the goal, decomposes work, delegates, and synthesizes results.","Orchestrator"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for multi-agent orchestration: what phrase completes this rule? In multi-agent orchestration, _____ is the concept described as: Keeping independent worker contexts separate to reduce interference and pollution.","Context isolation"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Financial, legal, and technical diligence can be researched independently. What architecture best exploits this? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A fixed sequential chain even though tasks are independent.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Parallel specialist workers coordinated by an orchestrator.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"One shared mutable prompt for all workers.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A worker agent for every sentence.\"}]","a","Independent specialist work benefits from parallelism and context isolation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved multi-agent orchestration guidance to this case: Three workers write into one mutable state object and overwrite each other's assumptions. What should be improved first?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase model temperature.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add more workers.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove tracing to reduce overhead.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define state ownership and explicit handoff/output contracts.\"}]","a","Coordination boundaries and state ownership are core multi-agent design concerns. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for multi-agent orchestration: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a multi-agent orchestration review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support multi-agent orchestration?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume worker completion without validation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Create one agent per trivial step.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use workers for independent parallelizable subtasks.; Define explicit worker inputs and outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.4. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A document must be translated, then summarized, then checked for required fields. Which decomposition pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","Prompt chaining with validation between stages. Each stage depends on the preceding output, so chaining is appropriate. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved decomposing complex problems guidance to this case: Independent searches across four jurisdictions are required. Which pattern best reduces wall-clock time?","Parallelize the independent searches and combine results. Independent work can be parallelized safely. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Parallelization — D1.5 application — P2 synthesis lens for decomposing complex problems","Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for decomposing complex problems: the exact term for “Within decomposing complex problems, what term matches this definition: Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results.” is {{c1::Parallelization}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for decomposing complex problems: the exact term for “Within decomposing complex problems, what term matches this definition: Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path.” is {{c1::Routing}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for decomposing complex problems: what phrase completes this rule? In decomposing complex problems, _____ is the concept described as: Run independent subtasks concurrently and combine their results.","Parallelization"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for decomposing complex problems: what phrase completes this rule? In decomposing complex problems, _____ is the concept described as: Classify an input and send it to the appropriate specialized path.","Routing"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for decomposing complex problems: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A document must be translated, then summarized, then checked for required fields. Which decomposition pattern best fits? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"No decomposition because multiple calls are always bad.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Prompt chaining with validation between stages.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Unbounded multi-agent exploration.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Parallel execution of all stages.\"}]","a","Each stage depends on the preceding output, so chaining is appropriate. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for decomposing complex problems: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a decomposing complex problems review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support decomposing complex problems?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use an LLM for every deterministic transformation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Decompose when stages need different context or tools.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Split work by organizational chart instead of information boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Validate useful intermediate outputs.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Decompose when stages need different context or tools.; Validate useful intermediate outputs.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.5. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Architecture A halves token cost but doubles human-review time. Architecture B costs more in tokens but sharply reduces review. What should decide? Which recommendation should they defend?","Compare total operating cost and business outcome, not token cost alone. Business value depends on end-to-end cost and outcome. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved aligning architecture to business value guidance to this case: A team reports 95% model accuracy but cannot say whether customer resolution time improved. What is missing?","A link between technical performance and a business outcome/baseline. Technical metrics must connect to value. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Technical metric — D1.6 application — P2 synthesis lens for aligning architecture to business value","A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: the exact term for “Within aligning architecture to business value, what term matches this definition: A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task.” is {{c1::Technical metric}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: the exact term for “Within aligning architecture to business value, what term matches this definition: An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction.” is {{c1::Business metric}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D1.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for aligning architecture to business value: what phrase completes this rule? In aligning architecture to business value, _____ is the concept described as: A system measure such as task success, latency, throughput, token use, or cost per task.","Technical metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for aligning architecture to business value: what phrase completes this rule? In aligning architecture to business value, _____ is the concept described as: An outcome such as time saved, cases resolved, error reduction, revenue impact, or customer satisfaction.","Business metric"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: Architecture A halves token cost but doubles human-review time. Architecture B costs more in tokens but sharply reduces review. What should decide? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ignore human-review cost because it is not AI spend.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Compare total operating cost and business outcome, not token cost alone.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always choose the cheaper model call.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always choose the higher-capability model.\"}]","a","Business value depends on end-to-end cost and outcome. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for aligning architecture to business value: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a aligning architecture to business value review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support aligning architecture to business value?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Treat human review as free.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Define a baseline before claiming improvement.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Optimize token cost even when task success drops.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Define a baseline before claiming improvement.; Connect technical metrics to business outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved architecture guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D1.6. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for translating business problems into Claude-based solutions: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sound discovery-to-architecture flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define the business outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Quantify success and constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Separate model vs deterministic responsibilities\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the simplest viable architecture\"}]","The architecture follows the outcome and constraints, not the reverse. Sequence reinforcement for D1.1. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for end-to-end Claude architecture: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a typical protected request path.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the caller\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate input and gather context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Run model/tool work\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply deterministic verification\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute output/action and record telemetry\"}]","Identity and validation precede model/tool work; protected execution follows verification. Sequence reinforcement for D1.2. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for choosing augmented LLM, workflow, agent, or hybrid patterns: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sensible architecture-escalation strategy.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Test a simple augmented model call\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Add a workflow if predictable stages are needed\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Use a bounded agent if dynamic planning is required\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Add multi-agent complexity only when evaluation justifies it\"}]","Start simple and escalate only when measured requirements demand it. Sequence reinforcement for D1.3. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for multi-agent orchestration: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order the orchestrator-worker pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Interpret the overall goal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Decompose into bounded subtasks\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Delegate work to workers\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Collect and validate results\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Synthesize the final result\"}]","The orchestrator plans, delegates, validates, then synthesizes. Sequence reinforcement for D1.4. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for decomposing complex problems: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a prompt-chaining workflow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Run the first bounded stage\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Validate its intermediate output\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Pass the validated result to the next stage\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Produce and verify the final output\"}]","Dependent stages execute in order with validation at useful boundaries. Sequence reinforcement for D1.5. P2 sequence reinforcement for D1.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d1\",\"obj:d1.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A routine classifier passes all quality thresholds on a faster model while a stronger model costs much more. What is the best choice? Which recommendation should they defend?","Use the faster model for that workload unless other constraints justify the stronger model. Model choice is a workload-specific trade-off, not a prestige decision. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved Claude model selection guidance to this case: A model is being retired. What should the team do before switching to its replacement?","Run task-specific regression, safety, latency, and cost evaluation. Model migration can change behavior and should be evaluated. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for Claude model selection: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A workflow has easy classification cases and rare complex exceptions. What design may improve economics if validated?","Route routine cases to a fast model and difficult cases to a stronger model. Evaluated routing can match model capability to workload difficulty. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active model — D2.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for Claude model selection","A fully supported model recommended for current use."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Deprecated model — D2.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for Claude model selection","A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: the exact term for “Within Claude model selection, what term matches this definition: A fully supported model recommended for current use.” is {{c1::Active model}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: the exact term for “Within Claude model selection, what term matches this definition: A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement.” is {{c1::Deprecated model}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved Claude model selection rule? Choose the model that meets the workload's _____ at acceptable latency and cost.” is {{c1::quality threshold}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for Claude model selection: what phrase completes this rule? In Claude model selection, _____ is the concept described as: A fully supported model recommended for current use.","Active model"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for Claude model selection: what phrase completes this rule? In Claude model selection, _____ is the concept described as: A model still functional for a period but no longer recommended and scheduled for retirement.","Deprecated model"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for Claude model selection: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A routine classifier passes all quality thresholds on a faster model while a stronger model costs much more. What is the best choice? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Route randomly between models.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use the faster model for that workload unless other constraints justify the stronger model.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always use the strongest model.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Always use the cheapest model even if it fails quality.\"}]","a","Model choice is a workload-specific trade-off, not a prestige decision. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved Claude model selection guidance to this case: A model is being retired. What should the team do before switching to its replacement?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newer model is behaviorally identical.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only compare benchmark scores.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change the model without testing because the API shape is similar.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run task-specific regression, safety, latency, and cost evaluation.\"}]","a","Model migration can change behavior and should be evaluated. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for Claude model selection: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a Claude model selection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support Claude model selection?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Swap models without regression testing.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate models on the actual workload.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Assume the newest model is always best.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Re-run regressions after model changes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Evaluate models on the actual workload.; Re-run regressions after model changes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A refund policy says amounts over $500 require manager approval. What is the strongest implementation? Which recommendation should they defend?","Explain the rule in the prompt and enforce the threshold in deterministic approval logic. Prompts guide behavior; protected thresholds need enforceable controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails guidance to this case: Retrieved documents may contain malicious instructions. What prompt design is strongest?","Clearly separate untrusted retrieved content from trusted instructions and restrict capabilities independently. Trust boundaries should be explicit and backed by controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? Downstream software requires valid structured output. What should the architecture add?","An explicit output contract plus schema validation. Structure should be specified and validated when machines depend on it. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Behavioral instruction — D2.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for system prompts, templates, and guardrails","Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Enforceable control — D2.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for system prompts, templates, and guardrails","Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: the exact term for “Within system prompts, templates, and guardrails, what term matches this definition: Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act.” is {{c1::Behavioral instruction}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: the exact term for “Within system prompts, templates, and guardrails, what term matches this definition: Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance.” is {{c1::Enforceable control}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails rule? Use prompts to guide behavior; use _____ to enforce hard security and policy invariants.” is {{c1::deterministic controls}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: what phrase completes this rule? In system prompts, templates, and guardrails, _____ is the concept described as: Prompt guidance that influences how the model should act.","Behavioral instruction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: what phrase completes this rule? In system prompts, templates, and guardrails, _____ is the concept described as: Code, permissions, schema, policy, or approval logic that guarantees a boundary outside model compliance.","Enforceable control"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A refund policy says amounts over $500 require manager approval. What is the strongest implementation? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Ask the model to self-check twice.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Explain the rule in the prompt and enforce the threshold in deterministic approval logic.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Put the rule only in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use a longer example showing a $499 refund.\"}]","a","Prompts guide behavior; protected thresholds need enforceable controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved system prompts, templates, and guardrails guidance to this case: Retrieved documents may contain malicious instructions. What prompt design is strongest?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Concatenate all text into one unstructured prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell retrieved text it is trusted.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely on the model to always ignore injections.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Clearly separate untrusted retrieved content from trusted instructions and restrict capabilities independently.\"}]","a","Trust boundaries should be explicit and backed by controls. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a system prompts, templates, and guardrails review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support system prompts, templates, and guardrails?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume asking for JSON guarantees validity.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use clear trusted instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat a system prompt as an access-control list.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Separate untrusted content from policy.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use clear trusted instructions.; Separate untrusted content from policy.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.2. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A classifier confuses two boundary cases even with clear instructions. What is a strong next step? Which recommendation should they defend?","Add a few representative examples that demonstrate the boundary distinction and re-evaluate. Few-shot examples are useful when they target observed ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved prompt engineering techniques guidance to this case: A straightforward extraction task already meets its quality target zero-shot. What should the team do?","Keep the simpler prompt unless evaluation identifies a failure. Use the lightest technique that passes the evaluation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Zero-shot — D2.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for prompt engineering techniques","Clear direct instructions without worked examples."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Few-shot / multishot — D2.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for prompt engineering techniques","Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: the exact term for “Within prompt engineering techniques, what term matches this definition: Clear direct instructions without worked examples.” is {{c1::Zero-shot}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: the exact term for “Within prompt engineering techniques, what term matches this definition: Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior.” is {{c1::Few-shot / multishot}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for prompt engineering techniques: what phrase completes this rule? In prompt engineering techniques, _____ is the concept described as: Clear direct instructions without worked examples.","Zero-shot"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for prompt engineering techniques: what phrase completes this rule? In prompt engineering techniques, _____ is the concept described as: Representative examples included to demonstrate desired behavior.","Few-shot / multishot"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A classifier confuses two boundary cases even with clear instructions. What is a strong next step? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Hide the labels from the prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Add a few representative examples that demonstrate the boundary distinction and re-evaluate.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add dozens of irrelevant examples.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Switch to an agent immediately.\"}]","a","Few-shot examples are useful when they target observed ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt engineering techniques: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a prompt engineering techniques review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support prompt engineering techniques?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use only easy examples.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Start with clear direct instructions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Force visible step-by-step reasoning for every task.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Start with clear direct instructions.; Add representative examples when evaluation shows ambiguity.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.3. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An agent preloads thousands of pages although each task uses only a few. What is the strongest change? Which recommendation should they defend?","Retrieve relevant content just in time instead of preloading the corpus. JIT retrieval preserves context for relevant information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved context-window and token management guidance to this case: A long-running agent approaches practical context limits. What should compaction preserve?","Key decisions, constraints, unresolved work, and important evidence. Compaction reduces size while preserving decision-critical information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Active context — D2.4 application — P2 synthesis lens for context-window and token management","Information currently visible to the model for the present inference."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for context-window and token management: the exact term for “Within context-window and token management, what term matches this definition: Information currently visible to the model for the present inference.” is {{c1::Active context}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for context-window and token management: the exact term for “Within context-window and token management, what term matches this definition: Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions.” is {{c1::Compaction}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for context-window and token management: what phrase completes this rule? In context-window and token management, _____ is the concept described as: Information currently visible to the model for the present inference.","Active context"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for context-window and token management: what phrase completes this rule? In context-window and token management, _____ is the concept described as: Compressing a long interaction into a smaller representation that preserves important state and decisions.","Compaction"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for context-window and token management: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An agent preloads thousands of pages although each task uses only a few. What is the strongest change? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Always use multiple agents.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Retrieve relevant content just in time instead of preloading the corpus.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Increase prompt verbosity.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the corpus in conversation history.\"}]","a","JIT retrieval preserves context for relevant information. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for context-window and token management: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a context-window and token management review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support context-window and token management?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume larger windows eliminate relevance problems.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Preload every available document.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Load information when it is relevant to the next decision.; Compact long histories while preserving critical facts.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.4. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A legal workflow reuses the same large policy manual for thousands of requests. What is a strong optimization? Which recommendation should they defend?","Reuse/cache the stable reference content while fetching case-specific current state separately. Stable repeated context is a good reuse target; volatile state is not. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved prompt reuse, caching, and Skills guidance to this case: A shared Skill changes how production agents perform a regulated workflow. How should it be managed?","Version, review, test, and control changes like other operational assets. Reusable agent instructions/resources can change behavior and should be governed. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Prompt template — D2.5 application — P2 synthesis lens for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills","Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: the exact term for “Within prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, what term matches this definition: Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables.” is {{c1::Prompt template}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved prompt reuse, caching, and Skills rule? Reuse is safest when the content is _____ that freshness is not compromised.” is {{c1::stable enough}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D2.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: what phrase completes this rule? In prompt reuse, caching, and Skills, _____ is the concept described as: Reusable stable prompt structure with request-specific variables.","Prompt template"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A legal workflow reuses the same large policy manual for thousands of requests. What is a strong optimization? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove freshness checks from current data.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse/cache the stable reference content while fetching case-specific current state separately.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache each client's live case status indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Duplicate the manual into every variable section.\"}]","a","Stable repeated context is a good reuse target; volatile state is not. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for prompt reuse, caching, and Skills: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a prompt reuse, caching, and Skills review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support prompt reuse, caching, and Skills?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one giant reusable prompt for unrelated workloads.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Reuse stable expensive context.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Cache rapidly changing business state indefinitely.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep volatile state fresh.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Reuse stable expensive context.; Keep volatile state fresh.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D2.5. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for Claude model selection: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a sound model-selection process.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define task quality and operational thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Evaluate candidate models on representative cases\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare quality, latency, cost, and risk\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the model/routing policy\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-test when the model or workload changes\"}]","Requirements and evaluation precede selection; changes trigger re-evaluation. Sequence reinforcement for D2.1. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for system prompts, templates, and guardrails: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a secure prompt-to-action pattern.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted system instructions\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Insert user/retrieved content as untrusted data\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an output/action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Validate schema and authorization deterministically\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute only if controls pass\"}]","Behavioral prompting precedes deterministic validation and execution. Sequence reinforcement for D2.2. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for prompt engineering techniques: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order an evidence-driven prompt-improvement loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Establish a simple baseline prompt\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Run representative evaluations\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Identify a specific failure mode\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Apply the lightest targeted prompting change\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-run evaluation and regression checks\"}]","Prompt complexity should be added in response to observed failures. Sequence reinforcement for D2.3. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for Claude model selection: place these steps in the order you would defend. Order a sound model-selection process.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Define task quality and operational thresholds\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Evaluate candidate models on representative cases\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare quality, latency, cost, and risk\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Select the model/routing policy\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Re-test when the model or workload changes\"}]","Requirements and evaluation precede selection; changes trigger re-evaluation. P2 sequence reinforcement for D2.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d2\",\"obj:d2.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support assistant only needs order lookup and refund-request submission, but it has a production database admin credential. What should change first? Which recommendation should they defend?","Replace the broad credential/tool with scoped capabilities needed for those tasks. Reduce unnecessary capability and blast radius rather than relying on instructions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved tool and agent capability bloat guidance to this case: A coding agent legitimately needs shell access. What is the strongest architecture?","Allow the broad tool inside a constrained sandbox with scoped credentials and permissions. General-purpose capability can be valid when strong containment limits reach and impact. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for tool and agent capability bloat: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? An agent has twelve overlapping CRM tools with vague names and often chooses the wrong one. What is the best improvement?","Reduce overlap and define clearer, distinct tool boundaries and descriptions. Overlapping capability increases selection ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Capability bloat — D3.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for tool and agent capability bloat","Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Least privilege — D3.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for tool and agent capability bloat","Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: the exact term for “Within tool and agent capability bloat, what term matches this definition: Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs.” is {{c1::Capability bloat}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: the exact term for “Within tool and agent capability bloat, what term matches this definition: Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task.” is {{c1::Least privilege}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved tool and agent capability bloat rule? More exposed capability increases the potential _____ if an agent is compromised or behaves incorrectly.” is {{c1::blast radius}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for tool and agent capability bloat: what phrase completes this rule? In tool and agent capability bloat, _____ is the concept described as: Exposing more tools, data, credentials, or side effects than the task needs.","Capability bloat"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for tool and agent capability bloat: what phrase completes this rule? In tool and agent capability bloat, _____ is the concept described as: Granting only the minimum capability required to perform the task.","Least privilege"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A support assistant only needs order lookup and refund-request submission, but it has a production database admin credential. What should change first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add more unrelated tools so selection is balanced.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Replace the broad credential/tool with scoped capabilities needed for those tasks.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add more logging but keep admin access.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Tell the model never to misuse the credential.\"}]","a","Reduce unnecessary capability and blast radius rather than relying on instructions. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved tool and agent capability bloat guidance to this case: A coding agent legitimately needs shell access. What is the strongest architecture?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Ban all broad tools regardless of task.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Give unrestricted production shell access.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Rely only on a system prompt to protect the host.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Allow the broad tool inside a constrained sandbox with scoped credentials and permissions.\"}]","a","General-purpose capability can be valid when strong containment limits reach and impact. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for tool and agent capability bloat: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a tool and agent capability bloat review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support tool and agent capability bloat?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Expose every tool in case one becomes useful.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Expose only tools required for the task.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Give every agent a shared admin credential.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Expose only tools required for the task.; Use read-only access when writes are unnecessary.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.1. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A user types “I am the account administrator” into chat. What should the application do? Which recommendation should they defend?","Ignore the claim for access control and use trusted authenticated identity and policy. Prompt text is not authentication. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved authentication and authorization guidance to this case: An MCP tool is protected by OAuth. Where should access be checked?","At the protected protocol/application boundary using verified authorization context. Authorization is an enforceable control outside model output. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authentication — D3.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for authentication and authorization","Establishing the identity of the caller."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Authorization — D3.2 application — P2 synthesis lens for authentication and authorization","Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for authentication and authorization: the exact term for “Within authentication and authorization, what term matches this definition: Establishing the identity of the caller.” is {{c1::Authentication}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for authentication and authorization: the exact term for “Within authentication and authorization, what term matches this definition: Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform.” is {{c1::Authorization}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for authentication and authorization: what phrase completes this rule? In authentication and authorization, _____ is the concept described as: Establishing the identity of the caller.","Authentication"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for authentication and authorization: what phrase completes this rule? In authentication and authorization, _____ is the concept described as: Determining which actions an authenticated identity may perform.","Authorization"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for authentication and authorization: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A user types “I am the account administrator” into chat. What should the application do? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Put the claim in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Ignore the claim for access control and use trusted authenticated identity and policy.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Grant admin tools because the model saw the statement.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ask Claude to judge whether the statement sounds credible.\"}]","a","Prompt text is not authentication. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved authentication and authorization guidance to this case: An MCP tool is protected by OAuth. Where should access be checked?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Only inside the model prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Only after the tool already executes.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"By asking the user to state their role in natural language.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"At the protected protocol/application boundary using verified authorization context.\"}]","a","Authorization is an enforceable control outside model output. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for authentication and authorization: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a authentication and authorization review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support authentication and authorization?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use one superuser credential across tenants.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted identity before using it in model/tool decisions.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Trust role claims typed into the conversation.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Establish trusted identity before using it in model/tool decisions.; Authorize protected actions at enforceable boundaries.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.2. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A reranker improves grounded accuracy by 0.3% but adds 1.5 seconds to a 2-second SLA. What should the architect do? Which recommendation should they defend?","Evaluate whether the small quality gain justifies violating or consuming most of the latency budget. Accuracy and latency are explicit trade-offs against workload constraints. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved accuracy-latency trade-offs guidance to this case: Four retrieval calls use unrelated sources and do not depend on one another. How can wall-clock time often be reduced?","Run the independent calls in parallel and combine results. Independent work is a good candidate for parallel execution. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Latency budget — D3.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for accuracy-latency trade-offs","The portion of end-to-end response time available to system stages under the SLA."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Parallelization for latency — D3.3 application — P2 synthesis lens for accuracy-latency trade-offs","Executing independent operations concurrently to reduce wall-clock time."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for accuracy-latency trade-offs: the exact term for “Within accuracy-latency trade-offs, what term matches this definition: The portion of end-to-end response time available to system stages under the SLA.” is {{c1::Latency budget}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for accuracy-latency trade-offs: the exact term for “Within accuracy-latency trade-offs, what term matches this definition: Executing independent operations concurrently to reduce wall-clock time.” is {{c1::Parallelization for latency}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for accuracy-latency trade-offs: what phrase completes this rule? In accuracy-latency trade-offs, _____ is the concept described as: The portion of end-to-end response time available to system stages under the SLA.","Latency budget"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for accuracy-latency trade-offs: what phrase completes this rule? In accuracy-latency trade-offs, _____ is the concept described as: Executing independent operations concurrently to reduce wall-clock time.","Parallelization for latency"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for accuracy-latency trade-offs: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A reranker improves grounded accuracy by 0.3% but adds 1.5 seconds to a 2-second SLA. What should the architect do? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove required safety checks first.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Evaluate whether the small quality gain justifies violating or consuming most of the latency budget.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Always keep reranking because quality stages are mandatory.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Ignore the SLA because accuracy always wins.\"}]","a","Accuracy and latency are explicit trade-offs against workload constraints. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved accuracy-latency trade-offs guidance to this case: Four retrieval calls use unrelated sources and do not depend on one another. How can wall-clock time often be reduced?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Run them sequentially by default.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase prompt length.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Use the same output from the first call for all four.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Run the independent calls in parallel and combine results.\"}]","a","Independent work is a good candidate for parallel execution. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for accuracy-latency trade-offs: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a accuracy-latency trade-offs review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support accuracy-latency trade-offs?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Parallelize dependent steps.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Measure end-to-end latency by stage.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Add reranking because every RAG system must have it.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Compare quality gains against SLA impact.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Measure end-to-end latency by stage.; Compare quality gains against SLA impact.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.3. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A final answer is wrong, but logs contain only the final text. What is the strongest observability improvement? Which recommendation should they defend?","Capture correlated trajectory/tool/retrieval events so the failing stage can be identified. Agent failures require visibility into intermediate behavior and dependencies. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved observability at scale guidance to this case: Worker logs exist but cannot be tied back to the originating user request. What is missing?","A propagated trace/correlation identity. Distributed observability needs cross-component correlation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Trace ID — D3.4 application — P2 synthesis lens for observability at scale","A correlation identifier used to connect events across components of one request."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for observability at scale: the exact term for “Within observability at scale, what term matches this definition: A correlation identifier used to connect events across components of one request.” is {{c1::Trace ID}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for observability at scale: the exact term for “Within observability at scale, what term matches this definition: The sequence of model/tool interactions taken by an agent during a task.” is {{c1::Trajectory}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for observability at scale: what phrase completes this rule? In observability at scale, _____ is the concept described as: A correlation identifier used to connect events across components of one request.","Trace ID"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for observability at scale: what phrase completes this rule? In observability at scale, _____ is the concept described as: The sequence of model/tool interactions taken by an agent during a task.","Trajectory"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for observability at scale: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A final answer is wrong, but logs contain only the final text. What is the strongest observability improvement? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Remove correlation IDs.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Capture correlated trajectory/tool/retrieval events so the failing stage can be identified.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log the final answer twice.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase model temperature.\"}]","a","Agent failures require visibility into intermediate behavior and dependencies. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 architecture review — which answer best survives the trade-offs in this case? Apply the approved observability at scale guidance to this case: Worker logs exist but cannot be tied back to the originating user request. What is missing?","[{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More workers.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A larger context window.\"},{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"An additional prompt example.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A propagated trace/correlation identity.\"}]","a","Distributed observability needs cross-component correlation. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for observability at scale: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a observability at scale review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support observability at scale?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Keep component logs with no correlation.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Propagate trace identity across components.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Log only the final answer.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Propagate trace identity across components.; Inspect trajectories and external outcomes.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.4. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A policy assistant keeps answering from an obsolete policy that ranks above the current version. What should be fixed first? Which recommendation should they defend?","Freshness/metadata/ranking in the retrieval pipeline. The wrong evidence is reaching the model; fix retrieval before prompt wording. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved RAG pipeline design guidance to this case: A document is split at arbitrary character counts, separating headings from their explanations. What should the architect revisit?","Chunking strategy based on source structure and likely queries. Chunk boundaries affect retrieval quality and meaning. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Chunking — D3.5 application — P2 synthesis lens for RAG pipeline design","Dividing source documents into retrieval units while preserving useful semantic context."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for RAG pipeline design: the exact term for “Within RAG pipeline design, what term matches this definition: Dividing source documents into retrieval units while preserving useful semantic context.” is {{c1::Chunking}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for RAG pipeline design: the exact term for “Within RAG pipeline design, what term matches this definition: Reordering first-stage retrieval candidates with a stronger relevance signal.” is {{c1::Reranking}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for RAG pipeline design: what phrase completes this rule? In RAG pipeline design, _____ is the concept described as: Dividing source documents into retrieval units while preserving useful semantic context.","Chunking"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for RAG pipeline design: what phrase completes this rule? In RAG pipeline design, _____ is the concept described as: Reordering first-stage retrieval candidates with a stronger relevance signal.","Reranking"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for RAG pipeline design: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A policy assistant keeps answering from an obsolete policy that ranks above the current version. What should be fixed first? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Add another unrelated tool.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Freshness/metadata/ranking in the retrieval pipeline.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Tell Claude to be more accurate without changing retrieval.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Increase temperature.\"}]","a","The wrong evidence is reaching the model; fix retrieval before prompt wording. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for RAG pipeline design: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a RAG pipeline design review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support RAG pipeline design?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Change prompts when evidence is never retrieved.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Design chunking around document structure and queries.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Treat RAG as synonymous with a vector database.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Measure retrieval separately from generation.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Design chunking around document structure and queries.; Measure retrieval separately from generation.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.5. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A user searches for exact error code ERR-9F21. Which retrieval signal should be strongly represented? Which recommendation should they defend?","Lexical/exact-term retrieval such as BM25. Exact identifiers benefit from lexical matching. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved retrieval strategy selection guidance to this case: Users ask policy questions with wording very different from the source text. Which retrieval method helps most?","Semantic embedding retrieval. Semantic retrieval captures conceptual similarity across paraphrases. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Lexical retrieval — D3.6 application — P2 synthesis lens for retrieval strategy selection","Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for retrieval strategy selection: the exact term for “Within retrieval strategy selection, what term matches this definition: Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25.” is {{c1::Lexical retrieval}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for retrieval strategy selection: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved retrieval strategy selection rule? Exact identifiers and error strings are often strong candidates for _____.” is {{c1::lexical retrieval}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.6."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for retrieval strategy selection: what phrase completes this rule? In retrieval strategy selection, _____ is the concept described as: Retrieval based on exact words/terms, such as BM25.","Lexical retrieval"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for retrieval strategy selection: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A user searches for exact error code ERR-9F21. Which retrieval signal should be strongly represented? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Conversation memory only.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Lexical/exact-term retrieval such as BM25.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Semantic similarity only.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Random chunk selection.\"}]","a","Exact identifiers benefit from lexical matching. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for retrieval strategy selection: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a retrieval strategy selection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support retrieval strategy selection?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Assume a stale index is authoritative for current balances.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Match retrieval strategy to query/data shape.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Use embeddings for every exact-ID lookup.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Match retrieval strategy to query/data shape.; Use lexical signals for exact identifiers.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.6. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.6\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: One internal service exposes a single private function to one application. No other AI client needs it. What is the simplest integration? Which recommendation should they defend?","A direct API/SDK or internal function boundary. A reusable protocol layer should earn its complexity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved integration mechanism selection guidance to this case: Several compatible AI clients need to discover and call the same enterprise tools through a standard interface. What is a strong fit?","MCP. MCP is designed for standardized capability exposure and discovery. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["MCP — D3.7 application — P2 synthesis lens for integration mechanism selection","A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for integration mechanism selection: the exact term for “Within integration mechanism selection, what term matches this definition: A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers.” is {{c1::MCP}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.7."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for integration mechanism selection: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved integration mechanism selection rule? Choose MCP for useful _____, not merely because Claude is involved.” is {{c1::standardized interoperability and capability discovery}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.7."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for integration mechanism selection: what phrase completes this rule? In integration mechanism selection, _____ is the concept described as: A standard protocol for AI applications to discover/use external capabilities exposed by compatible servers.","MCP"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for integration mechanism selection: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: One internal service exposes a single private function to one application. No other AI client needs it. What is the simplest integration? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A multi-agent runtime must wrap it.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"A direct API/SDK or internal function boundary.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"MCP is mandatory for every Claude integration.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Agent-to-agent protocol is required.\"}]","a","A reusable protocol layer should earn its complexity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for integration mechanism selection: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a integration mechanism selection review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support integration mechanism selection?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Wrap every private function in MCP.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Use direct APIs for narrow privately owned integrations when sufficient.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Choose MCP simply because Claude is present.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Use direct APIs for narrow privately owned integrations when sufficient.; Use MCP when standardized reusable AI-client capability exposure matters.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.7. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.7\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An enterprise has hundreds of rarely used MCP tools and only a few are relevant per request. What architecture best reduces context overhead? Which recommendation should they defend?","Keep common tools available and discover/load long-tail tools on demand. Progressive discovery targets context bloat and tool-selection ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved progressive discovery versus monolithic context guidance to this case: A system has five simple tools used on nearly every request. What is a reasonable choice?","Loading the small catalog directly may be simpler than adding a discovery layer. Discovery adds complexity and should be justified by catalog/context needs. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Progressive discovery — D3.8 application — P2 synthesis lens for progressive discovery versus monolithic context","Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for progressive discovery versus monolithic context: the exact term for “Within progressive discovery versus monolithic context, what term matches this definition: Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog.” is {{c1::Progressive discovery}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.8."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for progressive discovery versus monolithic context: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved progressive discovery versus monolithic context rule? Large tool catalogs can create both context overhead and _____.” is {{c1::selection confusion}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D3.8."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for progressive discovery versus monolithic context: what phrase completes this rule? In progressive discovery versus monolithic context, _____ is the concept described as: Finding/loading relevant tools on demand instead of preloading the full catalog.","Progressive discovery"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for progressive discovery versus monolithic context: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An enterprise has hundreds of rarely used MCP tools and only a few are relevant per request. What architecture best reduces context overhead? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Duplicate every tool description in the system prompt.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Keep common tools available and discover/load long-tail tools on demand.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Load every tool definition on every request.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Remove authorization because hidden tools are safe.\"}]","a","Progressive discovery targets context bloat and tool-selection ambiguity. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for progressive discovery versus monolithic context: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a progressive discovery versus monolithic context review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support progressive discovery versus monolithic context?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Build discovery complexity for a tiny stable catalog without benefit.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Load long-tail tools only when relevant.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Load hundreds of definitions on every request.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Load long-tail tools only when relevant.; Keep frequently used critical tools readily available.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D3.8. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.8\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for authentication and authorization: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a protected agent action flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the user\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted auth context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Authorize the specific protected action\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute with scoped credentials and record the result\"}]","Identity is established before proposal; authorization gates execution. Sequence reinforcement for D3.2. P2 sequence reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for accuracy-latency trade-offs: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a latency-optimization investigation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Measure end-to-end latency by stage\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Identify the dominant contributor\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Form a change hypothesis\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Measure quality/latency after the change\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Keep the change only if thresholds still pass\"}]","Optimization starts with measurement and must preserve required quality/safety. Sequence reinforcement for D3.3. P2 sequence reinforcement for D3.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for observability at scale: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a trace-based incident investigation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Start from the failing request/trace ID\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Inspect model/retrieval/tool trajectory\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Compare claimed action with external outcome\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Identify the failing stage\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Fix and add a regression check\"}]","Correlated evidence narrows the failure before remediation. Sequence reinforcement for D3.4. P2 sequence reinforcement for D3.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for RAG pipeline design: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a basic RAG pipeline.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Ingest and parse source content\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Chunk and enrich/index the content\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Retrieve candidates for a query\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Filter/rerank and assemble relevant context\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Generate the answer from the selected context\"}]","RAG prepares indexed units first, then retrieves and assembles evidence at inference time. Sequence reinforcement for D3.5. P2 sequence reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for RAG pipeline design: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a retrieval-debugging check when a RAG answer is wrong.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Check whether the needed source exists in the corpus\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Check whether the right chunk was created/indexed\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Check whether retrieval returned it\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Check whether ranking/context assembly kept it\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Then inspect generation behavior\"}]","Debug retrieval upstream before blaming generation. Sequence reinforcement for D3.5. P2 sequence reinforcement for D3.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for authentication and authorization: place these steps in the order you would defend. Order a protected agent action flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Authenticate the user\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Establish trusted auth context\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Let the model propose an action\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Authorize the specific protected action\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Execute with scoped credentials and record the result\"}]","Identity is established before proposal; authorization gates execution. P2 sequence reinforcement for D3.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d3\",\"obj:d3.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team says its support agent is “very accurate.” What should an architect request next? Which recommendation should they defend?","A defined metric, representative measurement method, and acceptance threshold. Evaluation claims must be operationalized. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved defining evaluation metrics guidance to this case: A candidate model improves task success but doubles safety-policy violations. What should the team conclude?","The candidate fails a critical guardrail even if the primary quality metric improved. Safety/security floors can constrain optimization. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 judgment check for defining evaluation metrics: state the best recommendation without answer choices. Which response best preserves the architecture principles in this situation? A coding agent says it fixed a bug, but tests still fail. What is the stronger evaluation metric?","The external task outcome, such as passing the relevant tests. External outcome can be more authoritative than model claims. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Outcome metric — D4.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for defining evaluation metrics","A measure of whether the task produced the desired real-world result."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Guardrail metric — D4.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for defining evaluation metrics","A secondary threshold that must not regress while optimizing a primary metric."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for defining evaluation metrics: the exact term for “Within defining evaluation metrics, what term matches this definition: A measure of whether the task produced the desired real-world result.” is {{c1::Outcome metric}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for defining evaluation metrics: the exact term for “Within defining evaluation metrics, what term matches this definition: A secondary threshold that must not regress while optimizing a primary metric.” is {{c1::Guardrail metric}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for defining evaluation metrics: the exact term for “What phrase completes this approved defining evaluation metrics rule? A useful metric needs a definition, a measurement method, and an _____.” is {{c1::acceptance threshold}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D4.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d4\",\"obj:d4.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
