{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for architecture documentation and implementation guidance: what phrase completes this rule? In architecture documentation and implementation guidance, _____ is the concept described as: Architecture Decision Record documenting a significant decision, context, alternatives, and rationale.","ADR"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for architecture documentation and implementation guidance: what phrase completes this rule? In architecture documentation and implementation guidance, _____ is the concept described as: Operational guidance for diagnosing, responding to, and recovering from known conditions/incidents.","Runbook"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for architecture documentation and implementation guidance: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: An ADR says only “Use MCP.” What key information is missing? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"A longer title.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Context, alternatives, trade-offs, rationale, assumptions, and review triggers.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"More screenshots.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"A model-generated slogan.\"}]","a","A decision record should preserve why the choice was made. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for architecture documentation and implementation guidance: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a architecture documentation and implementation guidance review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support architecture documentation and implementation guidance?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Leave docs stale after major changes.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Record rationale and alternatives.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Produce diagrams with no rationale.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Document assumptions and review triggers.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Record rationale and alternatives.; Document assumptions and review triggers.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.4. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team launches before agreeing on acceptance criteria, then tries to infer success from dashboards. Which lifecycle problem occurred? Which recommendation should they defend?","Discovery/design did not define success before handoff/monitoring. Later phases cannot repair undefined earlier requirements. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved solution lifecycle management guidance to this case: Architecture is complete, but no implementation owner or rollback plan exists. Which phase is not ready?","Handoff / implementation readiness. Handoff requires ownership and operational readiness. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Handoff — D6.5 application — P2 synthesis lens for solution lifecycle management","Transition from architecture/design into implementation and operational ownership with acceptance criteria and guidance."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for solution lifecycle management: the exact term for “Within solution lifecycle management, what term matches this definition: Transition from architecture/design into implementation and operational ownership with acceptance criteria and guidance.” is {{c1::Handoff}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"cloze","fields":["P2 synthesis for solution lifecycle management: the exact term for “Within solution lifecycle management, what term matches this definition: Evidence-driven changes after design/launch, accompanied by updated evaluation and documentation.” is {{c1::Iteration}}.","Exact-term reinforcement for D6.5."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for solution lifecycle management: what phrase completes this rule? In solution lifecycle management, _____ is the concept described as: Transition from architecture/design into implementation and operational ownership with acceptance criteria and guidance.","Handoff"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"type-answer","fields":["P2 exact recall for solution lifecycle management: what phrase completes this rule? In solution lifecycle management, _____ is the concept described as: Evidence-driven changes after design/launch, accompanied by updated evaluation and documentation.","Iteration"],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:concept\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-choice","fields":["P2 exam synthesis for solution lifecycle management: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team launches before agreeing on acceptance criteria, then tries to infer success from dashboards. Which lifecycle problem occurred? Which recommendation should they defend?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Iteration eliminates the need for acceptance criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Discovery/design did not define success before handoff/monitoring.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Monitoring should always define requirements retroactively.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Handoff should happen before design.\"}]","a","Later phases cannot repair undefined earlier requirements. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review. P2 emphasizes synthesis and edge-case judgment."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"multiple-select","fields":["P2 synthesis for solution lifecycle management: which TWO controls or decisions still hold under scrutiny? During a solution lifecycle management review, which TWO statements remain aligned with the approved guidance? Which TWO practices best support solution lifecycle management?","[{\"id\":\"d\",\"text\":\"Monitor infrastructure only.\"},{\"id\":\"a\",\"text\":\"Complete discovery before committing architecture.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"text\":\"Launch with no acceptance criteria.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"text\":\"Define acceptance criteria before handoff.\"}]","[\"a\",\"c\"]","Correct: Complete discovery before committing architecture.; Define acceptance criteria before handoff.. The other choices conflict with the approved guidance. This variant reinforces the approved decision set for D6.5. P2 reinforces the surviving decision set."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.5\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:decision\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for structured discovery and requirement gathering: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a structured discovery flow.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Clarify the business outcome and baseline\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Map users and current workflow\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Define measurable quality/latency/scale constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Identify risk/compliance boundaries\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Assign owners and acceptance criteria\"}]","Discovery progresses from outcome/workflow to measurable constraints and ownership. Sequence reinforcement for D6.1. P2 sequence reinforcement for D6.1."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for communicating architecture decisions and trade-offs: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a concise architecture-decision explanation.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"State the decision context/constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Present the recommended option\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Explain benefits and evidence\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Explain costs/risks and alternatives\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"State ownership/review triggers\"}]","The audience first needs context, then recommendation and its trade-offs. Sequence reinforcement for D6.2. P2 sequence reinforcement for D6.2."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.2\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for stakeholder feedback and expectation alignment: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order an actionable stakeholder feedback loop.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Collect a signal\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"Compare it to a trigger/threshold\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Assign investigation to the owner\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Take the targeted action\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Verify the outcome and update expectations/evals\"}]","Signals drive owned investigation, action, and verification. Sequence reinforcement for D6.3. P2 sequence reinforcement for D6.3."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.3\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"ordering","fields":["P2 synthesis sequence for architecture documentation and implementation guidance: place these steps in the order you would defend. Put these steps in the operational order you would defend during a P1 design review: Order a useful ADR structure.","[{\"id\":\"s1\",\"text\":\"Describe context and constraints\"},{\"id\":\"s2\",\"text\":\"State the decision\"},{\"id\":\"s3\",\"text\":\"Record meaningful alternatives\"},{\"id\":\"s4\",\"text\":\"Explain trade-offs and rationale\"},{\"id\":\"s5\",\"text\":\"Record assumptions, owner, and review trigger\"}]","ADRs preserve why a decision was made and when it may need revisiting. Sequence reinforcement for D6.4. P2 sequence reinforcement for D6.4."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d6\",\"obj:d6.4\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:sequence\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 synthesis — defend the architecture choice for this case: A design reviewer is evaluating this scenario: A team tells Claude Code “never touch production,” but every developer environment has production admin credentials. What is strongest? Which recommendation should they defend?","Remove/restrict production credentials and permissions; keep the instruction as supplemental guidance. Hard permission boundaries should not depend on model compliance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic","fields":["P2 edge-case review — what action should survive scrutiny here? Apply the approved team-level Claude tools and environments guidance to this case: Each developer has a different MCP/tool configuration and shared workflows behave inconsistently. What should the team do?","Standardize high-value repository/team configuration and version it. Shared configuration improves reproducibility and governance. This P1 variant tests the same approved principle in a re-framed design review."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:scenario\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Instruction — D7.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for team-level Claude tools and environments","Guidance intended to influence model behavior."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
{"kind":"note","note_type":"basic-reverse","fields":["Runtime control — D7.1 application — P2 synthesis lens for team-level Claude tools and environments","An enforceable runtime, permission, sandbox, policy, or CI boundary."],"tags_json":"[\"ccarp\",\"d7\",\"obj:d7.1\",\"priority:p2\",\"kind:compare\",\"source:approved\"]"}
